WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.109 --> 00:00:05.470
On March 15th, 2011, Martin Sims was wandering
down the streets of Carson, California. His

00:00:05.470 --> 00:00:10.589
clothes were ragged, he was filthy, and gibbering
like a madman with a full beard and long,

00:00:10.589 --> 00:00:15.970
unkempt hair. His body was covered in scars,
but he showed no signs of malnutrition. What

00:00:15.970 --> 00:00:20.981
made Martin’s sudden appearance so remarkable?
He’d been missing for three years. When

00:00:20.981 --> 00:00:24.460
he was interviewed by police, they asked him
where he’d been all this time. They couldn’t

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:30.150
believe his answer. He’d been trapped in
an Ikea since 2008. But this was no ordinary

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:35.390
Ikea – this was a dangerous anomaly that
would come to be known as SCP-3008 .

00:00:35.390 --> 00:00:40.150
Martin’s strange answers in his interview
were laughed off by his interviewing officers,

00:00:40.150 --> 00:00:43.880
who assumed he was either crazy or under the
influence of something, but they caught the

00:00:43.880 --> 00:00:48.650
attention of an SCP Foundation Field Agent
embedded in the precinct. The report was passed

00:00:48.650 --> 00:00:53.380
up the chain to a local Site Director, who
approved a detachment of Foundation Field

00:00:53.380 --> 00:00:57.630
Operatives to look into Martin’s case. While
he was reluctant to lead the Foundation Agents

00:00:57.630 --> 00:01:03.290
back to the offending Ikea – the Foundation
can be extremely persuasive. His screams of

00:01:03.290 --> 00:01:07.250
“Please, I’m begging you, don’t take
me back! Don’t make me go back!” were

00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:11.610
noted but ultimately disregarded.
When the SCP Foundation had triangulated the

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:17.490
position of SCP-3008 , which was indeed an
active Ikea, the entire retail zone was closed

00:01:17.490 --> 00:01:23.049
and barricaded under the pretence of a severe
black mold infestation. Armed Foundation Personnel

00:01:23.049 --> 00:01:27.080
also arrived on site shortly after, based
on Martin’s vague statements that there

00:01:27.080 --> 00:01:31.610
were creatures of some kind inside. Due to
his deteriorating mental health, Martin was

00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:37.480
unable to provide a great deal of lucid information
on the specific traits of SCP-3008 , but one

00:01:37.480 --> 00:01:41.040
phrase he kept repeating was “bigger on
the inside.”

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:44.869
Once researchers were satisfied that Martin
had delivered all the pertinent information

00:01:44.869 --> 00:01:49.560
he was able to, he was administered Foundation
Amnestics to erase his memory of the last

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:54.049
three years and returned to his family. A
cover story was formulated: Martin had been

00:01:54.049 --> 00:01:58.790
kidnapped and abused for three years by a
mentally-unbalanced stalker in downtown Carson.

00:01:58.790 --> 00:02:03.020
He’d been able to escape as said stalker
took his own life out of guilt – a suicide

00:02:03.020 --> 00:02:07.600
that the Foundation expertly fabricated to
make their cover story airtight. With the

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:12.280
loose end of Martin Sims taken care of, the
true observation of SCP-3008 could begin.

00:02:12.280 --> 00:02:17.890
A base set around the perimeter of the mysterious
Ikea kept a 24-hour watch on the building,

00:02:17.890 --> 00:02:22.300
covering all potential entrances and exits.
No exploratory missions had yet been approved

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:26.320
by the Foundation ethics committee, so they
first wanted to perform a week of external

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:31.099
observation to see if any of the store’s
anomalous properties extended beyond the confines

00:02:31.099 --> 00:02:35.400
of the building. After a week of nothing,
it appeared they did not. A local Site Director

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:41.700
approved the use of twenty disposable Class-D
Personnel to explore the interior of SCP-3008

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:43.489
.
The D-Class operatives would be split into

00:02:43.489 --> 00:02:48.380
four squads of five men – Alpha, Bravo,
Charlie, and Delta Squad. Each would be assigned

00:02:48.380 --> 00:02:52.360
a different quadrant of the store, and would
deliver information back to the control team

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:57.440
on site via a live audio and video link. Three
of the four teams, upon entering the store,

00:02:57.440 --> 00:03:01.319
reported nothing out of the ordinary. Neither
the audio or video they were sending back

00:03:01.319 --> 00:03:05.640
indicated anything different from a standard
Ikea store – from the flat-pack wardrobes

00:03:05.640 --> 00:03:10.760
to the Swedish meatballs. Team Delta, however,
suddenly began experiencing a scrambled audio

00:03:10.760 --> 00:03:14.030
and video connection.
Shortly after, communication with Team Delta

00:03:14.030 --> 00:03:18.629
dropped off entirely. They disappeared somewhere
inside the store, and haven’t been seen

00:03:18.629 --> 00:03:24.260
since – with one notable exception. After
the disappearance of the extraction of teams,

00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:29.440
Foundation Researchers classified SCP-3008
as Euclid, because its anomalous properties

00:03:29.440 --> 00:03:33.849
were at least confined to the interior of
the store. And even then, seemingly not the

00:03:33.849 --> 00:03:41.680
entire interior. The anomalous area within
SCP-3008 became known as SCP-3008-1, and containment

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:46.370
appeared to be 100% secure. There was no telling
how many people had already gone missing in

00:03:46.370 --> 00:03:49.819
the store over the years, but the disappearances
must be stopped.

00:03:49.819 --> 00:03:54.940
The Foundation maintained constant surveillance
around the perimeter of SCP-3008 , but it

00:03:54.940 --> 00:03:58.980
appeared they could prevent any further “incidents”
by simply preventing other civilians from

00:03:58.980 --> 00:04:03.379
accessing the Ikea store. Martin’s ravings
about monsters were assumed to just be the

00:04:03.379 --> 00:04:07.760
product of delirium. Until a surviving member
of Delta Team suddenly reappeared.

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:12.730
The date was November 3rd, 2011. It was a
cold night, a few hours after what would have

00:04:12.730 --> 00:04:16.560
been closing time if the store were still
active and seven months after the extraction

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:22.159
teams had disappeared somewhere in the confines
of SCP-3008. There had been no anomalous activity

00:04:22.159 --> 00:04:26.230
outside the store since the perimeter was
first secured, and Foundation researchers

00:04:26.230 --> 00:04:31.139
hadn’t expected that to change, until the
last surviving member of Delta Team came barging

00:04:31.139 --> 00:04:35.339
out of the store’s entrance. Startled Field
Operatives were amazed to see him again, but

00:04:35.339 --> 00:04:39.180
they were even more amazed to see what was
following him out of the store, repeating

00:04:39.180 --> 00:04:42.740
the same phrase: “The store is now closed,
please exit the building.”

00:04:42.740 --> 00:04:46.509
Despite the fact that the entity chasing the
Delta Team survivor was wearing the yellow

00:04:46.509 --> 00:04:51.949
shirt and blue pants of an Ikea store employee,
the being was definitely not human. It was

00:04:51.949 --> 00:04:57.469
around seven feet tall, with no visible face.
The entity had grossly extended limbs – with

00:04:57.469 --> 00:05:02.629
each arm being around five or six feet long,
and ending in a huge, oversized hand. The

00:05:02.629 --> 00:05:06.629
whole process was so sudden that the Field
Agents present at the perimeter weren’t

00:05:06.629 --> 00:05:11.030
able to save the Delta Team survivor, as the
entity reached forward with its freakishly

00:05:11.030 --> 00:05:14.979
long arms, grabbed him, and twisted his head
off like a child with a doll.

00:05:14.979 --> 00:05:19.190
The Field Operatives present drew their weapons
and peppered the entity with bullets. It would

00:05:19.190 --> 00:05:24.939
later be classified as SCP-3008-2. The being
appeared to collapse and die from the physical

00:05:24.939 --> 00:05:29.289
trauma, at which point both it and the body
of the former Delta Team survivor were taken

00:05:29.289 --> 00:05:33.740
for an autopsy by Foundation researchers.
There were no biological abnormalities to

00:05:33.740 --> 00:05:37.719
the body of the Delta Team survivor, so it
did not appear that the anomalous properties

00:05:37.719 --> 00:05:43.789
of SCP-3008-1 had any effect on the physiology
of its occupants. He was not malnourished

00:05:43.789 --> 00:05:47.939
despite being missing for months, and the
contents of his stomach looked to be half-digested

00:05:47.939 --> 00:05:52.680
food consistent with the menu of a typical
Ikea store restaurant.

00:05:52.680 --> 00:05:58.569
SCP-3008-2, on the other hand, raised a number
of perplexing biological questions. The autopsy

00:05:58.569 --> 00:06:01.960
revealed that the creature’s clothes were
actually a part of its body, like an additional

00:06:01.960 --> 00:06:06.830
layer of skin. The creature lacked blood or
any kind of vascular system. Even stranger,

00:06:06.830 --> 00:06:11.569
the entity didn’t appear to have any bones
or internal organs, not even a brain or nervous

00:06:11.569 --> 00:06:16.139
system. It was a being made entirely of skin,
all the way to its core. How it was able to

00:06:16.139 --> 00:06:20.280
move, or even live for that matter, remains
a mystery. Though when you work for The SCP

00:06:20.280 --> 00:06:24.340
Foundation, you learn to accept that some
things will always remain unexplained.

00:06:24.340 --> 00:06:28.330
One thing was certain, though: Martin Sims
was right about his monsters.

00:06:28.330 --> 00:06:32.369
After the incident with Delta Team, the Foundation
deemed that sending manned explorations into

00:06:32.369 --> 00:06:37.809
the heart of SCP-3008 was too much of a liability,
and planned a series of drone-based reconnaissance

00:06:37.809 --> 00:06:42.229
missions into the anomaly. The first of these
drones experienced connection issues and failed

00:06:42.229 --> 00:06:46.400
when attempting to venture into the Ikea’s
anomalous zone. However, after a lengthy period

00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:50.099
of trial and error, the Foundation was able
to establish a more secure connection with

00:06:50.099 --> 00:06:56.059
its drones, even when deep into the SCP-3008-1
anomalous zone. It was only then that some

00:06:56.059 --> 00:06:59.189
of the most extraordinary discoveries were
made.

00:06:59.189 --> 00:07:04.369
SCP-3008-1 seemed to break the laws of spatial
reality, as the area of the Ikea’s interior

00:07:04.369 --> 00:07:09.010
was at least an order of magnitude larger
than its exterior. Just as Martin Sims had

00:07:09.010 --> 00:07:13.389
said: It was bigger on the inside. But just
how much bigger? The Foundation has yet to

00:07:13.389 --> 00:07:18.649
find evidence of any physical terminators
within the store that might indicate SCP-3008-1

00:07:18.649 --> 00:07:22.789
has an “end point.” While an area of at
least ten kilometres squared has been uncovered

00:07:22.789 --> 00:07:28.279
in SCP-3008-1, it could – in theory – be
infinite. Laser rangefinder tests, which are

00:07:28.279 --> 00:07:32.159
normally very reliable, have only given inconclusive
results.

00:07:32.159 --> 00:07:36.190
Interestingly, the anomalous area doesn’t
have any clear, visual differences from the

00:07:36.190 --> 00:07:40.580
rest of the Ikea store except that it extends
forever. An individual trapped within the

00:07:40.580 --> 00:07:46.430
confines of SCP-3008-1 wouldn’t even realize
that they’d entered an anomalous zone until

00:07:46.430 --> 00:07:50.369
they tried to locate an exit and leave, at
which point, they’d find they were already

00:07:50.369 --> 00:07:56.330
hopelessly lost. The geography of SCP-3008-1
does at least appear to be consistent, so

00:07:56.330 --> 00:08:00.749
people trapped within are theoretically able
to retrace their steps and escape if they

00:08:00.749 --> 00:08:04.379
hadn’t already ventured too deep.
According to data collected during the drone

00:08:04.379 --> 00:08:10.100
reconnaissance missions, SCP-3008-2, of which
there appeared to be a vast population, would

00:08:10.100 --> 00:08:14.770
wander the stores aimlessly during the day.
They were unresponsive to the drone’s presence,

00:08:14.770 --> 00:08:18.409
and did not appear to be aggressive. While
the physical descriptions of these creatures

00:08:18.409 --> 00:08:23.070
could vary slightly, they all followed the
same overall trend: “Clothes” consistent

00:08:23.070 --> 00:08:28.209
with the Ikea uniform, no face, either seemingly
too tall or too short, and limbs that are

00:08:28.209 --> 00:08:32.440
grossly out of proportion with their bodies.
As the Foundation began sending drones deeper

00:08:32.440 --> 00:08:37.979
into SCP-3008-1, they found another incredible
discovery. There was an unknown population

00:08:37.979 --> 00:08:43.159
of humans trapped inside the Ikea’s anomalous
zone, and these people had used the Ikea furniture

00:08:43.159 --> 00:08:47.970
around them to create entire settlements and
towns within the store. There were several

00:08:47.970 --> 00:08:52.399
of these towns, all of which seemed to cohabitate
peacefully. Even Foundation personnel found

00:08:52.399 --> 00:08:55.579
this development in their research to be truly
extraordinary.

00:08:55.579 --> 00:09:00.540
Since SCP-3008 was first identified, there
have been only fourteen civilian escapes.

00:09:00.540 --> 00:09:05.180
Some had been trapped inside for months, others
had been in there for years – some far longer

00:09:05.180 --> 00:09:09.279
than Martin’s three-year stint. While every
one of these escapees has eventually been

00:09:09.279 --> 00:09:13.850
released back to their home, after a liberal
application of Amnestics and a proper cover

00:09:13.850 --> 00:09:18.520
story has been devised, the Foundation interviewed
each of them extensively first. According

00:09:18.520 --> 00:09:23.690
to these escapees, the people trapped inside
the Ikea have built an entirely new society

00:09:23.690 --> 00:09:27.610
across the various settlements.
Contrary to the “Lord of the Flies” expectations

00:09:27.610 --> 00:09:31.730
of a group of people isolated and afraid,
there’s immense cooperation between the

00:09:31.730 --> 00:09:37.470
trapped civilians. The food in the several
Ikea restaurants in SCP-3008-1 mysteriously

00:09:37.470 --> 00:09:42.329
replenishes while nobody is there, so there’s
no threat of starving. And the automatic turning

00:09:42.329 --> 00:09:47.500
on and off of the lights forms a kind of rudimentary
day and night cycle. Night time, however,

00:09:47.500 --> 00:09:52.860
is when things get dangerous, as the SCP-3008-2
entities – which are known to the people

00:09:52.860 --> 00:09:57.110
inside as “The Staff” – become extremely
hostile after dark.

00:09:57.110 --> 00:10:01.560
Aggressive hordes of the Staff swarm the settlements
at night, repeating “The store is now closed,

00:10:01.560 --> 00:10:05.529
please exit the building.” The civilians
inside are usually able to repel these attacks

00:10:05.529 --> 00:10:10.069
with minimal casualties, but the constant
war of attrition slowly wears down those inside.

00:10:10.069 --> 00:10:14.149
The bodies of the creatures also need to be
removed from the area after each attack, as

00:10:14.149 --> 00:10:18.110
the presence of corpses or even parts of corpses
has been known to heighten the ferocity of

00:10:18.110 --> 00:10:22.689
the next night’s attack. During the day,
the Staff return to a docile and unresponsive

00:10:22.689 --> 00:10:26.879
state, though they’ll still defend themselves
violently if anyone dares to attack.

00:10:26.879 --> 00:10:30.460
Over the course of the interviews with the
fourteen escapees, Foundation Researchers

00:10:30.460 --> 00:10:35.200
were able to answer another of their key questions:
How had so many people gone missing in the

00:10:35.200 --> 00:10:39.930
store for so long without being noticed? But
the answer they received only raised many

00:10:39.930 --> 00:10:44.740
more unsettling queries. According to the
escapees, there were people inside the settlements

00:10:44.740 --> 00:10:49.089
that, despite being otherwise of entirely
sound mind and standard intelligence, seemed

00:10:49.089 --> 00:10:53.680
to lack very common knowledge that even a
child should know. For example, some weren’t

00:10:53.680 --> 00:10:57.819
aware of the International Space Station orbiting
the earth, or stranger still, the existence

00:10:57.819 --> 00:11:01.079
of the Statue of Liberty.
This led the Researchers to a frightening

00:11:01.079 --> 00:11:07.930
conclusion: SCP-3008-1 may not only be a nexus
point of multiple Ikea stores in our dimension,

00:11:07.930 --> 00:11:12.509
it could be connected to Ikeas in every dimension
where Ikeas exist. While it only abducts a

00:11:12.509 --> 00:11:16.670
handful of people from each store over an
extended period of time, it suddenly becomes

00:11:16.670 --> 00:11:21.009
clear how this SCP was able to trap so many
people without detection over such a long

00:11:21.009 --> 00:11:24.649
period of time.
Which, in turn, led to an even more terrifying

00:11:24.649 --> 00:11:31.250
revelation: The SCP Foundation may not have
SCP-3008-1 as contained as they thought. It

00:11:31.250 --> 00:11:36.519
might even be tucked away in an Ikea somewhere
near you, just waiting for you to visit. After

00:11:36.519 --> 00:11:41.509
all, there’s always room for one more…
There are some things human beings aren’t

00:11:41.509 --> 00:11:45.970
meant to know, and it’s the sworn duty of
The SCP Foundation to discover and contain

00:11:45.970 --> 00:11:50.589
such information. But sometimes, knowledge
is discovered that shakes even the Foundation

00:11:50.589 --> 00:11:56.889
itself to its very core. One such discovery
occurred on April 28th, 2016 – the night

00:11:56.889 --> 00:12:02.250
that SCP – 2935 made itself known to Foundation
personnel. To this day, the exact nature of

00:12:02.250 --> 00:12:08.819
SCP – 2935 is a mystery that even the Foundation’s
brightest minds can’t completely understand.

00:12:08.819 --> 00:12:14.660
Everything we know about SCP – 2935 today
comes from three doomed missions into the

00:12:14.660 --> 00:12:19.279
anomalous zone’s interior. This is the story
of those infamous expeditions.

00:12:19.279 --> 00:12:25.139
The nightmare began around 5:00 AM, when SCP
Foundation Site 81 in Bloomingdale, Indiana,

00:12:25.139 --> 00:12:29.860
intercepted a distorted radio signal. Communications
personnel at the site traced this strange

00:12:29.860 --> 00:12:35.411
signal back to the unincorporated area of
Joppa, Indiana, near US Interstate 70. As

00:12:35.411 --> 00:12:40.310
is Foundation policy, a team of Field Agents
were dispatched to the location in order to

00:12:40.310 --> 00:12:44.920
determine what they were dealing with. However,
rather than finding anything that could logically

00:12:44.920 --> 00:12:50.230
produce such a signal, they instead discovered
a long abandoned cemetery. The most recent

00:12:50.230 --> 00:12:54.999
death on any of the tombstones was recorded
as being over a hundred years ago, all the

00:12:54.999 --> 00:12:59.180
way back in 1908.
On further investigation, the Foundation discovered

00:12:59.180 --> 00:13:03.910
an unmapped limestone cave opening beneath
the cemetery and when they sent a drone into

00:13:03.910 --> 00:13:08.550
the depths of the cave, it appeared to quickly
exit out the other side of the cave. But something

00:13:08.550 --> 00:13:12.370
wasn’t right. The area that the drone was
observing appeared consistent with the landscape

00:13:12.370 --> 00:13:16.860
from which it’d entered, but now it looked
somehow…greyer. It lacked the color and

00:13:16.860 --> 00:13:21.430
life of the place it’d just come from. The
grass was dead. There were no trees, no shrubs,

00:13:21.430 --> 00:13:25.589
no animals or birds in the sky.
They weren’t looking at our world. They

00:13:25.589 --> 00:13:29.480
were looking at a strange reflection of our
world on the other side of the cave. In fact,

00:13:29.480 --> 00:13:36.110
it wasn’t a cave at all – it was a passageway
between two dimensions. It was SCP – 2935.

00:13:36.110 --> 00:13:40.009
Just then they were able to unscramble the
distorted transmission they’d been receiving.

00:13:40.009 --> 00:13:43.189
It went as follows:
“This is an automated emergency broadcast

00:13:43.189 --> 00:13:48.089
from the SCP Foundation and your national
government. One or more of our sites is experiencing

00:13:48.089 --> 00:13:52.810
a communication breakdown, likely due to a
containment breach of unknown magnitude. All

00:13:52.810 --> 00:13:57.309
citizens are ordered to stay in their homes
as containment teams work to secure the breach.

00:13:57.309 --> 00:14:00.380
This message will broadcast from April 20th,
2016 until—”

00:14:00.380 --> 00:14:06.290
At that point, the message would cut and repeat,
as it had been for eight straight days. The

00:14:06.290 --> 00:14:11.730
message’s source? Site 81. But not this
Site 81. The SCP Foundation was receiving

00:14:11.730 --> 00:14:16.329
an emergency distress signal from themselves
in another dimension – a bizarre event that

00:14:16.329 --> 00:14:19.019
even the Foundation had never experienced
before.

00:14:19.019 --> 00:14:23.260
The Field Agents were terrified by the implications
of what they’d just heard and contacted

00:14:23.260 --> 00:14:27.779
Site 81 Command to request additional units.
The Foundation wished to fully understand

00:14:27.779 --> 00:14:31.509
this anomaly as quickly as possible, due to
the potential threat it could pose towards

00:14:31.509 --> 00:14:36.600
the Foundation, so they dispatched Mobile
Task Force Epsilon-13, codenamed “Manifest

00:14:36.600 --> 00:14:40.879
Destiny”, to perform the first of three
manned missions into the heart of the anomalous

00:14:40.879 --> 00:14:44.790
zone.
The first exploratory mission into SCP – 2935

00:14:44.790 --> 00:14:48.990
was codenamed “Gauntlet”, and consisted
of a four-man team fitted with full hazmat

00:14:48.990 --> 00:14:53.639
suits and direct video and audio links to
mission command. The team was led by a Field

00:14:53.639 --> 00:14:59.880
Operative known only as Agent Juno. His subordinates
were Agents Kael, Devon, and Underwood. Their

00:14:59.880 --> 00:15:03.990
directive was to gather samples and survey
the area positioned directly around the insertion

00:15:03.990 --> 00:15:08.230
point, meaning the other cave mouth of SCP
– 2935.

00:15:08.230 --> 00:15:11.830
The mission only lasted about an hour, but
what they saw in there would stay with these

00:15:11.830 --> 00:15:16.100
men for the rest of their lives.
After a fifteen-minute trek through the cave,

00:15:16.100 --> 00:15:20.059
Manifest Destiny arrived in the mirror dimension
where they were struck by the eerie silence

00:15:20.059 --> 00:15:24.499
of a place that seemed identical and yet so
different from their home dimension. The first

00:15:24.499 --> 00:15:30.189
observation they made was the total absence
of all living vegetation. Trees, grass, weeds,

00:15:30.189 --> 00:15:33.980
everything – it was all dead. On orders
from their superiors back in the original

00:15:33.980 --> 00:15:38.399
dimension – that we’ll refer to from here
on as Dimension Prime – Manifest Destiny

00:15:38.399 --> 00:15:41.800
headed deeper into the mirror dimension of
SCP – 2935.

00:15:41.800 --> 00:15:46.510
They travelled two kilometers without detecting
a single sign of plant or animal life. Not

00:15:46.510 --> 00:15:51.370
even insects. Eventually, they came upon a
farm house with two cars parked outside. With

00:15:51.370 --> 00:15:55.930
authorization from Command, Manifest Destiny
breached the house and headed inside. Agent

00:15:55.930 --> 00:15:59.829
Kael confirmed that there was still power
flowing to the building, as the lighting appeared

00:15:59.829 --> 00:16:04.709
to work just fine, but they came upon a horrifying
discovery in the house’s dining room: Three

00:16:04.709 --> 00:16:09.579
adult corpses, two female and one male, were
seated at the table. A fourth corpse, that

00:16:09.579 --> 00:16:12.629
of a male child, was sprawled out on the ground
nearby.

00:16:12.629 --> 00:16:16.920
If the death of what looked to be an entire
family wasn’t awful enough, the Manifest

00:16:16.920 --> 00:16:21.209
Destiny team noticed a number of other alarming
details. There were no signs of decomposition

00:16:21.209 --> 00:16:25.350
on the bodies, nor did there appear to be
any obvious cause of death. The family’s

00:16:25.350 --> 00:16:29.050
last meal was still on the table – Chicken,
mashed potatoes, and green beans. While the

00:16:29.050 --> 00:16:33.550
food looked cold and stale, there was no evidence
of rot or spoiling. The team found an opened

00:16:33.550 --> 00:16:38.339
newspaper dated April 19th, 2016, illustrating
that the family may have died a full eight

00:16:38.339 --> 00:16:43.339
days before the discovery. In Dimension Prime,
decay would already be well underway by that

00:16:43.339 --> 00:16:47.889
point, yet here, there wasn’t even a smell.
Instead, everything was just covered in a

00:16:47.889 --> 00:16:52.490
thin layer of dust. Command requested that
Manifest Destiny collect samples of the food

00:16:52.490 --> 00:16:57.380
as well as hair, skin, and fluids from the
corpses for further study. Small electronics

00:16:57.380 --> 00:17:01.379
like smart phones were also taken from the
bodies. Agent Devon turned on the television

00:17:01.379 --> 00:17:05.429
in the living room, and found that, while
most stations were now running test signals,

00:17:05.429 --> 00:17:09.510
the shopping channel was still live. Well
the feed was live at least. Both hosts sat

00:17:09.510 --> 00:17:14.059
in front of the cameras, dead, but perfectly
preserved. The date on the screen read April

00:17:14.059 --> 00:17:19.360
28th, 2016, suggesting that the times of Dimension
Prime and the Mirror Dimension were exactly

00:17:19.360 --> 00:17:22.260
the same.
In fact everything seemed the same, the only

00:17:22.260 --> 00:17:27.029
difference between the two dimensions being
that some kind of mysterious apocalyptic event

00:17:27.029 --> 00:17:32.110
had occurred in the last eight days in SCP
– 2935’s Mirror Dimension, but exactly

00:17:32.110 --> 00:17:36.770
what had happened, or how, remained a mystery.
When Manifest Destiny exited the farm house,

00:17:36.770 --> 00:17:40.730
they once again remarked on the lack of all
signs of life around them. At this point,

00:17:40.730 --> 00:17:45.600
the team returned to the insertion point of
SCP – 2935, but were instructed to remain

00:17:45.600 --> 00:17:49.510
in the Mirror Dimension while additional units
joined them inside.

00:17:49.510 --> 00:17:53.679
Manifest Destiny swelled to sixteen members,
with the notable addition of Agent Roy as

00:17:53.679 --> 00:17:57.570
the new commanding field officer. The team
split into two groups of eight, and Agent

00:17:57.570 --> 00:18:02.610
Roy and his men infiltrated the Mirror Dimension’s
Site 81 while Agent Juno’s detachment attempted

00:18:02.610 --> 00:18:07.450
to access the base’s off-site deep storage
servers. This second expedition was codenamed

00:18:07.450 --> 00:18:11.480
“Overland”, and led the Foundation’s
Field Agents even deeper into the terrifying

00:18:11.480 --> 00:18:16.890
mystery of SCP – 2935.
Accessing the site was easy for Roy’s detachment.

00:18:16.890 --> 00:18:20.679
It seemed there were relatively few cars on
the road at the time of the mysterious Extinction

00:18:20.679 --> 00:18:25.120
Event. In the distance, fires still smoldered
in the wreckage of planes that looked to have

00:18:25.120 --> 00:18:29.980
just dropped out of the sky. Agent Roy and
his team, like all SCP Foundation personnel,

00:18:29.980 --> 00:18:33.890
were fitted with vitals trackers, and they
assumed that the distress signal that started

00:18:33.890 --> 00:18:37.960
this whole thing could have been triggered
by the deaths of every member of the Foundation

00:18:37.960 --> 00:18:42.930
at once in the Mirror Universe. Once inside
Site 81, they realized that assumption was

00:18:42.930 --> 00:18:46.299
probably right.
Going door to door in the administrative wing,

00:18:46.299 --> 00:18:50.200
they found the perfectly preserved corpses
of everyone they knew to be stationed there

00:18:50.200 --> 00:18:55.060
in Dimension Prime. People without a doubt
were still alive in their universe. Samples

00:18:55.060 --> 00:18:58.650
from the corpses that the Foundation would
later study even confirmed the reason that

00:18:58.650 --> 00:19:03.080
the bodies were perfectly preserved: The corpses
had experienced complete and sudden death

00:19:03.080 --> 00:19:07.340
on a cellular level, and even the bacteria
that would typically take part in the decomposition

00:19:07.340 --> 00:19:13.960
process had died with it. In SCP – 2935,
death was total and absolute across all types

00:19:13.960 --> 00:19:17.210
of life forms.
As Agent Roy’s team ventured further into

00:19:17.210 --> 00:19:22.360
the bowels of Site 81, they made another unsettling
discovery - their own corpses, in roughly

00:19:22.360 --> 00:19:27.850
the spots they had been inside Dimension Prime’s
Site 81 eight days prior. Some of the Foundation’s

00:19:27.850 --> 00:19:32.950
top scientists, including the esteemed Dr.
Bright, were also found dead inside the facility.

00:19:32.950 --> 00:19:37.640
In an attempt to see just how far this unexplained
phenomenon stretched, Agent Roy’s team decided

00:19:37.640 --> 00:19:43.100
to inspect the containment cells – where
they found that all the Mirror Universe SCPs,

00:19:43.100 --> 00:19:48.200
including SCP – 2996, were dead.
In his desperation to find some kind of exception

00:19:48.200 --> 00:19:52.919
to the Extinction Event, Agent Roy revealed
a terrifying secret to the rest of his team:

00:19:52.919 --> 00:19:58.669
SCP – 682, the immortal, misanthropic lizard,
and one of the deadliest creatures known to

00:19:58.669 --> 00:20:03.049
the SCP Foundation, was contained at this
very facility, right below them. Could it

00:20:03.049 --> 00:20:06.500
have something to do with what was going on
here? They descended into its containment

00:20:06.500 --> 00:20:12.700
facility to discover an even more unsettling
truth. SCP – 682, the unkillable anomaly,

00:20:12.700 --> 00:20:18.380
floated dead in its tank Death truly made
no exceptions within SCP – 2935.

00:20:18.380 --> 00:20:22.620
Agent Roy’s team left the site and rendezvoused
with Agent Juno’s team to send their research

00:20:22.620 --> 00:20:26.461
and back to Dimension Prime using automated
drones. Both teams remained in the Mirror

00:20:26.461 --> 00:20:30.820
Dimension for another manned operation, codenamed
“Nineteen,” they had no idea it would

00:20:30.820 --> 00:20:35.360
be their final mission. As they descended
deeper into the facility, passing more dead

00:20:35.360 --> 00:20:40.440
SCPs they discovered one final clue. Based
on the last activity of the Foundation servers,

00:20:40.440 --> 00:20:46.399
the event occurred at roughly 3:00 AM.
While underground in SCP – 2935’s Site

00:20:46.399 --> 00:20:51.220
81, the team accidentally activated the base’s
on-site nuclear weapon – a failsafe meant

00:20:51.220 --> 00:20:55.890
to be detonated in the case of an emergency
containment breach. Due to the base’s failsafe

00:20:55.890 --> 00:21:00.860
protocols, every member of the Manifest Destiny
team was locked and sealed inside Site 81.

00:21:00.860 --> 00:21:05.761
They, along with everything else, were incinerated
in the nuclear blast. Once again, the Mirror

00:21:05.761 --> 00:21:11.620
Universe inside of SCP – 2935 was lifeless.
But that isn’t where this ends. When the

00:21:11.620 --> 00:21:16.850
automated drones returned out of the SCP – 2935
cave to the Field Operatives in Dimension

00:21:16.850 --> 00:21:21.519
Prime, they were in for their own horrifying
discovery. None of the footage or information

00:21:21.519 --> 00:21:27.451
gathered from SCP – 2935 illuminated how
or why the Extinction Event occurred. Everyone

00:21:27.451 --> 00:21:32.299
and everything simply dropped dead at the
exact same moment. Nobody was aware, nobody

00:21:32.299 --> 00:21:36.490
was prepared. Death came suddenly and silently,
and none were spared.

00:21:36.490 --> 00:21:40.220
All the Foundation on Dimension Prime were
left with was a message from one of the agents

00:21:40.220 --> 00:21:44.760
from Manifest Destiny, Agent Keller. His final
message was: “I don't have any answers.

00:21:44.760 --> 00:21:48.162
I don't think there are any. I'll do this
one thing, and hope that fixes it. Seal it

00:21:48.162 --> 00:21:53.210
shut. You've got to lock it in here with us.
I'm sorry.” The Foundation were at first

00:21:53.210 --> 00:21:57.779
confused by this, until they discovered a
final encrypted audio log buried in the files

00:21:57.779 --> 00:22:00.390
recovered from the Mirror Universe’s Site
81.

00:22:00.390 --> 00:22:04.370
It was a message from Keller himself, but
not the Keller from Universe Prime. In this

00:22:04.370 --> 00:22:08.600
message, Keller described the Foundation in
the Mirror Universe receiving the exact same

00:22:08.600 --> 00:22:13.460
distorted transmission that they did a few
days earlier from a cave in Joppa. When he

00:22:13.460 --> 00:22:17.549
and the others were dispatched inside, they
discovered the same lifeless, post-Extinction

00:22:17.549 --> 00:22:22.820
Event world that was now so familiar to Foundation
Command. But there was a key difference: This

00:22:22.820 --> 00:22:27.350
wasn’t the Mirror Dimension they’d just
been studying, but a third, entirely different

00:22:27.350 --> 00:22:29.610
dimension.
In his haunting final words, Mirror Dimension

00:22:29.610 --> 00:22:34.000
Keller admits that whatever caused the event
in that third dimension – an entity that

00:22:34.000 --> 00:22:39.220
Mirror Dimension Keller believed was the spectre
of Death itself – had followed him back

00:22:39.220 --> 00:22:45.240
into his world, and history had repeated itself.
SCP – 2935 was the passageway through which

00:22:45.240 --> 00:22:49.990
absolute death could pass from dimension to
dimension, and our dimension was the next

00:22:49.990 --> 00:22:54.720
in line. The deaths of Manifest Destiny may
have saved our entire universe, as anyone

00:22:54.720 --> 00:22:59.060
passing back through the cave had the potential
to bring Death itself back with them.

00:22:59.060 --> 00:23:02.940
The Foundation decided, in the end, to follow
Keller’s advice. They sealed the entrance

00:23:02.940 --> 00:23:08.340
to SCP – 2935 with concrete, and now keep
it under constant watch, since what waits

00:23:08.340 --> 00:23:13.159
behind the barrier is an entity even they
have no power to stop if it ever got through.

00:23:13.159 --> 00:23:17.730
After all, it had killed them all before,
or at least another version of them. What’s

00:23:17.730 --> 00:23:22.220
one more dimension on the pile? While it may
now just seem like a simple slab of concrete

00:23:22.220 --> 00:23:27.789
under an abandoned cemetery, this is why SCP
– 2935 might just be the most dangerous

00:23:27.789 --> 00:23:32.610
SCP of all.
A month ago, Dr. Robert Maxwell was a senior

00:23:32.610 --> 00:23:38.260
researcher working at the facility, but a
tragic mistake had cost the lives of several

00:23:38.260 --> 00:23:43.560
of his co-researchers. Now he was being led
down a bleak hallway in Armed Bio-Containment

00:23:43.560 --> 00:23:49.910
Area-14, a rifle-wielding guard flanking him
on either side. The once rising researcher

00:23:49.910 --> 00:23:58.559
had a very different title now: D-8724. He
had been made a D-Class personnel… a death

00:23:58.559 --> 00:24:01.850
sentence.
However, as the guards led him to his possible

00:24:01.850 --> 00:24:07.530
demise, he wasn’t dressed in the typical
D-Class orange jumpsuit. No, he was dressed

00:24:07.530 --> 00:24:14.039
in frilly, rococo dining wear more typical
of 18th century France. If anything, Dr. Maxwell

00:24:14.039 --> 00:24:19.779
looked like he was on his way to meet royalty.
And, in a sense, he was.

00:24:19.779 --> 00:24:24.490
The former researcher had begged for any other
assignment, but the site director insisted

00:24:24.490 --> 00:24:30.649
on committing Dr. Maxwell to teatime with
SCP – 082. He’d always been the talkative

00:24:30.649 --> 00:24:36.049
type, so the two would make a perfect pairing,
and if the creature found him sufficiently

00:24:36.049 --> 00:24:40.940
amusing, then Maxwell might even leave the
containment cell alive. He’d heard legends

00:24:40.940 --> 00:24:46.530
of the giant creature they called The Cannibal.
Maxwell hoped they were just stories.

00:24:46.530 --> 00:24:51.750
Dr. Maxwell was pushed by the guards into
a large, luxuriously-appointed room and the

00:24:51.750 --> 00:24:57.260
doors were locked behind him. He felt like
a child, surrounded by freakishly large furniture

00:24:57.260 --> 00:25:02.510
and ten foot high ceilings. The fog of obnoxious
floral perfumes couldn’t fully cover up

00:25:02.510 --> 00:25:07.559
the pervasive smell of death that lingered
in the cavernous halls of 082’s palace.

00:25:07.559 --> 00:25:14.990
Thanks to an elaborate ruse conducted by the
Foundation, SCP-082 believed he was the king

00:25:14.990 --> 00:25:19.789
of France, and that his containment cell was
a palace where he remained for his own safety.

00:25:19.789 --> 00:25:24.500
The creature’s continued good behaviour
and everyone else’s safety relied on visitors

00:25:24.500 --> 00:25:28.460
keeping up that lie.
Maxwell had never worked in this area of the

00:25:28.460 --> 00:25:33.990
facility, so a lot of the standard procedures
were new to him. Still, his superior had given

00:25:33.990 --> 00:25:40.720
him a clear directive: Talk to the monster,
communicate with him. Be cordial and friendly.

00:25:40.720 --> 00:25:46.440
See if you can find out more about his mysterious
past. And most importantly: If you want to

00:25:46.440 --> 00:25:51.500
survive, don’t annoy him.
The down-on-his-luck scientist gulped and

00:25:51.500 --> 00:25:57.299
sighed, trying to steady his nerves in this
oversized, fake French palace. He just kept

00:25:57.299 --> 00:26:02.330
thinking “Surely he can’t be that big?”
He almost talked himself into believing that

00:26:02.330 --> 00:26:07.700
the accounts of the creature were just that
- tall tales - until a huge figure began lumbering

00:26:07.700 --> 00:26:16.330
into the main chamber. It was him: SCP – 082,
also known as Fernand The Cannibal.

00:26:16.330 --> 00:26:22.309
SCP-082 was an eight-foot-tall hulking monster,
built sturdier than the castles it likes to

00:26:22.309 --> 00:26:27.950
imagine are its true home. Swollen, bloated,
and grossly out of proportion, the creature

00:26:27.950 --> 00:26:33.940
clocks in at over seven hundred pounds – most
of which is pure muscle that’s almost impossible

00:26:33.940 --> 00:26:41.230
to pierce with conventional weaponry. SCP-082
stopped just feet away and stared at Dr. Maxwell

00:26:41.230 --> 00:26:45.529
with its beady, sunken-in eyes, like a hungry
rat.

00:26:45.529 --> 00:26:50.120
Just the sight of it struck terror into Dr.
Maxwell’s heart, but he didn’t dare show

00:26:50.120 --> 00:26:56.149
his fear. Instead he remembered his brief
training, bowing politely and forcing a smile,

00:26:56.149 --> 00:27:01.250
referring to the creature as “your highness”
and profusely thanking it for granting him

00:27:01.250 --> 00:27:06.769
an audience. The monster continued staring
without saying anything and then gave a wide,

00:27:06.769 --> 00:27:13.179
lock-jawed grin, showing off its huge teeth.
It did everything through gritted teeth, except

00:27:13.179 --> 00:27:18.080
eat and sing. Dr. Maxwell hoped he wouldn’t
be a part of either activity.

00:27:18.080 --> 00:27:24.509
Fernand gave a low, booming chuckle. He thanked
Dr. Maxwell for coming to give him some company

00:27:24.509 --> 00:27:29.450
and invited him to come further inside and
take a seat. Adding, with a sly wink, that

00:27:29.450 --> 00:27:33.159
he won’t bite.
The monster complained that he so rarely gets

00:27:33.159 --> 00:27:37.690
visitors to the palace these days – but
he omitted the fact that the main reason for

00:27:37.690 --> 00:27:43.290
this was his tendency to devour them.
Maxwell nodded and followed the giant deeper

00:27:43.290 --> 00:27:47.700
into its oversized abode. He couldn’t help
but notice that the monster’s arms looked

00:27:47.700 --> 00:27:53.000
like huge, fleshy punching bags. He knew that
if Fernand wanted to, he could easily crush

00:27:53.000 --> 00:27:58.710
him flat, just like he’d done to so many
unfortunate guards during containment breaches.

00:27:58.710 --> 00:28:03.730
Fernand told Dr. Maxwell that he was thinking
of having some decorating work done. The walls

00:28:03.730 --> 00:28:08.010
of his palace were starting to look awfully
drab and he gestured to one covered with a

00:28:08.010 --> 00:28:13.419
rusty red streak. Maxwell remembered that
D-Class cleaners were sent into the containment

00:28:13.419 --> 00:28:18.500
cell twice a month to tidy any of Fernand’s
messes, but they often ended up becoming one

00:28:18.500 --> 00:28:22.550
the messes themself.
The creature encouraged Maxwell to take a

00:28:22.550 --> 00:28:27.269
seat at his oversized dining table, while
he tended to a pot of what he said was full

00:28:27.269 --> 00:28:32.500
of delicious onion soup. Maxwell obliged his
host’s request and took a seat at a huge

00:28:32.500 --> 00:28:37.409
chair that made him look like a six-year-old
sitting at the grownups’ table. Meanwhile,

00:28:37.409 --> 00:28:42.400
Fernand was using a huge machete-like knife
to cleave onions in half for his bubbling

00:28:42.400 --> 00:28:47.590
pot of stew. Even though Fernand had shown
no signs of outward aggression, as he watched

00:28:47.590 --> 00:28:52.160
the Cannibal hack away at onions with his
enormous knife, Maxwell could feel himself

00:28:52.160 --> 00:28:56.460
beginning to sweat.
After all, they didn’t call this creature

00:28:56.460 --> 00:29:01.930
“The Cannibal” for nothing – this was
a monster with a truly horrifying body count.

00:29:01.930 --> 00:29:05.909
During previous containment breaches it had
taken enough tranquilizer to put down two

00:29:05.909 --> 00:29:10.840
elephants to subdue the creature, but not
before multiple agents quite literally lost

00:29:10.840 --> 00:29:16.610
their heads in the process. Fernand was able
to bite them off with one huge chomp, like

00:29:16.610 --> 00:29:20.909
he was eating a drumstick, snapping right
through bone with his incredible tooth and

00:29:20.909 --> 00:29:24.070
jaw strength
Surprisingly when he wasn’t on a violent

00:29:24.070 --> 00:29:30.789
rampage, foundation researchers had found
SCP-082 to be unusually polite and forthcoming,

00:29:30.789 --> 00:29:36.000
offering the researchers plenty of information
about himself and his past. The only problem

00:29:36.000 --> 00:29:41.080
was that almost everything the creature said
was a complete lie.

00:29:41.080 --> 00:29:45.250
From his time as a researcher, Maxwell knew
that there were only a few details about the

00:29:45.250 --> 00:29:50.970
creature that could be ascertained for certain
- SCP-082 would reliably answer to the name

00:29:50.970 --> 00:29:56.210
“Fernand”, and genetically, Fernand was
technically human. The means by which Fernand

00:29:56.210 --> 00:30:03.159
became so grotesquely huge, strong, and cannibalistic
are still unknown – Foundation personnel

00:30:03.159 --> 00:30:07.900
are still looking into whether it’s due
to some kind of anomalous genetic mutation,

00:30:07.900 --> 00:30:14.130
or by more supernatural means. All we know
is that he’s big, unpredictable, and extremely

00:30:14.130 --> 00:30:18.750
dangerous.
Dr. Robert Maxwell sat, terrified, at the

00:30:18.750 --> 00:30:24.029
dining table of SCP – 082, listening to
Fernand’s slightly dull blade chop through

00:30:24.029 --> 00:30:28.889
the final onion, which he then tossed into
the boiling soup. Fernand had switched the

00:30:28.889 --> 00:30:34.510
topic of conversation to one of his favorite
fictional characters – Hannibal Lecter.

00:30:34.510 --> 00:30:38.799
Of course, Hannibal the Cannibal isn’t quite
so fictional to Fernand. While he’s been

00:30:38.799 --> 00:30:43.240
shown to be extremely intelligent in terms
of puzzle-solving and memory, he seems to

00:30:43.240 --> 00:30:48.799
have no understanding of the distinction between
fiction and reality. He assumes all movies

00:30:48.799 --> 00:30:52.700
and TV shows are a form of documentary or
reality television.

00:30:52.700 --> 00:30:58.629
And ever since seeing The Silence of the Lambs,
Fernand has been eager to meet with Dr. Lecter,

00:30:58.629 --> 00:31:03.889
which he emphasized to Maxwell over and over.
Since trying to explain the concept of fiction

00:31:03.889 --> 00:31:09.019
to Fernand has never previously worked, Maxwell
simply told him that Dr. Lecter is extremely

00:31:09.019 --> 00:31:14.429
busy at the moment, but will visit whenever
he gets a chance. This seemed to satisfy Fernand,

00:31:14.429 --> 00:31:19.019
who placed two large bowls of steaming soup
on the table before sitting down a little

00:31:19.019 --> 00:31:23.520
too close to Maxwell. He couldn’t help but
notice that the giant cannibal was now sitting

00:31:23.520 --> 00:31:29.269
within biting distance, and as a lowly D-Class,
nobody would be rushing in to save him if

00:31:29.269 --> 00:31:32.899
things went south.
Fernand began ranting through his clenched

00:31:32.899 --> 00:31:38.490
teeth once more, occasionally stopping to
consume a hefty spoonful of onion soup. Maxwell

00:31:38.490 --> 00:31:44.120
was sure to do the same, not wanting to seem
anything less than polite. But soon, the tenor

00:31:44.120 --> 00:31:49.220
of Fernand’s rant began to shift. Typically,
the monster spoke French or heavily accented

00:31:49.220 --> 00:31:54.429
English. Now, he was affecting the accent
of a Victorian gentleman, peppering his speech

00:31:54.429 --> 00:32:00.370
with “tally ho” and “the game is afoot.”
Maxwell was confused at first, but quickly

00:32:00.370 --> 00:32:05.190
realized the game Fernand was playing.
It’s well known that Fernand is a pathological

00:32:05.190 --> 00:32:11.370
liar who likes to play numerous characters,
changing his mannerisms and clothes accordingly.

00:32:11.370 --> 00:32:17.460
These personas have included: A vampire, Big
Bird, André the Giant, Foundation researcher

00:32:17.460 --> 00:32:23.740
Dr. Bright, The Incredible Hulk, Alexander
The Great, Captain Hook, Dr. Frankenstein,

00:32:23.740 --> 00:32:29.759
and Frankenstein's Monster.
And of course, in this case, the iconic fictional

00:32:29.759 --> 00:32:34.600
detective Sherlock Holmes.
Fearing for his life in this strange situation,

00:32:34.600 --> 00:32:40.510
Dr. Maxwell did the only thing he could - Play
along. As Fernand reeled off his Holmesian

00:32:40.510 --> 00:32:45.549
delusions, Maxwell began to play the role
of Dr. John Watson, asking follow-up questions

00:32:45.549 --> 00:32:50.179
and complimenting Fernand’s “impeccable”
deductive reasoning. And it seemed to be working

00:32:50.179 --> 00:32:55.769
– Fernand played along too, acting as though
the two of them really were Arthur Conan Doyle’s

00:32:55.769 --> 00:33:00.370
crime-fighting duo. Towards the end of their
game, Dr. Maxwell was even starting to enjoy

00:33:00.370 --> 00:33:05.000
it, amazed that his quick thinking was actually
keeping him safe.

00:33:05.000 --> 00:33:10.409
But just then the Cannibal froze, as if in
a trance. He locked eyes with Dr. Maxwell

00:33:10.409 --> 00:33:15.120
– like a mad dog, that you can’t tell
if it’s going to bite you or not. He saw

00:33:15.120 --> 00:33:20.490
the creature’s gargantuan teeth separating,
its huge jaws stretching open. This could

00:33:20.490 --> 00:33:26.529
surely only mean one thing. Dr. Maxwell winced
and prepared for death, cursing that all his

00:33:26.529 --> 00:33:32.509
quick thinking had amounted to nothing.
Fernand leaned towards him, his gaping maw

00:33:32.509 --> 00:33:38.840
with its hot onion scented breath just inches
away from Maxwell. And then… he began to

00:33:38.840 --> 00:33:44.700
sing – the Cannibal broke into a raucous
Victorian pub song, happy and jovial. In his

00:33:44.700 --> 00:33:50.580
moment of terror, Dr. Maxwell had forgotten
that this was the other reason SCP – 082

00:33:50.580 --> 00:33:56.669
opens his nightmarish jaws. Relief washed
over him, as he knew he was safe, at least

00:33:56.669 --> 00:34:03.399
for a moment. Not long after, foundation guards
arrived and escorted him from the cell, leaving

00:34:03.399 --> 00:34:08.600
the delusional giant to his own devices back
in the so-called palace.

00:34:08.600 --> 00:34:12.960
The former researcher had done it, he had
bested Fernand the Cannibal and hopefully

00:34:12.960 --> 00:34:18.761
it would be the last time he’d ever be face
to face with that deranged giant. Unfortunately

00:34:18.761 --> 00:34:24.020
for Dr. Robert Maxwell, in a performance review
later that week, one of his superiors remarked

00:34:24.020 --> 00:34:29.170
that Fernand enjoyed his company and he had
done a great job. Such a good job in fact,

00:34:29.170 --> 00:34:36.230
that Fernand insisted he have Dr. Maxwell
for dinner... or any other meal for that matter...

00:34:36.230 --> 00:34:40.860
sometime very soon.
The first thing that tipped the Foundation

00:34:40.860 --> 00:34:46.520
off to SCP-087’s presence were the reports
of numerous unexplained disappearances on

00:34:46.520 --> 00:34:50.560
campus. There were plenty of rumors about
what might be behind them, but Field Agents

00:34:50.560 --> 00:34:55.290
suspected that the true source of the vanishing
would be something beyond civilian imagination.

00:34:55.290 --> 00:35:00.950
All anyone knew for sure was that everyone
who had gone missing was last seen in a certain

00:35:00.950 --> 00:35:05.610
administrative building on the university
grounds, and that the disappearances only

00:35:05.610 --> 00:35:09.900
seemed to happen when the elevator was out.
The campus was soon flooded with Foundation

00:35:09.900 --> 00:35:15.280
agents, creating a barrier around the administrative
building, and the presumed habitat of SCP

00:35:15.280 --> 00:35:21.821
- 087. Nobody else could get in, and hopefully,
whatever was inside couldn’t get out. One

00:35:21.821 --> 00:35:26.680
of the Foundation’s lead scientists was
flown in to consult on the investigation.

00:35:26.680 --> 00:35:30.510
What could have been behind all those students
disappearing? The doctor’s preliminary interviews

00:35:30.510 --> 00:35:35.451
with university staff who worked in the building
yielded some interesting details: Strange

00:35:35.451 --> 00:35:40.500
noises, like banging and even a faint, shrill
crying, would be heard from a door that lead

00:35:40.500 --> 00:35:46.810
to a no longer used stairway in Hallway 3B.
Staff in the building had no reason to ever

00:35:46.810 --> 00:35:50.690
take these stairs, especially considering
how many of them reported a strange sense

00:35:50.690 --> 00:35:55.280
of unease when just standing outside the door.
The only reason someone might take those stairs

00:35:55.280 --> 00:36:01.750
is due to…Elevator malfunctions. In that
instant, the doctor had put it all together.

00:36:01.750 --> 00:36:05.690
The staff they interviewed had their memory
wiped with Amnetics – special chemicals

00:36:05.690 --> 00:36:10.740
used by the Foundation with the power to delete
human memories. The Foundation only used them

00:36:10.740 --> 00:36:15.381
for staff or civilians who had confirmed contact
with an SCP, and the doctor knew that they

00:36:15.381 --> 00:36:20.270
had a live one on their hands.
The staircase. There was something terribly

00:36:20.270 --> 00:36:26.231
wrong with that staircase, and it was the
SCP Foundation’s job to find out what – before

00:36:26.231 --> 00:36:32.821
it made anybody else disappear. This is the
story of SCP – 087, otherwise known as The

00:36:32.821 --> 00:36:38.190
Endless Staircase, and the three doomed journeys
down into its murky depths.

00:36:38.190 --> 00:36:43.170
The doctor was more than eager to begin research
into the staircase, and its frightening, anomalous

00:36:43.170 --> 00:36:47.830
properties. After all, you don’t claw your
way up to being one of the Foundation’s

00:36:47.830 --> 00:36:54.080
key researchers without being brave, and perhaps
just a little bit deranged. As was standard,

00:36:54.080 --> 00:36:59.190
once a perimeter was secured around the staircase,
the good doctor requested a selection of D-Class

00:36:59.190 --> 00:37:03.350
personnel for testing. For those not in the
know, D-Class is the Foundation’s polite

00:37:03.350 --> 00:37:07.880
way of saying “cannon fodder.”
The doctor was sent three D-Class prisoners

00:37:07.880 --> 00:37:15.420
for use in his investigation of SCP – 087.
The first, D-8432, was – according to official

00:37:15.420 --> 00:37:20.410
documentation on the incident – a “43-year
old male of average build and appearance and

00:37:20.410 --> 00:37:25.080
unremarkable psychological background.”
This man once worked for the Foundation in

00:37:25.080 --> 00:37:29.920
a more official capacity, but he was given
the often-deadly demotion to D-Class due to

00:37:29.920 --> 00:37:35.810
a dangerous mistake handling SCP – 682 that
lead to the deaths of several other agents.

00:37:35.810 --> 00:37:40.680
Now, it looked like it would be his turn.
The doctor explained his mission to him: Explore

00:37:40.680 --> 00:37:45.511
the staircase, gather data, help us find out
exactly what we’re dealing with here. If

00:37:45.511 --> 00:37:51.610
you come back alive, there may even be a promotion
in it for you. And with that promise, D-8432

00:37:51.610 --> 00:37:56.970
was given his load-out: a 75-watt flood lamp
with battery power capable of lasting 24 hours,

00:37:56.970 --> 00:38:03.370
an audio headset, and a handheld camcorder
fitted with a transmission stream.

00:38:03.370 --> 00:38:10.971
D-8432 was then pushed through the door in
Hallway 3B, and out onto the staircase. According

00:38:10.971 --> 00:38:17.510
to declassified Foundation files describing
the staircase, “SCP-087 is an unlit platform

00:38:17.510 --> 00:38:23.240
staircase. Stairs descend on a 38-degree angle
for 13 steps before reaching a semi-circular

00:38:23.240 --> 00:38:29.601
platform of approximately 3 meters in diameter.
Descent direction rotates 180 degrees at each

00:38:29.601 --> 00:38:36.750
platform. The design of SCP-087 limits subjects
to a visual range of approximately 1.5 flights.”

00:38:36.750 --> 00:38:42.770
But in D-8432’s mind, “unlit” really
didn’t seem like the right word. He would

00:38:42.770 --> 00:38:48.270
have chosen “all-consuming darkness.”
Despite carrying a powerful 75-watt lamp,

00:38:48.270 --> 00:38:53.441
D-8432 was only capable of partially lighting
the platform he was standing on – and the

00:38:53.441 --> 00:38:58.580
illumination only stretched down nine of the
thirteen steps to the next platform. When

00:38:58.580 --> 00:39:03.270
D-8432 observed how little help his lamp was
giving him, he was instructed to shine it

00:39:03.270 --> 00:39:09.070
out of the doorway into Hallway 3B. When he
did so, the light seemed to shine far further

00:39:09.070 --> 00:39:14.680
than it ever could in SCP – 087.
Already, the beginning of anomalous activity

00:39:14.680 --> 00:39:21.490
was obvious: Everywhere else, darkness is
just the absence of light. In SCP – 087,

00:39:21.490 --> 00:39:25.860
darkness eats light. It was like a tangible,
black mass that only a certain amount of light

00:39:25.860 --> 00:39:29.100
could survive, while the rest just wouldn’t
show.

00:39:29.100 --> 00:39:34.650
D-8432 swallowed hard over a lump in his throat.
The door to Hallway 3B was closed behind him,

00:39:34.650 --> 00:39:39.520
and he was ordered to descend. Surviving to
see that promotion was feeling unlikely, but

00:39:39.520 --> 00:39:45.450
it’s not like he had a choice. If he tried
to escape SCP – 087 before he was permitted,

00:39:45.450 --> 00:39:48.850
he’d be shot by SCP Foundation Field Agents
on the spot.

00:39:48.850 --> 00:39:52.900
So he followed the high-ranking doctor’s
orders and began to descend the steps to the

00:39:52.900 --> 00:39:57.720
next platform. Nothing about the physical
makeup of the staircase itself seemed abnormal

00:39:57.720 --> 00:40:02.960
– the base and walls were a very plain,
dull concrete, with a metal handrail. The

00:40:02.960 --> 00:40:07.450
only thing that seemed unique about it so
far was the strange light-bending properties.

00:40:07.450 --> 00:40:14.610
That was, until he reached the second platform
down and he heard it, a soft, echoing cry.

00:40:14.610 --> 00:40:20.350
A child’s cry. It was shrieks of panic,
or maybe even pain, echoing up from below.

00:40:20.350 --> 00:40:24.840
He was asked why he had stopped, and he explained
the crying sound he’d been hearing. It sounded

00:40:24.840 --> 00:40:29.810
like it was coming from far down the stairs,
maybe 200 meters below him. He could just

00:40:29.810 --> 00:40:34.290
make out the words “please”, help”,
and “down here” coming from the darkness.

00:40:34.290 --> 00:40:39.010
But the team outside the stairwell couldn’t
hear anything, so they asked him to descend

00:40:39.010 --> 00:40:41.610
further.
Another platform down, and they could hear

00:40:41.610 --> 00:40:45.720
it too, the unmistakable cries of a terrified
child.

00:40:45.720 --> 00:40:50.980
“Please”, “help”, and “down here.”
D-8432 was ordered to keep going and only

00:40:50.980 --> 00:40:57.371
stop if he noticed changes to the visual environment
or in the sounds he was hearing. D-8432, knowing

00:40:57.371 --> 00:41:02.130
his life was on the line, had to keep going,
and descended another twenty flights of stairs

00:41:02.130 --> 00:41:06.160
before stopping to remark that the sounds
of the child hadn’t gotten any closer. They

00:41:06.160 --> 00:41:10.880
still sounded just as far away as when he’d
first heard them. He was told his observations

00:41:10.880 --> 00:41:16.540
were noted, and pressured to continue. Within
half an hour, D-8432 had descended a full

00:41:16.540 --> 00:41:20.870
fifty floors, with no sign of a bottom in
sight.

00:41:20.870 --> 00:41:24.710
Somehow the volume of the child’s crying
had remained consistent throughout, as if

00:41:24.710 --> 00:41:30.920
it was moving away from D-8432 at the same
rate he was descending.

00:41:30.920 --> 00:41:33.980
At this point, D-8432 reported that he was
feeling uneasy. The doctor said that this

00:41:33.980 --> 00:41:38.190
was understandable, given the circumstances.
He’d been watching what little there was

00:41:38.190 --> 00:41:45.610
to see over a live video feed the entire time,
and something about the truly bottomless nature

00:41:45.610 --> 00:41:49.550
of the staircase, and the ever-elusive crying,
was undeniably eerie. But things were about

00:41:49.550 --> 00:41:55.000
to really take a turn for the worst. As D-8432
stepped forward towards the next set of stairs,

00:41:55.000 --> 00:41:58.550
he froze. There was something on the platform
below him, barely illuminated by the light

00:41:58.550 --> 00:42:04.950
of his 75-watt bulb.
It was a face. Vaguely human in size and shape,

00:42:04.950 --> 00:42:10.470
but with a few terrifying differences: it
had greyish skin, and no mouth, nostrils,

00:42:10.470 --> 00:42:17.310
or pupils. And yet, D-8432 could feel that
this thing was making eye contact with him.

00:42:17.310 --> 00:42:22.460
He couldn’t move, trapped in this thing’s
piercing gaze. In an instant, the face jerked

00:42:22.460 --> 00:42:28.030
forwards, suddenly only about a foot away
from D-8432’s face – eyes staring into

00:42:28.030 --> 00:42:33.740
his own. D-8432 screamed and ran, scaling
all fifty flights in an astonishing eighteen

00:42:33.740 --> 00:42:38.580
minutes, before charging out into Hallway
3B. There, he collapsed from the exhaustion

00:42:38.580 --> 00:42:43.460
and the fear of what he’d just seen.
Upon reviewing the footage, the strange face

00:42:43.460 --> 00:42:51.280
was designated “SCP-087-1.” Fascinating.
It was time for a second experiment. The doctor

00:42:51.280 --> 00:42:57.000
just had to know more.
The second test subject was D-9035, a 28-year-old

00:42:57.000 --> 00:43:01.260
male with a history of aggravated assaults
against women. He was given the same loadout

00:43:01.260 --> 00:43:06.800
as his predecessor, except this time with
an even more powerful 100-watt bulb. He was

00:43:06.800 --> 00:43:12.150
also given 100 small LED lights that had adhesive
backs and a battery life of approximately

00:43:12.150 --> 00:43:18.440
3 weeks, with which they intended to permanently
illuminate SCP – 087. However, despite the

00:43:18.440 --> 00:43:24.190
extra wattage of his bulb, he still couldn’t
illuminate beyond the ninth step. SCP – 087

00:43:24.190 --> 00:43:27.680
wouldn’t allow it.
Having no idea of the horrors that lurked

00:43:27.680 --> 00:43:32.490
below him, he descended on the doctor’s
orders, and began fixing the LEDs to walls

00:43:32.490 --> 00:43:37.620
of each platform he passed. The LED always
illuminated the landing, but the light couldn’t

00:43:37.620 --> 00:43:43.230
pass the first step on either side. The flights
of stairs themselves would remain in perpetual

00:43:43.230 --> 00:43:47.310
darkness.
After the second flight, D-9035 noticed the

00:43:47.310 --> 00:43:53.801
same crying D-8432 had heard and became uneasy.
Just like before, as D-9035 descended, the

00:43:53.801 --> 00:44:00.181
volume of the crying didn’t seem to increase,
as if for every step he descended, the source

00:44:00.181 --> 00:44:06.760
of the crying descended one, too, keeping
them at a constant 200 meters apart. Still,

00:44:06.760 --> 00:44:11.510
he was ordered to continue his descent and
the placing of LED’s even as his paranoia

00:44:11.510 --> 00:44:14.530
grew.
When he reached the 51s floor, he observed

00:44:14.530 --> 00:44:19.030
damage to the wall and steps – sections
appeared to have been smashed to rubble by

00:44:19.030 --> 00:44:24.360
an extreme force. As he descended past the
broken step, he only felt his fear, anxiety,

00:44:24.360 --> 00:44:30.710
and paranoia grow. The doctor made a note
of the fact that SCP – 087 seemed to cause

00:44:30.710 --> 00:44:37.800
instances of anxiety and terror in its occupants,
even before they encountered SCP – 087 – 1.

00:44:37.800 --> 00:44:45.200
As D-9035 reached platform 89 – a full 350
meters under the initial platform – he stopped

00:44:45.200 --> 00:44:50.780
dead in his tracks, and saw something staring
up at him from the platform below. That same

00:44:50.780 --> 00:44:55.970
terrible, grey face, with those dead, white
eyes.

00:44:55.970 --> 00:45:00.390
He was encouraged to stay calm and try to
get better footage of the face, but it charged

00:45:00.390 --> 00:45:06.740
for him and D-9035 ran for his life. He ascended
the staircase at a staggering pace, even passing

00:45:06.740 --> 00:45:13.080
out from exhaustion and remaining motionless
for 14 minutes half way. When D-9035 finally

00:45:13.080 --> 00:45:18.330
gathered the strength to get up, he scrambled
back to Hallway 3B and fell into a state of

00:45:18.330 --> 00:45:23.520
catatonia. He remains unresponsive to all
external stimuli to this day, just staring

00:45:23.520 --> 00:45:29.271
off into the distance with a haunted expression.
Almost like he’s still there in the hallway.

00:45:29.271 --> 00:45:34.260
The doctor wanted to conduct one more test
before he ordered SCP – 087 shut off from

00:45:34.260 --> 00:45:41.350
the world forever, and it was the most terrifying
of all. The final subject was D-9884, a 23-year-old

00:45:41.350 --> 00:45:46.090
woman with a history of depression and the
use of excessive force. The doctor had hoped

00:45:46.090 --> 00:45:51.480
that D-9884 would travel the deepest yet,
and so, he gave her the additional supplies

00:45:51.480 --> 00:45:57.860
of a backpack containing 3.75 liters of water,
15 nutrient bars, and 1 thermal blanket. As

00:45:57.860 --> 00:46:02.260
far as the Foundation was concerned, she was
in this for the long haul.

00:46:02.260 --> 00:46:06.240
But none of them had any idea quite how right
they were.

00:46:06.240 --> 00:46:12.520
When D-9884 entered SCP – 087, all the lights
from the previous expedition had disappeared.

00:46:12.520 --> 00:46:18.430
Still, she was ordered to go deeper. She heard
the crying of the mysterious child – if

00:46:18.430 --> 00:46:24.860
it was even a child at all – and again she
was ordered to go deeper. At the 496th landing,

00:46:24.860 --> 00:46:29.930
even as D-9884 seemed to slip into a state
of mortal terror, once again she was ordered

00:46:29.930 --> 00:46:36.070
to go even deeper. Every moment, he was hoping
to get a better look at the face of SCP – 087

00:46:36.070 --> 00:46:42.900
– 1. And when D-9884 finally broke, and
fled back upstairs, he did.

00:46:42.900 --> 00:46:48.770
The face appeared but this time it was mere
inches behind her, staring directly into the

00:46:48.770 --> 00:46:53.990
camera with its blank eyes – startling even
this veteran of the supernatural. The face

00:46:53.990 --> 00:46:58.700
appearing caused D-9884 to panic and flee,
but instead of going back up the stairs to

00:46:58.700 --> 00:47:04.950
safety, she went deeper down the staircase
in an attempt to escape it. Deeper, and deeper,

00:47:04.950 --> 00:47:11.180
and deeper, until her video feed cut out.
D-9884 was never seen again.

00:47:11.180 --> 00:47:15.930
In the aftermath of the tests, the SCP was
classified as Euclid – it may have been

00:47:15.930 --> 00:47:21.020
dangerous, but at least it was easy to contain.
The door to Hallway 3B was replaced with one

00:47:21.020 --> 00:47:25.990
made out of reinforced steel, with an electro-release
lock mechanism. It has been disguised to resemble

00:47:25.990 --> 00:47:30.290
a janitorial closet consistent with the rest
of the building. The lock won’t release

00:47:30.290 --> 00:47:34.530
unless a classified number of electrical volts
are applied, while the key is turned counter

00:47:34.530 --> 00:47:38.210
clockwise. And after a few inches of foam
insulation were applied to the inner side

00:47:38.210 --> 00:47:42.070
of the door, staff at the building never again
reported hearing strange noises.

00:47:42.070 --> 00:47:47.380
As for the fates of those lost within the
endless turning flights and platforms of SCP

00:47:47.380 --> 00:47:54.510
– 087, we may never know. But one can only
assume it isn’t pleasant.

00:47:54.510 --> 00:47:58.760
A tangled mass of yarn and ribbon sounds more
like what you’d find in the back room of

00:47:58.760 --> 00:48:03.530
a craft store or a forgotten closet than a
mysterious creature worthy of investigation.

00:48:03.530 --> 00:48:10.330
And yet that’s exactly what SCP-066 appeared
to be, or at least it did at first glance.

00:48:10.330 --> 00:48:15.470
But the SCP Foundation doesn’t contain and
study just anything, and there was - and still

00:48:15.470 --> 00:48:23.020
is - something incredibly strange just below
the surface of SCP-066, also known as “Eric’s

00:48:23.020 --> 00:48:25.950
Toy.”
At first, Eric’s Toy seemed to be completely

00:48:25.950 --> 00:48:30.670
harmless and even helpful, a knot of string
that produced strange but harmless items and

00:48:30.670 --> 00:48:37.240
effects. But, the Foundation soon discovered
a dark side to SCP-066. While it may be referred

00:48:37.240 --> 00:48:43.830
to as a toy, this is no mere plaything.
SCP-066 weighs only about one kilogram and

00:48:43.830 --> 00:48:47.940
appears to be a braided bunch of yarn and
ribbon. Though there is no apparent musical

00:48:47.940 --> 00:48:52.560
capability within the strands of yarn and
ribbon themselves, music can be produced by

00:48:52.560 --> 00:48:58.320
moving individual strands one at a time. When
it was first being studied, this SCP was composed

00:48:58.320 --> 00:49:03.180
of multicolored strings and ribbons, but it
has since undergone a transformation and now

00:49:03.180 --> 00:49:06.920
presents an appearance somewhat different
from its initial description.

00:49:06.920 --> 00:49:13.460
The strands of yarn and ribbon can be used
to play the notes of a diatonic scale - C-D-E-F-G-A-B

00:49:13.460 --> 00:49:19.660
- though the research has not been able to
determine just how SCP-066 produces music,

00:49:19.660 --> 00:49:25.710
or any sound at all. SCP-066 was thought to
be completely benign at first and was classified

00:49:25.710 --> 00:49:32.020
as Safe, but following an incident known as
Incident 066-2, its classification was adjusted

00:49:32.020 --> 00:49:38.350
to a subcategory of Euclid: Euclid-impetus.
Euclid is a classification given to SCPs that

00:49:38.350 --> 00:49:44.230
are more difficult to contain than those classified
as “Safe.” Impetus, in Latin, means “attack”

00:49:44.230 --> 00:49:50.680
and specifies that SCP-066 is not only Euclid
class, but on the more aggressive side. While

00:49:50.680 --> 00:49:56.550
066 is not always aggressive toward humans,
the events of Incident 066-2 proved that it

00:49:56.550 --> 00:49:59.850
is highly unpredictable, and should not be
provoked.

00:49:59.850 --> 00:50:05.460
Like many SCPs, it proved that underestimating
its capabilities can be a dangerous mistake.

00:50:05.460 --> 00:50:12.071
Before the incident, SCP-066 displayed only
charming, if unusual, behavior. Various researchers

00:50:12.071 --> 00:50:16.290
spent their time playing random assortments
of notes using its strings, curious about

00:50:16.290 --> 00:50:20.900
what would happen and determined to record
anything this unusual ball of string had to

00:50:20.900 --> 00:50:25.850
offer. They did not yet know that the creature
was capable of any hostility, and went about

00:50:25.850 --> 00:50:30.640
their work with a lighthearted, carefree spirit.
After playing an improvised six-note melody

00:50:30.640 --> 00:50:36.750
with the strands, a researcher was thrilled
to find that SCP-066 was capable of shapeshifting.

00:50:36.750 --> 00:50:41.400
Its appearance changed to resemble a small
calico kitten for seventeen minutes. The kitten

00:50:41.400 --> 00:50:45.350
was incredibly friendly, rubbing its head
against the researcher’s gloved hand and

00:50:45.350 --> 00:50:50.720
purring loudly. Ironically enough, the kitten
also spent time playing with a piece of string.

00:50:50.720 --> 00:50:56.200
After the seventeen minutes were up, the kitten
transformed back into SCP-066’s original

00:50:56.200 --> 00:51:00.810
form. A few days later, another researcher
played a different melody on the strands,

00:51:00.810 --> 00:51:05.460
and was surprised to find that, when they
stopped, the music continued on its own.

00:51:05.460 --> 00:51:09.860
The sound of an acoustic guitar kicked in,
accompanied by vocals, with no visible source

00:51:09.860 --> 00:51:15.310
for either sound. The SCP then played a four-minute
song with lyrics warning against the use of

00:51:15.310 --> 00:51:20.050
sharp objects without the supervision of a
parent, especially scissors. After the song

00:51:20.050 --> 00:51:23.230
ended, the SCP was silent for the rest of
the day.

00:51:23.230 --> 00:51:28.380
The following week, a research assistant used
the strands of SCP-066 to play the opening

00:51:28.380 --> 00:51:32.710
notes of “Happy Birthday,” and a chocolate
cupcake with a lit birthday candle appeared

00:51:32.710 --> 00:51:37.380
from within the braided strings. Against the
warnings of his peers, the assistant ate the

00:51:37.380 --> 00:51:41.990
cupcake. In response, the SCP played the rest
of “Happy Birthday,” and the assistant

00:51:41.990 --> 00:51:47.140
suffered no adverse effects from the cupcake.
All of this fun was brought to a swift end

00:51:47.140 --> 00:51:52.980
when one scientist suggested that a portion
of SCP-066’s yarn body be cut off and removed

00:51:52.980 --> 00:51:59.100
so that the specimen could be tested. On April
18, 2008, the event that would become known

00:51:59.100 --> 00:52:08.480
as Incident 066-2 took place. A young man
known only as D-066-4437, or D, was assigned

00:52:08.480 --> 00:52:14.250
to the task. Naturally, he was a member of
the highly disposable D Class personnel. But

00:52:14.250 --> 00:52:19.060
D was grateful for the opportunity, as most
experiments of a similar nature involved quite

00:52:19.060 --> 00:52:25.280
a bit more obvious risk. It was a simple enough
job: take a pair of scissors, snip off some

00:52:25.280 --> 00:52:30.360
yarn, and bring it back to the lab for further
study. It was hardly on the level of supervising

00:52:30.360 --> 00:52:37.660
173 or being 682’s latest chew toy.
He entered the containment room, where SCP-066

00:52:37.660 --> 00:52:41.021
was lying dormant and still, and approached
it with the scissors.

00:52:41.021 --> 00:52:44.860
He grabbed a small handful of string, and
started to cut. As soon as the scissors began

00:52:44.860 --> 00:52:49.980
to cut through the fabric, the SCP rolled
out of his grasp. It came to a stop one meter

00:52:49.980 --> 00:52:54.440
away, where it started to make a high-pitched
squeaking sound resembling the cry of a frightened

00:52:54.440 --> 00:52:59.570
rabbit. Unsure what to do and unprepared for
this scenario, D approached the entity again.

00:52:59.570 --> 00:53:04.460
He snagged another fistful of yarn and cut,
only for 066 to curl into a ball and roll

00:53:04.460 --> 00:53:08.910
away from him again, even faster this time.
Once it was safely on the other side of the

00:53:08.910 --> 00:53:11.830
room and away from the scissors it stopped
moving.

00:53:11.830 --> 00:53:16.800
Only this time it didn't squeak. Instead,
for the very first time since its containment,

00:53:16.800 --> 00:53:23.360
it spoke in a deep, uncannily human voice
and asked: “Are you Eric?” After recovering

00:53:23.360 --> 00:53:27.580
from his initial shock at hearing a voice
come out of a mass of string, D responded

00:53:27.580 --> 00:53:34.030
“No, I’m not.” This answer set something
off in SCP-066, and its form began to shift

00:53:34.030 --> 00:53:38.430
and change. The string wriggled around on
the floor, unbraiding and wrapping around

00:53:38.430 --> 00:53:44.350
itself into a mound. The colors, previously
a rainbow of shades, shifted until every strand

00:53:44.350 --> 00:53:48.140
was blood red.
Much to D’s horror, the transformation was

00:53:48.140 --> 00:53:53.170
not yet complete. Small bumps began to emerge
from the spaces between the strands of yarn,

00:53:53.170 --> 00:53:57.750
popping out all over the bright red mass.
If that wasn’t terrifying enough, suddenly

00:53:57.750 --> 00:54:04.220
all together as one, they blinked open, revealing
themselves to be over a dozen small eyes.

00:54:04.220 --> 00:54:10.730
Every single eye was focused at D, studying
him, staring him down. SCP-066 then began

00:54:10.730 --> 00:54:15.940
to produce loud, abrupt, dissonant notes like
someone banging on the keys of a piano. D

00:54:15.940 --> 00:54:20.010
had seen enough. He abandoned his task and
fled the containment room.

00:54:20.010 --> 00:54:25.050
After this failed attempt to extract a sample,
SCP-066’s behavior and its treatment of

00:54:25.050 --> 00:54:29.520
personnel who interacted with it began to
change dramatically. Before the incident,

00:54:29.520 --> 00:54:34.950
the SCP was largely dormant, only becoming
active if a melody was played using its strands.

00:54:34.950 --> 00:54:40.600
Following the incident, and its change of
form, 066 began to move on its own. Long strands

00:54:40.600 --> 00:54:45.120
of its yarn body would move like tentacles,
writhing and wriggling around at a high speed.

00:54:45.120 --> 00:54:50.240
It no longer needed human interaction in order
to produce sound, or to produce any other

00:54:50.240 --> 00:54:53.690
effects.
At the sight of any human, regardless of the

00:54:53.690 --> 00:54:58.930
human’s behavior, the SCP would begin to
react with sound and effect within six seconds.

00:54:58.930 --> 00:55:03.280
The first of these effects was noted by a
research assistant who entered the SCP’s

00:55:03.280 --> 00:55:08.260
containment facility a week after the incident
with D. As she approached 066 to take notes

00:55:08.260 --> 00:55:13.310
about its current state and its new ability
to move, a bee appeared out of nowhere. It

00:55:13.310 --> 00:55:15.950
stung the assistant and flew away before it
could be captured.

00:55:15.950 --> 00:55:21.210
Weeks later, a team of eleven personnel were
monitoring the SCP when it suddenly burst

00:55:21.210 --> 00:55:25.970
into a rendition of Beethoven’s second symphony.
It produced this music at a volume of over

00:55:25.970 --> 00:55:30.930
140 decibels, permanently deafening three
of the personnel, and causing permanent hearing

00:55:30.930 --> 00:55:36.040
damage in the other eight. It was theorized
that the SCP did this as an act of retribution

00:55:36.040 --> 00:55:40.770
for its perceived mistreatment. These personnel
refused to work with SCP-066 again.

00:55:40.770 --> 00:55:45.930
When a new team was assigned to monitor the
entity, everything seemed to be going well

00:55:45.930 --> 00:55:50.940
at first. It was moving around, flailing its
tentacles of yarn at nothing in particular,

00:55:50.940 --> 00:55:55.950
and staring at the personnel with its many
eyes, but otherwise was on its best behavior.

00:55:55.950 --> 00:56:01.270
Then, suddenly, every light in the room went
dark, and there was a complete loss of visibility.

00:56:01.270 --> 00:56:05.400
The lights were unable to be turned on for
five hours, and any attempt at an alternate

00:56:05.400 --> 00:56:10.520
light source such as a flashlight was unsuccessful.
It was as if the darkness in the room swallowed

00:56:10.520 --> 00:56:16.350
any and all light right up. It was similar
to the oppressive darkness within SCP – 087,

00:56:16.350 --> 00:56:20.540
or the unlimited black of SCP – 3001’s
shadow dimension.

00:56:20.540 --> 00:56:24.530
The personnel in the room later reported hearing
the sound of loud, labored breathing just

00:56:24.530 --> 00:56:28.730
behind their shoulders, though when they searched
for a source of the sound, they could find

00:56:28.730 --> 00:56:31.660
nothing.
There have been no recent anomalies reported,

00:56:31.660 --> 00:56:37.480
or any additional hostile behavior. Instead,
whenever it sees a new human, SCP-066 repeats

00:56:37.480 --> 00:56:43.120
the name “Eric” again and again in that
same deep voice. Who is Eric? No one at the

00:56:43.120 --> 00:56:47.930
facility knows, or, if they do, they have
not reported it to any official channels.

00:56:47.930 --> 00:56:52.990
It is possible that the SCP was once owned
by someone named Eric and perhaps, given the

00:56:52.990 --> 00:56:58.690
circumstances under which SCP-066 first said
the name, Eric attempted to cut the threads

00:56:58.690 --> 00:57:03.190
of the entity while it was in his care.
Unfortunately, there are no official records

00:57:03.190 --> 00:57:09.210
of how SCP-066 was discovered, or why it was
brought to the foundation in the first place.

00:57:09.210 --> 00:57:14.990
Its origins remain murky and as mysterious
as everything else about it. All that is known

00:57:14.990 --> 00:57:19.670
is that, whoever Eric is, SCP-066 is determined
to find him.

00:57:19.670 --> 00:57:23.770
Once the SCP’s class was changed from Safe
to Euclid, its containment procedures had

00:57:23.770 --> 00:57:28.770
to be adjusted. While it was previously kept
in a simple room, it is now contained in a

00:57:28.770 --> 00:57:34.180
tungsten carbide box at its site’s high-value
item storage facility. Once a month, the box

00:57:34.180 --> 00:57:39.680
is inspected for damage to its interior, due
to the SCP’s tendency to use its appendages

00:57:39.680 --> 00:57:46.450
to wear down the walls of the box over time.
If there is any damage, SCP-066 is to be moved

00:57:46.450 --> 00:57:52.010
to a new box using a robotic arm that performs
this transfer in less than three seconds.

00:57:52.010 --> 00:57:56.530
The Foundation has attempted to place recording
devices in the box with the entity in order

00:57:56.530 --> 00:58:01.410
to monitor its behavior when there are no
humans present. But the SCP destroys every

00:58:01.410 --> 00:58:06.260
recording device placed inside of its containment
box and any attempts to record its behavior

00:58:06.260 --> 00:58:11.140
when it is not being observed by humans have
been unsuccessful. Whatever it’s doing when

00:58:11.140 --> 00:58:14.580
there is no one around it wants to keep a
secret.

00:58:14.580 --> 00:58:19.520
On the surface, SCP-066 is one of the less
frightening finds contained within the walls

00:58:19.520 --> 00:58:25.420
of the SCP Foundation. It does not have claws,
or teeth, or the ability to cause mass deaths,

00:58:25.420 --> 00:58:31.480
but it has incredible, unpredictable capabilities,
and seems very capable of holding a grudge.

00:58:31.480 --> 00:58:36.090
There is so much that is unknown about it,
from its origins, to its form, to its ability

00:58:36.090 --> 00:58:40.720
to manifest matter from nothing, and there
is something deeply unsettling about this

00:58:40.720 --> 00:58:46.390
SCP’s unpredictable behavior and increased
hostility toward being observed. We do not

00:58:46.390 --> 00:58:51.610
know what it has done, and we do not know
what it will do next. All we can do is wonder.

00:58:51.610 --> 00:58:58.570
As we ponder the nature of SCP-066, it does
nothing but sit, staring with unblinking eyes,

00:58:58.570 --> 00:59:04.530
waiting for Eric to come back.
An SCP Foundation researcher sits at a table

00:59:04.530 --> 00:59:10.450
inside of a standard containment cell. These
are often dangerous places to be, especially

00:59:10.450 --> 00:59:15.391
when the SCP you’re supposed to be studying
is one that you can’t see. The researcher

00:59:15.391 --> 00:59:21.020
is taking notes, unsure of exactly what’s
going to happen next. He can hear the sounds

00:59:21.020 --> 00:59:27.740
of knives scraping behind, of flesh sizzling
and searing from high heat. He braces himself

00:59:27.740 --> 00:59:32.470
as a burst of heat hits the back of his head,
as if a fireball has erupted. Just then it

00:59:32.470 --> 00:59:35.980
happens - an object floats through the air
and settles in front of him on the table.

00:59:35.980 --> 00:59:41.780
It’s a plate of food, and it looks delicious.
It may surprise you to learn that there is

00:59:41.780 --> 00:59:48.150
no rule that the SCP Foundation must deal
exclusively with violent and vicious creatures.

00:59:48.150 --> 00:59:53.050
Not every SCP held in containment shares the
same malevolence and contempt for humanity

00:59:53.050 --> 01:00:02.080
as SCP-682, or the world-ending threat posed
by the likes of SCP-2317. Some - perhaps not

01:00:02.080 --> 01:00:07.340
many, but some - are benign and might even
seem outwardly friendly, but you’d still

01:00:07.340 --> 01:00:12.780
be taking a huge risk to assume that anything
contained by the SCP Foundation is completely

01:00:12.780 --> 01:00:18.330
harmless.
Such is the case with SCP-5031. As per the

01:00:18.330 --> 01:00:22.460
Foundation’s containment procedures, this
quasi-humanoid – meaning it appears to have

01:00:22.460 --> 01:00:27.650
some vaguely human features - is held in an
airtight cell that is regularly checked by

01:00:27.650 --> 01:00:34.380
Foundation personnel on a bi-weekly basis.
SCP-5031 has no need for regular nutrition

01:00:34.380 --> 01:00:41.900
or regular interactions from staff. The trick
with SCP-5031, is not being eaten by it, since

01:00:41.900 --> 01:00:47.940
though it doesn’t need food, it does still
hunt and consume anything it encounters - human

01:00:47.940 --> 01:00:52.370
or otherwise.
Avoiding being eaten is hard enough with creatures

01:00:52.370 --> 01:00:58.420
that can actually be seen, but like so many
other creatures the Foundation keeps contained,

01:00:58.420 --> 01:01:04.570
SCP-5031 has developed an almost-perfect defense
mechanism - which is that when observed, it

01:01:04.570 --> 01:01:10.180
will literally cease to exist. Some might
choose to refer to this as a ‘quantum lock’,

01:01:10.180 --> 01:01:15.800
however it is worth noting that traces left
by SCP-5031 still remain observable when the

01:01:15.800 --> 01:01:20.790
creature has temporarily disappeared. For
example, trails of blood and scratch marks

01:01:20.790 --> 01:01:26.860
left behind by SCP-5031 still exist when the
SCP itself does not.

01:01:26.860 --> 01:01:32.450
Naturally, this makes both avoiding the creature
and capturing it using cameras difficult.

01:01:32.450 --> 01:01:39.680
However, when SCP-5031’s existence ceases
it still casts a shadow. From this, researchers

01:01:39.680 --> 01:01:44.540
have been able to determine several of the
creature’s physical traits. Based on its

01:01:44.540 --> 01:01:49.820
silhouette, it has been deduced that SCP-5031
levitates about half a meter above ground

01:01:49.820 --> 01:01:55.370
level, it sports an abnormally small, neckless
head atop an elongated torso - approximately

01:01:55.370 --> 01:02:01.240
1.9 meters long - with three sets of spindly
lower arms that branch outwards.

01:02:01.240 --> 01:02:06.820
Using these arms and its loosely hanging body,
SCP-5031 will lower itself to hunt any human

01:02:06.820 --> 01:02:13.800
or animal that draws near to it and uses the
bladelike tail to cut up food.

01:02:13.800 --> 01:02:19.310
Perhaps the most interesting facet of SCP-5031
beyond its defensive capabilities and apparent

01:02:19.310 --> 01:02:25.210
physical attributes, are the series of nine
tests conducted by Senior Researcher Stanley

01:02:25.210 --> 01:02:29.940
Huxtable. Appalled by the conditions that
the creature was being kept in, Huxtable took

01:02:29.940 --> 01:02:36.560
over the role of HCL Supervisor for SCP-5031.
Having grown increasingly frustrated and empathetic

01:02:36.560 --> 01:02:41.470
towards the creature, listening to its screams
from inside its iron containment unit, Huxtable

01:02:41.470 --> 01:02:47.810
devised a series of tests to introduce SCP-5031
to various different stimuli as a way to better

01:02:47.810 --> 01:02:52.160
understand the creature and hopefully keep
it contained in a way that didn’t seem to

01:02:52.160 --> 01:02:56.680
cause so much suffering.
It's worth remembering that the SCP Foundation

01:02:56.680 --> 01:03:02.600
makes it its mission to be cold, not cruel,
in performing their duties to protect normality

01:03:02.600 --> 01:03:07.210
and many of the researchers and staff are
just as capable of having empathy for creatures

01:03:07.210 --> 01:03:12.590
as you might for a stray animal at a shelter.
The first of Huxtable’s tests involved installing

01:03:12.590 --> 01:03:17.820
speakers in SCP-5031’s cell, through which
a variety of different ambient and popular

01:03:17.820 --> 01:03:22.190
pieces of music were played to see if they
had any effect on reducing the creature’s

01:03:22.190 --> 01:03:27.630
stress. By judging SCP-5031’s stress levels
based on how much it screamed when compared

01:03:27.630 --> 01:03:33.550
to normal, Huxtable was able to determine
how to best to use music to calm the creature.

01:03:33.550 --> 01:03:38.440
SCP-5031 seemed to convey higher levels of
stress when listening to ‘Morning Forest’,

01:03:38.440 --> 01:03:43.680
‘Deep Grotto’ and ‘Seaside Paradise’
ambience, as well as the best of late 60s

01:03:43.680 --> 01:03:48.710
British rock band Jethro Tull.
However, the best of Mozart, Enya, KISS and

01:03:48.710 --> 01:03:54.180
Ben Folds produced dramatically different
results, decreasing SCP-5031’s apparent

01:03:54.180 --> 01:03:59.670
stress. Following this test, Senior Researcher
Huxtable compiled a playlist featuring SCP-5031’s

01:03:59.670 --> 01:04:06.610
favorite music. Over time, the stress-reducing
effects of music on SCP-5031 seemed to decrease,

01:04:06.610 --> 01:04:11.220
but keeping the playlist on shuffle seemed
to keep the creature consistently calmer than

01:04:11.220 --> 01:04:15.880
it had been previously.
The next test involved introducing inanimate

01:04:15.880 --> 01:04:22.010
objects into SCP-5031’s enclosure to monitor
its reactions and how its stress levels were

01:04:22.010 --> 01:04:27.580
affected. When a softball was thrown into
the enclosure, SCP-5031 immediately sliced

01:04:27.580 --> 01:04:32.820
the ball in two with its tail in one swift
motion. A similar result occurred when researchers

01:04:32.820 --> 01:04:38.540
threw the creature a basketball, which was
quickly punctured and sliced open by SCP-5031’s

01:04:38.540 --> 01:04:43.980
tail. Its stress levels first seemed to diminish
when the creature was offered a bowling ball,

01:04:43.980 --> 01:04:48.710
which it rolled around the enclosure and then
later knocked against a second bowling ball.

01:04:48.710 --> 01:04:54.870
However, when one of the balls chipped, rendering
it unable to roll properly, SCP-5031’s stress

01:04:54.870 --> 01:05:00.380
increased dramatically, until a replacement
was offered. Researcher Huxtable noted that

01:05:00.380 --> 01:05:05.950
SCP-5031 seemed to possess a similar level
of motor skills to an average human toddler,

01:05:05.950 --> 01:05:09.770
with similarly explosive emotional reactions
to match.

01:05:09.770 --> 01:05:15.290
Next, when given the choice between two food
sources at opposite ends of its enclosure,

01:05:15.290 --> 01:05:20.730
SCP-5031 seemed to gravitate towards higher-quality
food, most notably favoring cooked rotisserie

01:05:20.730 --> 01:05:26.410
chickens over animal carcasses. It even chose
this option over a live chicken, using its

01:05:26.410 --> 01:05:30.900
tail to cut its food into more manageable
bite-sized portions, rather than ripping its

01:05:30.900 --> 01:05:37.060
meat with its hands or teeth like many of
its fellow SCPs. Researcher Huxtable recorded

01:05:37.060 --> 01:05:42.450
these findings and highlighted that, even
though SCP-5031 didn’t need to eat in order

01:05:42.450 --> 01:05:47.970
to survive, providing the creature with food
of a better quality marginally reduced its

01:05:47.970 --> 01:05:51.620
stress.
Senior Researcher Huxtable next attempted

01:05:51.620 --> 01:05:58.390
to test SCP-5031’s coexistence with other
living subjects, each time making sure that

01:05:58.390 --> 01:06:04.400
the creature had been adequately fed to avoid
any unseemly incidents. First, a live chicken

01:06:04.400 --> 01:06:10.171
was introduced. SCP-5031 rolled its bowling
ball at high speed towards the chicken, increasing

01:06:10.171 --> 01:06:15.590
both its and the chicken’s stress levels,
and inadvertently killing the chicken in the

01:06:15.590 --> 01:06:21.160
process. When a second chicken was introduced,
SCP-5031 gently rolled a basketball towards

01:06:21.160 --> 01:06:25.300
it but ceased any further engagement after
the chicken squawked from being hit by the

01:06:25.300 --> 01:06:30.460
ball. Next to be introduced into the enclosure
was a blindfolded D Class staff member, who

01:06:30.460 --> 01:06:35.440
was instructed to sit down and roll the basketball
towards SCP-5031.

01:06:35.440 --> 01:06:39.960
After doing so for several minutes, the creature
began to approach the D class subject, who

01:06:39.960 --> 01:06:43.870
was instructed to remove their blindfold to
cease the creature’s existence and prevent

01:06:43.870 --> 01:06:49.171
any potentially deadly incidents. Finally,
Researcher Huxtable had another Class-D engage

01:06:49.171 --> 01:06:56.200
in a game of catch with SCP-5031 while facing
away from the creature. This test proceeded

01:06:56.200 --> 01:07:01.400
successfully, and Senior Researcher Huxtable
remarked how SCP-5031’s motor skills were

01:07:01.400 --> 01:07:06.380
improving. Albeit gradually, and with some
gentle encouragement, through Huxtable’s

01:07:06.380 --> 01:07:12.660
tests the creature was learning.
The next test, focused on teaching SCP-5031

01:07:12.660 --> 01:07:18.760
linguistic symbols, utilized LCD displays
and buttons connected to a food dispenser.

01:07:18.760 --> 01:07:23.080
One display showed an image of a rock, and
the other an image of a rotisserie chicken.

01:07:23.080 --> 01:07:28.270
After some brief probing, SCP-5031 was quickly
able to understand that pressing the button

01:07:28.270 --> 01:07:32.570
under the correct display would dispense a
rotisserie chicken for it to eat. The creature

01:07:32.570 --> 01:07:37.900
was later able to adapt when, the following
day, the screen displays and materials dispensed

01:07:37.900 --> 01:07:43.240
were swapped, and then later set to swap at
random intervals. When additional rock-dispensing

01:07:43.240 --> 01:07:47.760
stations were introduced, this time displaying
the word ‘rock’ as opposed to an image,

01:07:47.760 --> 01:07:52.770
SCP-5031 was able to determine which station
dispensed ‘chicken’ through a process

01:07:52.770 --> 01:07:56.830
of elimination.
Whenever the functions and displays were swapped,

01:07:56.830 --> 01:08:01.530
SCP-5031 would find whichever displayed the
word ‘chicken’ to receive its food. The

01:08:01.530 --> 01:08:07.200
final phase of this test presented SCP-5031
with a single station, displaying the word

01:08:07.200 --> 01:08:11.340
‘chicken’, but with a button that would
remain inactive unless the creature spelled

01:08:11.340 --> 01:08:16.839
out the same word with a collection of lettered
blocks it was provided with. After some initial

01:08:16.839 --> 01:08:23.319
confusion and frustration as to why the button
would not dispense food when pressed, SCP-5031

01:08:23.319 --> 01:08:28.539
was able to assemble the word correctly, not
only activating the button and dispensing

01:08:28.539 --> 01:08:34.329
food, but proving to Researcher Huxtable that
the creature was capable of learning language.

01:08:34.329 --> 01:08:39.139
Huxtable continued to test the creature, encouraging
it to spell words using lettered blocks as

01:08:39.139 --> 01:08:45.259
a method of communicating. By increasing SCP-5031’s
vocabulary and the amount of human interaction

01:08:45.259 --> 01:08:51.839
it received, Senior Researcher Huxtable observed
that SCP-5031 was gradually learning to sing

01:08:51.839 --> 01:08:57.469
- albeit nonverbally - as well as to juggle
with its six hands and was even communicating

01:08:57.469 --> 01:09:04.940
its own food preferences and dish pairings.
Later, another Class-D, D-52125, was introduced

01:09:04.940 --> 01:09:11.660
to SCP-5031’s enclosure to aid in further
testing. Through D-52125’s instructions,

01:09:11.660 --> 01:09:16.839
the creature quickly learned to draw using
crayons, and created artworks depicting itself,

01:09:16.839 --> 01:09:24.420
its newfound friend D-52125, Researcher Huxtable,
a cat and a rotisserie chicken.

01:09:24.420 --> 01:09:29.299
SCP-5031’s new creative side didn’t stop
there though, as the creature quickly learned

01:09:29.299 --> 01:09:36.279
to play Chopsticks in only two days once a
piano was introduced into the enclosure. SCP-5031

01:09:36.279 --> 01:09:41.109
even managed to start creating its own original,
admittedly crude, compositions.

01:09:41.109 --> 01:09:47.679
Next, a spice rack was placed inside the creature’s
cell and D-52125 demonstrated how to season

01:09:47.679 --> 01:09:54.239
meat. This proved to be SCP-5031’s new favorite
hobby, as it spent the next three days experimenting

01:09:54.239 --> 01:10:00.119
with different combinations of foods and spices,
using its letter blocks to request ‘more,

01:10:00.119 --> 01:10:05.460
more, more’ garlic powder. Interestingly,
the creature only created artwork or music

01:10:05.460 --> 01:10:11.740
when D-52125 was present, but seemed to thoroughly
enjoy its experimentation with food when left

01:10:11.740 --> 01:10:14.989
alone.
Following this development, Senior Researcher

01:10:14.989 --> 01:10:20.969
Huxtable devised a new test for SCP-5031.
Providing the creature with cooking utensils

01:10:20.969 --> 01:10:27.719
and using D-52125 to demonstrate, 5031 was
shown how to prepare a variety of different

01:10:27.719 --> 01:10:34.210
dishes, from hamburgers and tacos, to Mongolian
Beef, steak, clam chowder and profiteroles.

01:10:34.210 --> 01:10:40.630
In addition to a small peanut allergy, this
eighth test revealed SCP-5031 to be a phenomenal

01:10:40.630 --> 01:10:46.090
chef, possessing culinary skills far beyond
the average person. The creature quickly and

01:10:46.090 --> 01:10:52.040
enthusiastically embraced its newfound talents,
concocting its very own brand-new recipes,

01:10:52.040 --> 01:10:58.329
with D-52125 even volunteering to be the first
to taste test 5031’s dishes.

01:10:58.329 --> 01:11:05.420
It was shortly after this test that SCP-5031
spoke its very first word, and it should come

01:11:05.420 --> 01:11:11.090
as no surprise that the word was ‘salt’.
Naturally, Senior Researcher Huxtable was

01:11:11.090 --> 01:11:15.190
very proud of the progress the creature had
made with its development.

01:11:15.190 --> 01:11:19.329
The final test almost seemed to be what the
creature was born for. Over the course of

01:11:19.329 --> 01:11:24.930
two months, SCP-5031 was tasked with creating
a full three-course meal which would then

01:11:24.930 --> 01:11:31.250
be served to Foundation staff for Thanksgiving.
SCP-5031 not only rose to the task, but exceeded

01:11:31.250 --> 01:11:36.219
all of Researcher Huxtable’s expectations,
creating a meal that even Gordon Ramsey would

01:11:36.219 --> 01:11:41.250
be hard pressed to find fault with. The creature
created a first course consisting of sweet

01:11:41.250 --> 01:11:47.210
potato miso soup seasoned with turmeric. Next
came a beautiful duck confit, glazed luxuriously

01:11:47.210 --> 01:11:51.920
with apple cider and topped generously with
sweet cranberry compote, paired with a side

01:11:51.920 --> 01:11:56.780
of butternut squash gnocchi and served on
a bed of kale seasoned with truffle salt.

01:11:56.780 --> 01:12:02.010
The grand finale of the exquisite meal was
a spiced cassava pie for dessert, complemented

01:12:02.010 --> 01:12:09.239
with the finest French vanilla ice cream and
a maple-hazelnut syrup. And SCP-5031 didn’t

01:12:09.239 --> 01:12:13.909
stop there, the creature also debuted one
of its original musical compositions to compliment

01:12:13.909 --> 01:12:19.909
the decadent meal it had created. As the staff
enjoyed the food, SCP-5031 performed live

01:12:19.909 --> 01:12:26.190
from its enclosure the deeply moving Piano
Concerto for Six Hands, to an overwhelmingly

01:12:26.190 --> 01:12:32.260
positive response from not only Senior Researcher
Huxtable, but the entire Foundation staff.

01:12:32.260 --> 01:12:36.829
As a fitting end to the creature’s tale,
Huxtable reported that, during the Thanksgiving

01:12:36.829 --> 01:12:44.030
banquet it had created, SCP-5031’s stress
levels reduced entirely. New kinder containment

01:12:44.030 --> 01:12:50.360
measures that would keep 5031 safer but also
far more contented were submitted for approval.

01:12:50.360 --> 01:12:54.829
Perhaps some of you may find it refreshing
to learn that SCP-5031 isn’t simply just

01:12:54.829 --> 01:12:59.010
another malicious, malevolent monster that
the Foundation has to keep under lock and

01:12:59.010 --> 01:13:05.930
key for the safety of the world. Instead,
SCP-5031 is a gentle – if a little frightening

01:13:05.930 --> 01:13:11.190
at first creature - that just requires careful
and considered guidance instead of a cold

01:13:11.190 --> 01:13:16.860
iron cage and around-the-clock armed guards.
Through testing, Senior Researcher Stanley

01:13:16.860 --> 01:13:22.500
Huxtable and his fellow Foundation staff were
not only able to help the creature develop,

01:13:22.500 --> 01:13:28.140
but also found what makes it tick; and not
just for the purposes of containing it. Instead,

01:13:28.140 --> 01:13:33.889
it is hoped that SCP-5031’s creativity and
flair for culinary and musical masterpieces

01:13:33.889 --> 01:13:39.769
can continue to thrive and grow, under the
proud watch of Researcher Huxtable.

01:13:39.769 --> 01:13:46.269
Over fifty men and women, clad in red robes,
kneel before an unholy altar. They chant and

01:13:46.269 --> 01:13:53.630
mutter indecipherable words - words of cruelty
and madness… of obsession and sacrilege.

01:13:53.630 --> 01:14:00.909
Not long ago, these were regular people. Computer
technicians, teachers, plumbers, construction

01:14:00.909 --> 01:14:06.480
workers, accountants. This was before they
fell under the ungodly influence of a new

01:14:06.480 --> 01:14:12.260
ruler. The center of this makeshift place
of worship was once a normal school gymnasium,

01:14:12.260 --> 01:14:18.981
but it’s now the home of a huge statue.
A humanoid being, wreathed in tentacles. Its

01:14:18.981 --> 01:14:24.690
head is more like a squid or cuttlefish than
anything resembling an actual human face.

01:14:24.690 --> 01:14:29.650
While he’s known to the cultists as the
Tentacled God, the beast they worship is known

01:14:29.650 --> 01:14:36.250
to the SCP Foundation as SCP - 2662, and he
sits in the belly of one of their expansive

01:14:36.250 --> 01:14:42.610
containment facilities, locked away from the
world. But not for long, if his devoted followers

01:14:42.610 --> 01:14:49.060
have anything to say about it. This is their
god, all-powerful and unchanging, and when

01:14:49.060 --> 01:14:54.810
it comes to springing him from containment,
no tactic is too vile or underhanded to get

01:14:54.810 --> 01:14:56.260
the job done.

01:14:56.260 --> 01:15:01.869
Their mortal leader and high-priest, a man
in a purple robe calling himself Brother Marsh,

01:15:01.869 --> 01:15:07.280
walks among their crouched forms. He whispers
instructions for the great day of liberation

01:15:07.280 --> 01:15:12.910
that’s soon to come, providing everyone
plays their part. It’s a plan months in

01:15:12.910 --> 01:15:17.610
the making - and one that, if it goes off
without a hitch, could free their monstrous

01:15:17.610 --> 01:15:24.719
god into the world. They would strike at the
very heart of their enemy, The SCP Foundation,

01:15:24.719 --> 01:15:30.760
when they least expect it, and nothing shall
stand in their way. How could they lose when

01:15:30.760 --> 01:15:32.389
they have a god on their side?

01:15:32.389 --> 01:15:37.571
But why did all these normal people become
violent zealots for squid-faced deity? It

01:15:37.571 --> 01:15:43.719
all began with a dream. To those who experienced
these dreams, they felt more like prophecies,

01:15:43.719 --> 01:15:50.639
premonitions of the glorious horrors to come.
A red sky, billions dead and billions more

01:15:50.639 --> 01:15:57.239
enslaved. A dark silhouette on the horizon
- Their Tentacled God, holding dominion over

01:15:57.239 --> 01:16:02.760
all. At first, it just seemed like a strange
nightmare. The ones who experienced it woke

01:16:02.760 --> 01:16:08.969
up shaken and afraid, hoping to shake the
images from their mind. But they couldn’t.

01:16:08.969 --> 01:16:15.260
Every night, the nightmare would return. They’d
see the images - the red sky, the dead and

01:16:15.260 --> 01:16:21.170
enslaved, the Tentacled God. And after a while
it would come to them even when they weren’t

01:16:21.170 --> 01:16:25.929
asleep, eventually happening whenever they
closed their eyes. Little by little, this

01:16:25.929 --> 01:16:32.550
scene stopped looking so hideous… and started
to look glorious. They felt his presence in

01:16:32.550 --> 01:16:37.820
their minds, slowly pushing them towards their
inevitable future. They started to realize

01:16:37.820 --> 01:16:43.900
that they wanted him to rule over the universe,
and to experience the honor of serving him.

01:16:43.900 --> 01:16:48.900
Many of them abandoned their homes and families
- leaving their friends and loved ones left

01:16:48.900 --> 01:16:52.120
to worry that they’d gone insane.

01:16:52.120 --> 01:16:57.809
In their eyes, they were safer than they’d
ever been. They finally had purpose. They

01:16:57.809 --> 01:17:02.070
were working in service of something far greater
than themselves.

01:17:02.070 --> 01:17:07.389
The influence of the tentacled god drew them
closer to one another. They would meet in

01:17:07.389 --> 01:17:13.139
secret, exchanging information from the prophecies
their ruler sent them in their dreams. They

01:17:13.139 --> 01:17:17.639
worshipped together, building altars and idols
to congregate around. They performed dark

01:17:17.639 --> 01:17:23.270
blood rituals, involving human and animal
sacrifice. It was when Brother Marsh, The

01:17:23.270 --> 01:17:28.039
Anointed One, arrived to guide them towards
their true mission that things kicked into

01:17:28.039 --> 01:17:29.829
high gear.

01:17:29.829 --> 01:17:34.350
Just three months prior, Brother Marsh had
been an office drone working in data entry

01:17:34.350 --> 01:17:39.630
for a large insurance company, before the
Tentacled God invaded his thoughts with a

01:17:39.630 --> 01:17:47.770
simple message: “FREE ME, AND THE NEW WORLD
I CREATE SHALL BE YOUR PLAYGROUND.” Since

01:17:47.770 --> 01:17:52.690
then, he’d devoted himself completely to
the cause, quitting his job and maxing out

01:17:52.690 --> 01:17:58.809
his credit cards to help fund his new life’s
purpose - infiltrating the SCP Foundation,

01:17:58.809 --> 01:18:02.920
and releasing his inhuman ruler from its imprisonment.

01:18:02.920 --> 01:18:08.530
That was the single goal he united the cultists
under: Freedom for the Tentacled God. And

01:18:08.530 --> 01:18:14.130
at long last, they had all the pieces in place
to strike. They’d finally gathered the necessary

01:18:14.130 --> 01:18:19.980
intel to subvert the will of the most powerful
secret organization on earth. Even the strongest

01:18:19.980 --> 01:18:26.940
institution is made of people, and people
are weak. Unlike the almighty Tentacled God,

01:18:26.940 --> 01:18:29.139
people could be broken.

01:18:29.139 --> 01:18:35.409
The people in question were Kelly Thompson,
Sidney Levitt, Jordan Brosh, Dr. Juan Gutierrez,

01:18:35.409 --> 01:18:40.519
and Gillian Larson. Dr. Juan Gutierrez was
a researcher with Level 3 clearance on the

01:18:40.519 --> 01:18:45.929
site where the Tentacled God was being contained.
Sidney Levitt and Jordan Brosh were both Security

01:18:45.929 --> 01:18:50.429
Officers charged with verifying personnel
clearance on site. Kelly Thompson was a member

01:18:50.429 --> 01:18:55.910
of Site Administration with research authorization
powers, and Gillian Larson was a research

01:18:55.910 --> 01:19:01.409
assistant who often collaborated with Dr.
Gutierrez. These five were the key to getting

01:19:01.409 --> 01:19:07.510
access to SCP-2662 and bringing their plan
to fruition.

01:19:07.510 --> 01:19:12.030
Normally, personnel dossiers on people working
for the Foundation were highly confidential,

01:19:12.030 --> 01:19:17.320
but the Devotees of the Tentacled God had
their ways. They had a number of computer

01:19:17.320 --> 01:19:22.099
experts in their ranks more than capable of
hacking in and pulling some basic information

01:19:22.099 --> 01:19:27.139
off of Foundation servers without being detected.
For the other information they needed they

01:19:27.139 --> 01:19:32.300
turned to some good, old-fashioned torture,
which is often the most effective method when

01:19:32.300 --> 01:19:34.580
you need some quick results.

01:19:34.580 --> 01:19:39.760
Of course, while the cult’s grip on sanity
may have been a little tenuous, they weren’t

01:19:39.760 --> 01:19:44.519
stupid. While gathering their intel, they
also made sure to find out what exactly they

01:19:44.519 --> 01:19:51.659
were up against. SCP-2662 was being held in
a humanoid containment cell, and guarded by

01:19:51.659 --> 01:19:57.300
on-site Task Force TAU-9, better known as
the “Belligerent Bodyguards.” These aren’t

01:19:57.300 --> 01:20:02.530
lazy, donut-chomping mall cops - these are
a heavily trained, heavily armed fighting

01:20:02.530 --> 01:20:09.019
force. Though the cultists had one thing that
these Foundation soldiers didn’t: The element

01:20:09.019 --> 01:20:10.619
of surprise.

01:20:10.619 --> 01:20:14.849
For everything to go off perfectly, Brother
Marsh’s plans would have to be executed

01:20:14.849 --> 01:20:20.199
within a single day, and they were already
on the clock. TAU-9 had been charged with

01:20:20.199 --> 01:20:26.639
tracking down any new SCP - 2662 cults and
dismantling them, and Brother Marsh knew that

01:20:26.639 --> 01:20:31.960
it was only a matter of time before the Foundation
tracked them down and did the same to them.

01:20:31.960 --> 01:20:37.369
If they wanted any chance of freeing the Tentacled
God, then they needed to strike quickly and

01:20:37.369 --> 01:20:39.550
with overwhelming force.

01:20:39.550 --> 01:20:46.409
The SCP-2662 worshippers were able to secure
the addresses of the five key Foundation personnel,

01:20:46.409 --> 01:20:52.600
and station members outside each of them - including
one who could realistically imitate each.

01:20:52.600 --> 01:20:57.999
They waited for night to fall, and broke into
each of their homes as they slept. What followed

01:20:57.999 --> 01:21:03.260
was a sequence of ruthless and efficient murders
done in the cause of freeing their god.

01:21:03.260 --> 01:21:08.110
Dr. Gutierrez was shot in the head while he
slept. Sidney Levitt and Jordan Brosh were

01:21:08.110 --> 01:21:13.170
both stabbed to death before either even realized
what was happening. Thompson, who’d gotten

01:21:13.170 --> 01:21:18.739
up to use the bathroom, went down in a hail
of machine gun fire. Gillian Larson had seen

01:21:18.739 --> 01:21:22.679
that masked figures were breaking into her
home and attempted to flee, but was caught

01:21:22.679 --> 01:21:27.900
and beaten to death by cultists in her hallway.
It was a strange irony that people whose day

01:21:27.900 --> 01:21:32.949
jobs entailed working with some of the most
dangerous and nightmarish anomalies imaginable

01:21:32.949 --> 01:21:38.130
were murdered in their homes by nothing more
than regular humans.

01:21:38.130 --> 01:21:43.889
So far, Brother Marsh’s plan had gone perfectly,
with all five key personnel murdered within

01:21:43.889 --> 01:21:49.550
a two minute period. Next, the selected doppelgängers
stole clothes from their victims’ closets

01:21:49.550 --> 01:21:54.810
and were handed the correct forged documentation.
The next morning, each replacement began their

01:21:54.810 --> 01:21:59.889
journeys to the site where the Tentacled God
was being contained, while the rest of the

01:21:59.889 --> 01:22:04.469
cult armed themselves in preparation for their
own part in the plan.

01:22:04.469 --> 01:22:09.119
Nobody at the Foundation seemed to notice
anything amiss when the five arrived on site.

01:22:09.119 --> 01:22:13.250
When you work for the SCP Foundation, more
mental energy is devoted to following the

01:22:13.250 --> 01:22:18.670
rules that keep you alive than to memorizing
the faces of all your co-workers and each

01:22:18.670 --> 01:22:25.900
one slipped neatly into position, disappearing
into the familiarity of office life. But,

01:22:25.900 --> 01:22:30.320
infiltrating the site was one thing, getting
past the Belligerent Bodyguards and into the

01:22:30.320 --> 01:22:33.889
cell of the Tentacled God would be another
thing entirely.

01:22:33.889 --> 01:22:39.000
That’s where the rest of the cult would
come into play. Heavily armed with whatever

01:22:39.000 --> 01:22:43.659
firearms they could get their hands on, the
rest of the Devotees of the Tentacled God

01:22:43.659 --> 01:22:49.929
- Brother Marsh included - would attack the
containment site head-on. In the ensuing chaos,

01:22:49.929 --> 01:22:54.550
the five cultists who had already infiltrated
the site could take advantage of the distraction,

01:22:54.550 --> 01:22:59.301
and break into the containment chamber. It
was perfect. They’d launch their attack

01:22:59.301 --> 01:23:02.280
from the outside… and from within.

01:23:02.280 --> 01:23:07.800
When Brother Marsh declared that the time
was right, the assault began. A legion of

01:23:07.800 --> 01:23:11.889
gun-wielding cultists seemed to spring out
of nowhere and started shooting up the warehouse

01:23:11.889 --> 01:23:16.409
that was a front for the containment site.
The site quickly mobilized guards and task

01:23:16.409 --> 01:23:21.580
force members to take on the sudden threat,
and just as Brother Marsh had anticipated,

01:23:21.580 --> 01:23:26.350
the Site Director called on the majority of
TAU-9 to help repel the violent cultists from

01:23:26.350 --> 01:23:27.440
their perimeter.

01:23:27.440 --> 01:23:34.050
TAU-9 obeyed, leaving three task force members
behind to guard SCP - 2662’s containment

01:23:34.050 --> 01:23:38.870
chamber. They expected to be guarding the
cell from rampaging religious zealots seeking

01:23:38.870 --> 01:23:44.289
an audience with their god. What they didn’t
expect was a group of five Foundation employees

01:23:44.289 --> 01:23:50.349
walking right up to them and opening fire,
killing two TAU-9 members and taking the third

01:23:50.349 --> 01:23:55.849
as a hostage. While the war was being waged
outside, the infiltrators had found the Tentacled

01:23:55.849 --> 01:23:59.920
God’s containment cell in the low-risk humanoid
ward.

01:23:59.920 --> 01:24:04.380
Their hostage insisted that using him wouldn’t
give them any leverage - the rest of his team

01:24:04.380 --> 01:24:09.590
would neutralize the whole group, him included,
if that’s what it took to stop them. The

01:24:09.590 --> 01:24:14.659
infiltrators explained that using him as leverage
was never their intention - he wasn’t a

01:24:14.659 --> 01:24:18.790
hostage at all. He was a sacrifice.

01:24:18.790 --> 01:24:23.520
The cultists of the Tentacled God detonated
explosives, creating a hole in the wall and

01:24:23.520 --> 01:24:28.570
finally giving them access to their deity.
They climbed through and gazed upon him in

01:24:28.570 --> 01:24:37.059
awe. There stood SCP-2662, twice as tall as
a regular man, with ten huge tentacles emerging

01:24:37.059 --> 01:24:41.389
from its back. In their months of envisioning
this creature, they’d pictured it sitting

01:24:41.389 --> 01:24:47.219
on a throne made of thousands of human bones,
ready to dictate its commands to the obedient

01:24:47.219 --> 01:24:52.949
liberators. What they certainly didn’t expect
was to see the Tentacled God hunched over

01:24:52.949 --> 01:24:57.869
a computer screen.
Still, gods work in mysterious ways, so they

01:24:57.869 --> 01:25:02.810
stuck to the plan and began chanting. They
pulled out a sacrificial dagger, and began

01:25:02.810 --> 01:25:09.090
sacrificing their captured TAU-9 member. It
was at this point that SCP - 2662 turned and

01:25:09.090 --> 01:25:14.310
saw what they were doing with a look of pure
horror. He rose up from his computer, his

01:25:14.310 --> 01:25:19.020
headphones getting caught as he did so. He
told them to go away, that he didn’t want

01:25:19.020 --> 01:25:23.260
them here, and that them murdering people
in his bedroom like this was inconsiderate

01:25:23.260 --> 01:25:28.480
and disgusting. The cultists became even more
confused - why wasn’t their god accepting

01:25:28.480 --> 01:25:33.770
their offerings? What were they doing wrong?
They tried more chanting, and painting arcane

01:25:33.770 --> 01:25:39.030
symbols on the floor in blood, but this just
seemed to make the creature angrier. He told

01:25:39.030 --> 01:25:44.050
them, in a tone more fitting for a teenage
boy than a Lovecraftian God, to just leave

01:25:44.050 --> 01:25:51.320
him alone so he could play his video games.
This was seriously not cool! The cultists

01:25:51.320 --> 01:25:55.900
were baffled. They told the Tentacled God
they were there to free him. He replied that

01:25:55.900 --> 01:26:01.110
he didn’t need saving. That crazy stalkers
like them were why he turned himself in to

01:26:01.110 --> 01:26:03.909
the Foundation in the first place!

01:26:03.909 --> 01:26:07.480
Before the cultist infiltrators could get
another word in, the remaining members of

01:26:07.480 --> 01:26:12.730
TAU-9 stormed into the containment cell and
gunned them down with surgical precision.

01:26:12.730 --> 01:26:17.340
The war outside was already over - Brother
Marsh and the rest of the cultists were all

01:26:17.340 --> 01:26:18.739
killed in the firefight.

01:26:18.739 --> 01:26:25.099
TAU-9 didn’t look the least bit surprised
upon entering 2662’s cell, this was a common

01:26:25.099 --> 01:26:30.079
occurrence unfortunately. They had to deal
with an attempted cult invasion every few

01:26:30.079 --> 01:26:37.170
months, because SCP-2662’s main anomalous
ability is inspiring violent cults who relentlessly

01:26:37.170 --> 01:26:41.249
track down and worship it with arcane and
bloodthirsty rituals.

01:26:41.249 --> 01:26:48.190
The problem is, 2662 doesn’t do this consciously,
and definitely doesn’t like the results.

01:26:48.190 --> 01:26:53.119
That’s why he’s under the voluntary care
of the SCP Foundation who keeps him amused

01:26:53.119 --> 01:26:57.730
with video games and reading material while
fending off the deranged cults who try to

01:26:57.730 --> 01:27:00.070
invade and abduct him.

01:27:00.070 --> 01:27:04.429
Following the termination of The Devotees
of the Tentacled God, just one of many cults

01:27:04.429 --> 01:27:09.849
who’d broken into 2662’s containment cell,
the remaining TAU-9 members apologized to

01:27:09.849 --> 01:27:14.789
the tentacled creature for the disturbance,
allowing him to return to his gaming. They

01:27:14.789 --> 01:27:18.749
assured him that it’d probably be at least
a few more months before something like this

01:27:18.749 --> 01:27:20.670
happened again.

01:27:20.670 --> 01:27:26.350
SCP-2662’s cell was repaired, and the Foundation
returned to its task of seeking out would-be

01:27:26.350 --> 01:27:32.059
cultist emancipators, because for the SCP
Foundation, it’s not always about the anomaly

01:27:32.059 --> 01:27:36.010
that’s being kept in containment, but what’s
being kept out.

01:27:36.010 --> 01:27:37.960
“This is impossible!”

01:27:37.960 --> 01:27:43.239
The SCP site director wasn’t normally a
calm or cheerful man, but the researcher had

01:27:43.239 --> 01:27:47.219
rarely seen him as angry as he was right now.

01:27:47.219 --> 01:27:51.869
His face turned a deep beet red as he scanned
the documents on his desk before he asked

01:27:51.869 --> 01:27:57.489
how months of valuable research on this subject
had suddenly gone blank, the data was completely

01:27:57.489 --> 01:27:58.489
gone.

01:27:58.489 --> 01:28:03.739
The researcher gulped nervously, hoping a
demotion wasn’t in his future, and nodded.

01:28:03.739 --> 01:28:08.219
How could this be possible. This was an experienced
researcher who should have been taking all

01:28:08.219 --> 01:28:13.030
of the necessary precautions. Could the being
they were studying somehow have erased all

01:28:13.030 --> 01:28:14.580
these documents himself?

01:28:14.580 --> 01:28:19.630
That’s just what the researcher had been
trying to find out for months, with hours

01:28:19.630 --> 01:28:23.130
and hours spent trying to learn the extent
of its abilities.

01:28:23.130 --> 01:28:29.159
“Well? Where are they?” the site director
asked. “I want everything you have!”

01:28:29.159 --> 01:28:33.400
The researcher dropped a print-out of their
research on the mysterious subject’s abilities

01:28:33.400 --> 01:28:38.079
on the director’s desk. Every relevant line
read “Data Lost”.

01:28:38.079 --> 01:28:43.489
The director let out a deep sigh. He wanted
to hear everything the researcher knew, well

01:28:43.489 --> 01:28:47.489
everything he could remember at least, from
the beginning.

01:28:47.489 --> 01:28:53.780
The researcher sat town and began to relay
everything he could about SCP-343, which some

01:28:53.780 --> 01:28:58.800
of the other researchers had started to refer
to by the nickname… God.

01:28:58.800 --> 01:29:04.739
SCP-343 was first sighted in Prague, just
an unassuming older man wandering the streets.

01:29:04.739 --> 01:29:09.590
He seemed completely normal to everyone who
passed him by - until he decided he was tired

01:29:09.590 --> 01:29:14.800
of staying on the ground. An SCP agent stationed
in the area noticed the old man disappear

01:29:14.800 --> 01:29:20.199
from the streets as if he was blinking out
of existence - only to appear on a rooftop

01:29:20.199 --> 01:29:24.889
nearby. The local SCP teams were marshalled,
and they had soon tracked down what seemed

01:29:24.889 --> 01:29:30.900
to be a very powerful specimen.
But SCP-343 didn’t seem concerned. He reacted

01:29:30.900 --> 01:29:35.489
calmly when detained by the foundation and
went with them willingly. He was detained

01:29:35.489 --> 01:29:40.270
in a standard holding cell for interrogation
and examination, but he seemed completely

01:29:40.270 --> 01:29:46.610
at ease with his sudden confinement. It would
soon become clear that this ordinary old man

01:29:46.610 --> 01:29:47.940
was anything but.

01:29:47.940 --> 01:29:52.449
Doctors Beck and Ndlovu were brought in to
consult on the SCP’s classification, and

01:29:52.449 --> 01:29:57.659
that’s when the first anomalies began. Their
assessments matched initially, but when it

01:29:57.659 --> 01:30:02.579
came time to describe him physically, things
took a strange turn.

01:30:02.579 --> 01:30:07.869
Older male, seemingly non-descript and with
no unusual physical features. Caucasian in

01:30:07.869 --> 01:30:09.019
appearance.

01:30:09.019 --> 01:30:13.710
Doctor Ndlovu was confused by what Doctor
Beck was describing in his report. This man

01:30:13.710 --> 01:30:17.230
was clearly black.
The two doctors quarrelled, unable to square

01:30:17.230 --> 01:30:21.869
their differing perceptions. They decided
to bring in a third impartial view to settle

01:30:21.869 --> 01:30:24.260
it - their fellow researcher, Dr. Wan.

01:30:24.260 --> 01:30:28.739
She didn’t take long before coming back
with her assessment. Older male, seemingly

01:30:28.739 --> 01:30:34.800
non-descript and with no unusual physical
features. Asian in appearance, possibly Chinese.

01:30:34.800 --> 01:30:40.639
Whatever SCP-343 was, he seemed to be perceived
by each staff member as close in appearance

01:30:40.639 --> 01:30:45.820
to their own race. But that was only the start
of the anomalies surrounding the old man in

01:30:45.820 --> 01:30:46.820
the holding cell.

01:30:46.820 --> 01:30:52.059
Dr. Beck started making regular visits to
the mysterious man, and in their first interview,

01:30:52.059 --> 01:30:58.340
he asked the old man who he was and how he
came by his abilities. The old man had a simple

01:30:58.340 --> 01:30:59.340
response.

01:30:59.340 --> 01:31:00.960
“I created this universe.”

01:31:00.960 --> 01:31:06.949
Dr. Beck stifled a laugh and decided to indulge
the old man’s delusion. It was a fascinating

01:31:06.949 --> 01:31:09.110
claim, but could he prove it?

01:31:09.110 --> 01:31:14.440
Without another word, SCP-343 got up from
his chair, laughed, and turned around and

01:31:14.440 --> 01:31:19.040
walked through the solid wall in the holding
cell and disappeared. Dr. Beck was about to

01:31:19.040 --> 01:31:23.880
hit the panic button and marshall the facility’s
security to find him when the strange man

01:31:23.880 --> 01:31:28.390
reappeared, walking through the solid wall.
The only thing that was different? He was

01:31:28.390 --> 01:31:31.830
holding a hamburger, which he sat down and
enjoyed.

01:31:31.830 --> 01:31:36.989
The facility quickly went on lockdown and
a full investigation was done into how SCP-343

01:31:36.989 --> 01:31:43.460
breached containment. But there was no evidence
of any security breach, no failures in containment,

01:31:43.460 --> 01:31:49.409
and no evidence of any other cells failing.
SCP-343 hadn’t broken through the security

01:31:49.409 --> 01:31:54.380
- he had just ignored it, as if it wasn’t
there at all. When questioned about how he

01:31:54.380 --> 01:31:59.829
had gone on his hamburger run, he simply repeated
his belief that he was God - in between bites

01:31:59.829 --> 01:32:01.539
of his fast food treat.

01:32:01.539 --> 01:32:06.070
This would be far from the only time strange
things happened around SCP-343.

01:32:06.070 --> 01:32:11.780
SCP containment cells are as secure as they
need to be, but even the least-strict containment

01:32:11.780 --> 01:32:16.590
isn’t known for its decor. Which is why
Dr. Beck was in for a surprise the next time

01:32:16.590 --> 01:32:23.070
he paid a visit to SCP-343. The bare-bones
cell now looked like a comfortable home, decorated

01:32:23.070 --> 01:32:29.090
in Old English fashions. The scientists assumed
that SCP-343 had been making many more trips

01:32:29.090 --> 01:32:34.090
out of his cell to get accessories to feel
more at home - but that didn’t explain all

01:32:34.090 --> 01:32:37.699
the changes to the cell.
No one could explain how he had installed

01:32:37.699 --> 01:32:41.960
a roaring fireplace in the containment cell
- and everyone who entered could swear the

01:32:41.960 --> 01:32:47.889
cell looked many times bigger than any other
cell in the facility. SCP-343 wasn’t just

01:32:47.889 --> 01:32:53.349
breaking containment - he now seemed to be
breaking the laws of physics in the facility.

01:32:53.349 --> 01:32:59.120
The rules of the SCP containment facility
didn’t seem to be a concern to SCP-343,

01:32:59.120 --> 01:33:04.110
but there was one thing he didn’t seem to
want to do - escape. After every sudden exit,

01:33:04.110 --> 01:33:09.090
he would always return to his personal cell
and treat it as his home. When interviewed

01:33:09.090 --> 01:33:14.489
by staff members, he was polite but vague,
and everyone seemed to enjoy talking to him.

01:33:14.489 --> 01:33:20.030
It was decided to keep him on site, not attempt
to increase his security, but restrict access

01:33:20.030 --> 01:33:24.960
and keep his room guarded at all times to
ensure only researchers with Level 3 access

01:33:24.960 --> 01:33:27.630
and above were allowed to meet with him.

01:33:27.630 --> 01:33:30.780
But God works in mysterious ways.

01:33:30.780 --> 01:33:36.640
Minimal Security Site 17 was one of the less-restrictive
SCP containment sites, hosting anomalies that

01:33:36.640 --> 01:33:41.969
could be safely contained and weren’t likely
to mount violent escapes. But as in every

01:33:41.969 --> 01:33:47.760
SCP facility, security was still taken seriously
and only those with proper clearance could

01:33:47.760 --> 01:33:54.499
interact with the subjects. So why did SCP-343
seem impossible to guard? While only Level

01:33:54.499 --> 01:33:58.730
3 clearance and above were allowed in, the
guards assigned to protect the entrance all

01:33:58.730 --> 01:34:01.330
seemed to fall down on the job.

01:34:01.330 --> 01:34:06.290
Security Officer James, who was supposed to
be keeping people out of SCP-343’s cell,

01:34:06.290 --> 01:34:11.461
had instead let in multiple visitors in addition
to dropping in several times himself. When

01:34:11.461 --> 01:34:16.619
questioned on why he had gone against orders
and done so, he simply replied that 343 seemed

01:34:16.619 --> 01:34:21.579
lonely and was so happy every time he got
company that it just seemed like the right

01:34:21.579 --> 01:34:22.639
thing to do.

01:34:22.639 --> 01:34:27.030
The security guard was reassigned and new
ones were brought in - but history repeated

01:34:27.030 --> 01:34:33.210
itself. Guards were given stricter instructions
to minimize exposure - but SCP-343’s presence

01:34:33.210 --> 01:34:38.650
always seemed to influence them anyway. His
containment cell was a revolving door, with

01:34:38.650 --> 01:34:42.690
staff members at the facility entering regularly
for friendly conversations.

01:34:42.690 --> 01:34:49.790
Dr. Beck decided it was time to take matters
into his own hands. He would meet with SCP-343

01:34:49.790 --> 01:34:54.789
one-on-one and express how dangerous these
security breaches were. He would try to convince

01:34:54.789 --> 01:34:59.139
the mysterious being that he needed to stop
influencing the minds of the guards watching

01:34:59.139 --> 01:35:03.510
him, or the facility would have to look into
new measures to contain him.

01:35:03.510 --> 01:35:09.540
Dr. Beck entered the containment cell and
had a long conversation with SCP-343, and

01:35:09.540 --> 01:35:14.230
when he emerged...he had a big smile on his
face, like he had just finished a reunion

01:35:14.230 --> 01:35:19.139
with an old friend. He gave the current guard
a friendly clap on the back, and told him

01:35:19.139 --> 01:35:23.630
not to worry so much about security. After
all, nothing bad was going to happen from

01:35:23.630 --> 01:35:29.510
letting people at the facility visit SCP-343,
right? He wasn’t dangerous in any way. He

01:35:29.510 --> 01:35:33.999
also said that security should bring him anything
he requests so he would feel less need to

01:35:33.999 --> 01:35:35.309
leave his cell.

01:35:35.309 --> 01:35:41.030
Minimal Security Site 17 soon became a model
SCP facility, with morale being the highest

01:35:41.030 --> 01:35:47.389
of any site - with most giving the credit
to the presence of SCP-343. Employees generally

01:35:47.389 --> 01:35:51.570
make daily visits to his chambers, and he
seems to have an encyclopedic knowledge of

01:35:51.570 --> 01:35:56.691
anything they want to talk about - including
things he should have no way of knowing. Guards

01:35:56.691 --> 01:36:01.530
no longer quit their posts or break protocol,
as their only real duty is to keep track of

01:36:01.530 --> 01:36:07.940
who meets with SCP-343 so they can be interviewed
and debriefed after. Everyone’s conversation

01:36:07.940 --> 01:36:12.190
is different, but they all report being in
a better mood after leaving than when they

01:36:12.190 --> 01:36:13.190
came in.

01:36:13.190 --> 01:36:19.690
No further information is available on SCP-343’s
origins, the full extent of his powers, or

01:36:19.690 --> 01:36:24.249
whether he is telling the truth about being
the God who created the universe.

01:36:24.249 --> 01:36:28.219
The site director rubbed his temples after
hearing the researcher’s explanation. “So

01:36:28.219 --> 01:36:32.860
what you’re telling me is that we have an
uncontained, highly powerful SCP that has

01:36:32.860 --> 01:36:37.300
not only been breaking containment whenever
it wants, but has managed to destroy all the

01:36:37.300 --> 01:36:39.690
files regarding the research on it?”

01:36:39.690 --> 01:36:45.059
The researcher’s answer was yes. However,
the situation at Site 17 seemed to be stable,

01:36:45.059 --> 01:36:50.559
and they had come up with a plan that should
help to maximize the positive effect SCP-343

01:36:50.559 --> 01:36:55.249
has on the facility. They were even hypothesizing
that staff from other sites and even certain

01:36:55.249 --> 01:36:59.100
anomalies could be pacified by 343’s presence.

01:36:59.100 --> 01:37:02.840
The site director wasn’t impressed though.
He wanted the researcher to go back to the

01:37:02.840 --> 01:37:07.610
drawing board and redo the research. After
all, if all the files were blank, how could

01:37:07.610 --> 01:37:12.070
they ever learn how to properly contain it?
That’s what the C in SCP stood for after

01:37:12.070 --> 01:37:13.780
all - containment.

01:37:13.780 --> 01:37:17.520
The researcher finally had to stand up to
the director though, and told them that it

01:37:17.520 --> 01:37:22.869
wasn’t a good idea. That they had already
tried everything to contain SCP-343, but that

01:37:22.869 --> 01:37:26.860
it wasn’t that he broke containment, it
was as if he didn’t even acknowledge that

01:37:26.860 --> 01:37:32.389
an attempt had been made to contain him. He
was omnipotent, aware of things he shouldn’t,

01:37:32.389 --> 01:37:37.660
and able to do things that broke the laws
of physics without breaking a sweat. There

01:37:37.660 --> 01:37:42.570
was no evidence that this was God, the creator
of the universe as he claimed to be, but there

01:37:42.570 --> 01:37:46.969
also wasn’t any evidence yet to conclusively
prove he wasn’t.

01:37:46.969 --> 01:37:51.550
The researcher’s best guess was that this
was a powerful reality bender whose abilities

01:37:51.550 --> 01:37:56.289
knew no limits, and that the only reason he
was staying in the facility was because he

01:37:56.289 --> 01:38:02.300
wanted to, and doing anything to change that
might cause him to change his benevolent ways.

01:38:02.300 --> 01:38:07.719
The director sighed. As much as he hated to
admit it, his researcher was making good points.

01:38:07.719 --> 01:38:12.889
He wanted to meet SCP-343 personally. But
did he need to know anything first?

01:38:12.889 --> 01:38:18.210
“Well, sir…” the researcher replied,
“he likes hamburgers. But beyond that, he’ll

01:38:18.210 --> 01:38:22.090
take care of the rest. He’s right where
we left him, in his home - waiting for his

01:38:22.090 --> 01:38:25.360
next guest.”
The esteemed doctor Thomas Morstead entered

01:38:25.360 --> 01:38:26.960
the cell of the anomaly.

01:38:26.960 --> 01:38:32.420
He’d been warned and even chastised by his
colleagues, but who in the foundation could

01:38:32.420 --> 01:38:33.460
tell him what to do?

01:38:33.460 --> 01:38:40.219
He was the best at what he did, maybe the
greatest in the whole history of the foundation.

01:38:40.219 --> 01:38:46.920
As he entered the room, SCP-049 bid him welcome,
cordial as always, so polite in fact that

01:38:46.920 --> 01:38:50.139
you’d never guess you were talking to a
killer.

01:38:50.139 --> 01:38:54.130
Doctor Morstead knew the truth of what he
was dealing with, but he also believed he

01:38:54.130 --> 01:38:59.360
could get through to 049, calm him, exorcise
the devil from him.

01:38:59.360 --> 01:39:05.139
It was the meeting of two great minds, one
of them human, one of them part-human, part...

01:39:05.139 --> 01:39:07.469
something that has never been clear.

01:39:07.469 --> 01:39:12.909
It was to be a battle of wits, and like so
many great battles, this one would turn into

01:39:12.909 --> 01:39:14.539
a massacre.

01:39:14.539 --> 01:39:17.559
Before we get to that fateful meeting, there
are some things you should know about the

01:39:17.559 --> 01:39:19.019
anomaly known as SCP-049.

01:39:19.019 --> 01:39:24.710
If you saw him in the street the first thing
you’d think of is “plague”, because

01:39:24.710 --> 01:39:30.479
049 always looked the same - a man dressed
in black robes with a plague doctor’s mask.

01:39:30.479 --> 01:39:32.690
But this wasn’t a costume that could be
taken off.

01:39:32.690 --> 01:39:35.829
In fact it wasn’t a costume at all.

01:39:35.829 --> 01:39:41.999
It was him… the robes had grown out of him
like an exoskeleton, that horrible mask with

01:39:41.999 --> 01:39:48.050
the pointed nose wasn’t covering his face,
it was his face, a kind of shell that had

01:39:48.050 --> 01:39:49.900
seemingly sprouted from bone.

01:39:49.900 --> 01:39:51.869
The first reports came during World War Two.

01:39:51.869 --> 01:39:57.570
In a picturesque town in the south of France
called Montauban, people had begun going missing.

01:39:57.570 --> 01:40:01.059
Children disappeared from their beds in the
middle of the night and weren’t seen again;

01:40:01.059 --> 01:40:04.139
adults went to the market and never returned.

01:40:04.139 --> 01:40:08.940
Local authorities searched high and low; they
scoured nearby woods and dragged the rivers,

01:40:08.940 --> 01:40:10.519
but nothing was found.

01:40:10.519 --> 01:40:14.289
Because what was happening wasn’t criminal,
there was no clue they could stumble upon

01:40:14.289 --> 01:40:16.369
or eye witness who would break the case.

01:40:16.369 --> 01:40:21.090
No, this was something else, something that
the townsfolk could never understand.

01:40:21.090 --> 01:40:26.460
Word spread, and that’s when a search and
discovery team was sent from The Foundation.

01:40:26.460 --> 01:40:31.800
It was a cold, dark night in January of 1941
when the team found what they were looking

01:40:31.800 --> 01:40:32.800
for.

01:40:32.800 --> 01:40:36.739
They walked through the open door of a small
house located not too far from the grand Château

01:40:36.739 --> 01:40:40.489
de Richelieu, to find a masked man sitting
next to an open fire.

01:40:40.489 --> 01:40:41.889
And he wasn’t alone.

01:40:41.889 --> 01:40:44.489
The floor around him looked like it was moving.

01:40:44.489 --> 01:40:49.260
Upon closer inspection the team saw that the
floor was covered with writhing, grasping

01:40:49.260 --> 01:40:50.260
bodies.

01:40:50.260 --> 01:40:52.070
Its patients as it called them.

01:40:52.070 --> 01:40:57.810
“Bienvenue chez moi,” said the thing,
“Welcome to my home.”

01:40:57.810 --> 01:41:02.260
Those so-called patients crawled towards the
team, intent it seemed to cause harm.

01:41:02.260 --> 01:41:08.949
The hostiles, now known as SCP-049-2s, were
deemed dangerous and had to be eliminated.

01:41:08.949 --> 01:41:13.711
A sight, it seemed, that didn’t bother 049
in the slightest.

01:41:13.711 --> 01:41:17.729
It just sat there, occasionally looking up
from writing notes in a leather-bound book

01:41:17.729 --> 01:41:20.050
as his patients were gunned down.

01:41:20.050 --> 01:41:25.929
Once the carnage ended it simply closed its
book, stood up, and allowed itself to be escorted

01:41:25.929 --> 01:41:26.929
away.

01:41:26.929 --> 01:41:31.280
And that’s the story of how 049 ended up
at the facility, becoming a guest of sorts

01:41:31.280 --> 01:41:36.119
staying in a Standard Secure Humanoid Containment
Cell, Research Sector-02, Site-19.

01:41:36.119 --> 01:41:41.440
The few that came into contact with 049, remarked
that it was a pleasure for them.

01:41:41.440 --> 01:41:46.059
With its impeccable manners, vast knowledge
of medicine and human anatomy, sharp tongue

01:41:46.059 --> 01:41:47.650
and stinging wit.

01:41:47.650 --> 01:41:52.119
They almost became spellbound listening to
it, caught in the throes of its charms until,

01:41:52.119 --> 01:41:55.719
with the simple touch of its hand, it would
drain the life from them.

01:41:55.719 --> 01:41:59.570
That’s why SCP-049 was classified as a Euclid.

01:41:59.570 --> 01:42:02.599
That’s why armed guards were always stationed
outside its cell.

01:42:02.599 --> 01:42:05.909
It’s why doctors took great precautions
when in its presence.

01:42:05.909 --> 01:42:08.769
And it’s why Doctor Morstead should have
known better.

01:42:08.769 --> 01:42:14.139
Remember, when 049 was discovered in France
it willingly went with the team, like it was

01:42:14.139 --> 01:42:17.760
happy it had been found; as if it had planned
its own capture.

01:42:17.760 --> 01:42:21.679
When it arrived at the facility it didn’t
act like it was contained against its will,

01:42:21.679 --> 01:42:24.179
it was like it was returning home.

01:42:24.179 --> 01:42:28.130
Initial findings as to the biology of 049
were that it didn’t require any sustenance

01:42:28.130 --> 01:42:29.929
at all, not even water.

01:42:29.929 --> 01:42:32.800
It seemed content to be left alone with its
notebooks.

01:42:32.800 --> 01:42:36.449
It did not object when it was asked if it
could share some of its notes and gladly handed

01:42:36.449 --> 01:42:40.389
over its journals, but upon examination it
was discovered that they were written in a

01:42:40.389 --> 01:42:45.519
language that no linguist or cryptologist
has so far been able to translate.

01:42:45.519 --> 01:42:51.489
It’s apparent that 049 derives much satisfaction
from seeing so-called experts struggle over

01:42:51.489 --> 01:42:52.489
its text.

01:42:52.489 --> 01:42:58.019
Unable to read those notes, a long line of
doctors visited 049 in its cell, each fascinated

01:42:58.019 --> 01:42:59.019
by what they beheld.

01:42:59.019 --> 01:43:01.380
It was learned that it has traveled the globe.

01:43:01.380 --> 01:43:06.370
It speaks many languages, but prefers to speak
what it calls “le langage de l'amour”

01:43:06.370 --> 01:43:07.370
- French.

01:43:07.370 --> 01:43:11.159
It asked for only one thing, warm-blooded
animals.

01:43:11.159 --> 01:43:16.119
The facility agreed to supply 049 with various
kinds, including rabbits, cattle, and even

01:43:16.119 --> 01:43:18.050
an ape on one occasion.

01:43:18.050 --> 01:43:22.229
Just like with humans, it could kill the animals
with a mere touch of its hand, sucking the

01:43:22.229 --> 01:43:23.860
life right out of them.

01:43:23.860 --> 01:43:26.400
But that wasn’t even the most incredible
part.

01:43:26.400 --> 01:43:30.229
Soon those animals would rise again, as if
reanimated by 049.

01:43:30.229 --> 01:43:35.040
They would become, for all intents and purposes,
the living dead.

01:43:35.040 --> 01:43:37.349
And they were hostile.

01:43:37.349 --> 01:43:40.679
After several unfortunate incidents, they
were then taken from the cell the moment they

01:43:40.679 --> 01:43:43.650
arose and disposed of in the incinerator.

01:43:43.650 --> 01:43:48.289
This was not to the liking of 049, who would
claim it had “cured” the animals.

01:43:48.289 --> 01:43:52.920
For it, the world was sick…it saw plague
and pestilence everywhere and the meaning

01:43:52.920 --> 01:43:56.219
of its existence was to rid the world of disease.

01:43:56.219 --> 01:44:01.229
Humans, it said contained a virus, and had
to be cleansed.

01:44:01.229 --> 01:44:06.219
In the first days after arriving at the facility,
049 didn’t seem to pose a threat to humans.

01:44:06.219 --> 01:44:08.449
It was quite friendly in fact.

01:44:08.449 --> 01:44:12.800
It seemed aware of the fear it caused in staff
and would often go out its way to make them

01:44:12.800 --> 01:44:14.849
feel comfortable and safe.

01:44:14.849 --> 01:44:19.170
This was a ruse, of course, or a “canard”
as 049 liked to say.

01:44:19.170 --> 01:44:21.540
It had no intention to help humans.

01:44:21.540 --> 01:44:24.650
No, it had come for humans.

01:44:24.650 --> 01:44:28.329
It wasn’t trapped…it had set a trap.

01:44:28.329 --> 01:44:33.119
One of the first people to truly upset 049
was Dr. Raymond Hamm, a well-respected physician

01:44:33.119 --> 01:44:36.860
that had twice been a contender for the Nobel
Prize for his more mainstream work.

01:44:36.860 --> 01:44:41.760
What had confused Dr. Hamm the most was not
049’s clothes-like exoskeleton, or even

01:44:41.760 --> 01:44:45.449
his ability to reanimate the dead, but the
bag that it used.

01:44:45.449 --> 01:44:50.769
049 was somehow able to pull a seemingly endless
supply of surgical tools from that bag.

01:44:50.769 --> 01:44:54.080
Sometimes it would even pull out objects that
were somehow larger than the bag itself.

01:44:54.080 --> 01:44:58.520
It was as if the bag connected to somewhere
else, and that’s what Dr. Hamm wanted to

01:44:58.520 --> 01:45:00.590
talk about on that fateful day.

01:45:00.590 --> 01:45:05.460
With 049 on one side of the cell and Dr. Hamm
on the other, he asked, “How is it that

01:45:05.460 --> 01:45:09.969
you can produce a great quantity of tools
from that bag…I have observed you, and it

01:45:09.969 --> 01:45:12.030
seems to me, that you are doing the impossible.”

01:45:12.030 --> 01:45:16.750
“Dear doctor,” replied 049, “The Scourge!

01:45:16.750 --> 01:45:20.690
The Great Dying, cannot be fought with a handful
of toys.

01:45:20.690 --> 01:45:25.949
My bag is merely the product of my imagination,
it gives me what I require.

01:45:25.949 --> 01:45:31.150
You dear sir, it seems, are limited by your
imagination.”

01:45:31.150 --> 01:45:34.070
It stopped for a second or two and stared
at Dr. Hamm.

01:45:34.070 --> 01:45:38.889
“I detect you are unwell,” it said, in
a voice not as amiable as before.

01:45:38.889 --> 01:45:41.599
“It’s just a cold,” said the doctor.

01:45:41.599 --> 01:45:43.340
“Ah, just a cold?

01:45:43.340 --> 01:45:47.710
If you had seen what I have seen you would
not utter such insulting words.”

01:45:47.710 --> 01:45:52.880
Dr. Hamm pulled out some papers from a briefcase
and approached 049, holding them close enough

01:45:52.880 --> 01:45:54.460
so it could read them.

01:45:54.460 --> 01:45:57.940
“You see,” said Doctor Hamm pointing to
the results on the paper, “Those animals

01:45:57.940 --> 01:46:03.330
you say you cured, they were not diseased…they
were perfectly healthy before they died…and

01:46:03.330 --> 01:46:06.800
your so-called cure, it turned them into something
quite terrible.

01:46:06.800 --> 01:46:11.349
We found that if they were left alone, they
began to eat each other, and then themselves.”

01:46:11.349 --> 01:46:16.979
049 did not respond and after a brief pause
said only, “A good day to you doctor, please

01:46:16.979 --> 01:46:18.479
close the door on your way out.

01:46:18.479 --> 01:46:20.479
You should get some rest.”

01:46:20.479 --> 01:46:26.360
Hamm refused to go, and instead turned the
conversation to this real interest, the bag,

01:46:26.360 --> 01:46:29.270
demanding that 049 let him see inside of it.

01:46:29.270 --> 01:46:30.949
“Very well, doctor.”

01:46:30.949 --> 01:46:33.190
049 said, “in private.”

01:46:33.190 --> 01:46:37.739
049 began to pull a series of long metal poles
out of its bag followed by a rolled up curtain

01:46:37.739 --> 01:46:41.650
that it hung between them, creating a kind
of medical tent around Doctor Hamm.

01:46:41.650 --> 01:46:45.579
It seemed to stare for just a moment into
the observation camera outside of its cell

01:46:45.579 --> 01:46:47.630
before whipping the curtains shut.

01:46:47.630 --> 01:46:52.400
Doctor Hamm was discovered three hours later,
crawling around the floor of 049’s cell,

01:46:52.400 --> 01:46:54.670
now another mindless undead.

01:46:54.670 --> 01:46:59.389
When he was retrieved by security, 049 didn’t
even look up from his notebook.

01:46:59.389 --> 01:47:03.840
Doctor Hamm didn’t get the incinerator treatment,
but he did receive a fatal dose of drugs.

01:47:03.840 --> 01:47:04.960
A mercy.

01:47:04.960 --> 01:47:10.050
A removal team was sent to 049’s cell, but
it said there was no need for special extraction

01:47:10.050 --> 01:47:11.050
techniques.

01:47:11.050 --> 01:47:13.250
It would go willingly, wherever they wanted
it to go.

01:47:13.250 --> 01:47:15.829
It was not, it said, an enemy of the people.

01:47:15.829 --> 01:47:20.670
“The Hippocratic Oath forbids me to hurt
a human being,” it said while walking to

01:47:20.670 --> 01:47:21.960
the interrogation center.

01:47:21.960 --> 01:47:26.920
“My only desire is to offer you my services
and expertise.”

01:47:26.920 --> 01:47:31.059
The floors and walls of the interrogation
center room were painted a bright white.

01:47:31.059 --> 01:47:36.150
Even the table was white, which contrasted
with 049, a mass of black, sitting in the

01:47:36.150 --> 01:47:37.561
middle of the room.

01:47:37.561 --> 01:47:42.099
During interrogation it refused to admit or
even accept that it had killed Dr. Hamm.

01:47:42.099 --> 01:47:46.019
“I cured him, I removed the pestilence from
his body,” it said.

01:47:46.019 --> 01:47:51.019
It was later asked if it regretted its actions,
to which it replied, “Well, good sir, one

01:47:51.019 --> 01:47:56.099
always regrets the loss of a colleague for
any reason, but I stand by my actions.

01:47:56.099 --> 01:47:59.610
The pestilence must be abated before it’s
too late.”

01:47:59.610 --> 01:48:03.080
Every two weeks from that point 049 was given
animals.

01:48:03.080 --> 01:48:07.640
The scientists at the facility observed it
time and again, touching the animals, killing

01:48:07.640 --> 01:48:11.159
them, before producing a saw or scalpel and
opening them up.

01:48:11.159 --> 01:48:13.820
Organs would be carefully removed with perfect
precision.

01:48:13.820 --> 01:48:18.519
It was astounding to even trained surgeons
just how talented 049 was.

01:48:18.519 --> 01:48:24.170
“I require a close relative of yours,”
said 049 one day to a young doctor, who expressed

01:48:24.170 --> 01:48:26.960
shock that it was asking for one of the do
ctor’s family members.

01:48:26.960 --> 01:48:32.440
“I mean a great ape,” said 049, “not
your dear aunt.”

01:48:32.440 --> 01:48:36.600
There were several instances of 049 displaying
a crude sense of humor.

01:48:36.600 --> 01:48:39.170
Staff would almost forget that the thing they
were talking to wasn’t human… almost.

01:48:39.170 --> 01:48:45.520
And it was Doctor Thomas Morstead that had
supplied the great apes, orangutans in fact,

01:48:45.520 --> 01:48:50.800
that had been rescued from the rainforests
of Borneo only to be taken to 049’s cell.

01:48:50.800 --> 01:48:53.159
Then one day something changed.

01:48:53.159 --> 01:48:57.940
049 told Doctor Morstead that its work was
done, that it had accomplished what it had

01:48:57.940 --> 01:49:01.269
wanted to do, and could someone remove the
cured animal from its cell.

01:49:01.269 --> 01:49:06.291
“I think you’ll find that it’s quite
the work of art.

01:49:06.291 --> 01:49:07.810
A triumph,” 049 said through the intercom.

01:49:07.810 --> 01:49:11.980
When the removal team entered the cell they
found the orangutan, or what was left of it.

01:49:11.980 --> 01:49:15.789
It was lying in the corner of the cell, the
top of its skull had been removed leaving

01:49:15.789 --> 01:49:17.170
its brain exposed.

01:49:17.170 --> 01:49:22.489
On its face was an expression of relaxation
and from its mouth it issued very soft squeaks,

01:49:22.489 --> 01:49:24.840
like that of an infant.

01:49:24.840 --> 01:49:30.880
049 said, “Tell Doctor Morstead that it’s
rage mechanism no longer exists, I’ve removed

01:49:30.880 --> 01:49:35.170
the amygdala and made some changes to the
hypothalamus and limbic system.

01:49:35.170 --> 01:49:38.119
It is cured and quite harmless.”

01:49:38.119 --> 01:49:42.630
The next day Doctor Morstead announced that
he wanted to visit 049’s cell himself, after

01:49:42.630 --> 01:49:47.660
which he heard a chorus of disapproval from
his colleagues, all telling him that 049 was

01:49:47.660 --> 01:49:49.110
now too dangerous.

01:49:49.110 --> 01:49:53.519
“Dr. Hamm was sick,” replied Morstead,
“and 049 has assured us that he would never

01:49:53.519 --> 01:49:54.830
take another human life.

01:49:54.830 --> 01:49:58.289
He’s never lied to us and I’m going to
take him at his word.”

01:49:58.289 --> 01:50:02.340
It appeared that 049 had created the perfect
specimen, so what was next?

01:50:02.340 --> 01:50:04.969
Dr. Morstead had to know.

01:50:04.969 --> 01:50:10.530
“Everyone is sick,” 049 told Doctor Morstead
after the two had talked for a couple of minutes.

01:50:10.530 --> 01:50:12.800
“The great pandemic has started.

01:50:12.800 --> 01:50:18.729
Fear not doctor, I have a cure, no longer
will you humans spread your disease.”

01:50:18.729 --> 01:50:23.110
“I’m afraid you are wrong,” replied
the doctor, “This pandemic you speak of

01:50:23.110 --> 01:50:24.320
does not exist.

01:50:24.320 --> 01:50:25.699
We can happily live with our pathogens.

01:50:25.699 --> 01:50:27.940
We have done so for millennia.”

01:50:27.940 --> 01:50:30.550
Doctor Morstead became angry that he couldn’t
get through to 049.

01:50:30.550 --> 01:50:33.230
“I’m afraid you are suffering from paranoia.

01:50:33.230 --> 01:50:38.650
It is you who need to be cured”
“You have no idea,” said 049, standing

01:50:38.650 --> 01:50:39.650
up.

01:50:39.650 --> 01:50:43.150
“What are you doing?” shouted Morstead,
“you promised you wouldn’t hurt a human

01:50:43.150 --> 01:50:44.150
again!”

01:50:44.150 --> 01:50:50.340
“I’m not hurting you, I’m healing you”
049 said and leapt across the room in a flash,

01:50:50.340 --> 01:50:52.039
placing a hand on the doctor’s head.

01:50:52.039 --> 01:50:53.860
Morstead slumped to the ground.

01:50:53.860 --> 01:50:57.719
They were being watched in the observation
room and this had gone too far.

01:50:57.719 --> 01:51:01.090
He had to be moved to the containment cells,
permanently.

01:51:01.090 --> 01:51:05.000
Mobile Task Force Epsilon-11 was right on
the scene and burst through the door.

01:51:05.000 --> 01:51:11.489
“No imagination,” 049 said to himself,
“those humans have no imagination at all.”

01:51:11.489 --> 01:51:15.869
It began walking towards the task force who
opened fire on the anomaly, but the bullets

01:51:15.869 --> 01:51:19.199
bounced off its black coat and mask.

01:51:19.199 --> 01:51:24.139
SCP-049 calmly touched each of the members
of the task force one by one draining the

01:51:24.139 --> 01:51:25.390
life from them.

01:51:25.390 --> 01:51:31.409
The last one standing stopped firing and attempted
to run but again 049 leapt across the room,

01:51:31.409 --> 01:51:36.039
black cape billowing out behind him, and gently
touched the man causing him to drop to the

01:51:36.039 --> 01:51:37.039
floor.

01:51:37.039 --> 01:51:40.920
049 stepped over the bodies of the fallen
team and walked out of the confinement cell.

01:51:40.920 --> 01:51:45.289
The full details of what happened next are
available only to The O5 Council, what are

01:51:45.289 --> 01:51:46.789
sometimes called The Overseers.

01:51:46.789 --> 01:51:51.449
The redacted report that is available reads:
Standard Secure Humanoid Containment Cell,

01:51:51.449 --> 01:51:58.099
Research Sector-02, Site-19 – subject: SCP-049
Date of breach: REDACTED.

01:51:58.099 --> 01:52:03.269
Euclid Class SCP-049 breached cell and subsequently
gained access to adjoining rooms and nearby

01:52:03.269 --> 01:52:04.269
buildings.

01:52:04.269 --> 01:52:06.989
Breach lasted approximately three days and
five hours.

01:52:06.989 --> 01:52:11.789
Total Casualties: REDACTED with REDACTED number
of survivors requiring incineration therapy

01:52:11.789 --> 01:52:16.500
Course of action: Department of Science - Alchemy
Division, suggested injecting anti-transmogrify

01:52:16.500 --> 01:52:21.079
disinfectant into Class D former prisoners
who were transported to site and allowed to

01:52:21.079 --> 01:52:23.159
come into contact with SCP-049.

01:52:23.159 --> 01:52:27.860
SCP-049 failed to reanimate injected prisoners
and “cure” them.

01:52:27.860 --> 01:52:31.469
SCP-049 acknowledged this failure and surrendered
to Mobile Task Force Alpha-1.

01:52:31.469 --> 01:52:35.249
SCP-049 then requested to be contained.

01:52:35.249 --> 01:52:38.789
Present containment under responsibility of:
REDACTED; REDACTED.

01:52:38.789 --> 01:52:41.409
Present location of SCP-049: REDACTED.

01:52:41.409 --> 01:52:43.699
End of report.

01:52:43.699 --> 01:52:49.980
We were a team…despite our differences,
in spite of the terrible things they’d done,

01:52:49.980 --> 01:52:52.340
we were still a team.

01:52:52.340 --> 01:52:55.429
That’s not how the higher-ups saw it, though..

01:52:55.429 --> 01:53:00.619
No, the guys upstairs with their perfectly
pressed shirts… for them, we were judged

01:53:00.619 --> 01:53:06.400
by our level of expendability and they knew
that our next mission... was a death sentence.

01:53:06.400 --> 01:53:12.050
One by one that… that thing, took out my
team, my friends.

01:53:12.050 --> 01:53:16.030
Snapping their necks so quickly and with such
ease that no sooner did I hear the scream...

01:53:16.030 --> 01:53:17.780
they were dead.

01:53:17.780 --> 01:53:21.289
We had been used…I’d been used.

01:53:21.289 --> 01:53:27.530
Delivered as prey to the predator, a plot
that was sanctioned by the bosses and approved

01:53:27.530 --> 01:53:29.289
with a blood-red stamp.

01:53:29.289 --> 01:53:31.489
Why did they do it?

01:53:31.489 --> 01:53:34.821
I’m still trying to figure that out.

01:53:34.821 --> 01:53:38.170
Maybe that’s something you can tell me after
you hear how these so-called scientific men

01:53:38.170 --> 01:53:43.810
left us in the cell, and in the hands, of
SCP-173.

01:53:43.810 --> 01:53:49.960
For me it had been the best of times before
it became the worst of times.

01:53:49.960 --> 01:53:54.699
The best, because I’d quickly risen through
the ranks at the facility…the worst because,

01:53:54.699 --> 01:53:57.329
well, I’ll get to that.

01:53:57.329 --> 01:53:59.039
I was never the best student.

01:53:59.039 --> 01:54:03.270
I’d finished high-school by the skin of
my teeth, and my job prospects looked bleak.

01:54:03.270 --> 01:54:05.369
But I was lucky I guess…

01:54:05.369 --> 01:54:08.520
Or at least I thought so at the time.

01:54:08.520 --> 01:54:11.659
You see I have an Uncle Siegfried who did
some work for the government.

01:54:11.659 --> 01:54:15.260
I never actually knew what he did, just that
it was secretive work.

01:54:15.260 --> 01:54:20.179
I used to imagine he was some sort of super
spy so you can imagine how excited I was when

01:54:20.179 --> 01:54:23.139
he found out I needed a job and he offered
to help me out.

01:54:23.139 --> 01:54:27.219
I couldn’t believe it, I always thought
he hated me.

01:54:27.219 --> 01:54:31.119
I’d overheard him telling my parents that
I was a no good deadbeat but now he’d had

01:54:31.119 --> 01:54:35.239
a change of heart and was willing to take
me under his wing.

01:54:35.239 --> 01:54:36.239
What would I get to do?

01:54:36.239 --> 01:54:37.769
Undercover intelligence gathering?

01:54:37.769 --> 01:54:39.889
International assassinations?

01:54:39.889 --> 01:54:42.680
“Just you wait,” he said.

01:54:42.680 --> 01:54:48.079
And that’s how I found myself walking into
a sprawling, futuristic-looking facility where

01:54:48.079 --> 01:54:52.380
they handed me a level one security clearance
card with big bold letters that read…

01:54:52.380 --> 01:54:53.380
Janitor.

01:54:53.380 --> 01:54:58.829
But I was happy, just the words “security
clearance” made me feel important and it

01:54:58.829 --> 01:55:00.389
beat flipping burgers.

01:55:00.389 --> 01:55:06.889
I pushed mops, turned off lights, fired-up
generators, clocked in and clocked out, but

01:55:06.889 --> 01:55:12.079
all that time they must have been watching
me, grooming me, waiting for the day they

01:55:12.079 --> 01:55:13.639
could throw me to the wolves.

01:55:13.639 --> 01:55:18.640
I should have known; I’ve always been an
expendable kind of guy.

01:55:18.640 --> 01:55:24.119
After a few years I was called to an office,
and there was a man in a plaid shirt and kind

01:55:24.119 --> 01:55:26.280
of tweed jacket professors wear.

01:55:26.280 --> 01:55:31.159
He asked me, “Do you have any idea about
what we actually do here?”

01:55:31.159 --> 01:55:34.980
And to be honest, I didn’t.

01:55:34.980 --> 01:55:38.159
I knew that there were many parts of the facility
I couldn’t enter.

01:55:38.159 --> 01:55:42.869
I imagined that down the maze of corridors
were weapons being built, or prisoners being

01:55:42.869 --> 01:55:45.469
interrogated, but I had no idea about the
anomalies.

01:55:45.469 --> 01:55:47.260
How could I?

01:55:47.260 --> 01:55:51.619
Before I was told anything I had to sign a
bunch of forms…there were so many I thought

01:55:51.619 --> 01:55:53.249
I’d get to find out who really killed JFK.

01:55:53.249 --> 01:55:58.650
And while they didn’t come out and say it,
what I inferred was that if I ever talk about

01:55:58.650 --> 01:56:03.610
what happens at the facility to someone outside
the facility, well let’s just say it’s

01:56:03.610 --> 01:56:07.530
not the kind of thing they’d spell out on
a piece of paper but it involves padded cells

01:56:07.530 --> 01:56:09.150
and rusty tools.

01:56:09.150 --> 01:56:11.869
I wasn’t scared though.

01:56:11.869 --> 01:56:16.199
I was a part of something big, something secret,
and I loved it.

01:56:16.199 --> 01:56:19.749
So I signed my life away with no hesitation.

01:56:19.749 --> 01:56:24.039
Soon after I was introduced to my first anomaly,
the “Safe” class of course.

01:56:24.039 --> 01:56:28.889
They took me to an observation room and from
that room I could see into another room with

01:56:28.889 --> 01:56:31.690
a sign on the wall that read, “SCP-067.”

01:56:31.690 --> 01:56:36.400
I just stood there, waiting for something
to happen, when in walked another guy in a

01:56:36.400 --> 01:56:37.400
white lab coat.

01:56:37.400 --> 01:56:39.400
“Welcome to your first anomaly,” he said.

01:56:39.400 --> 01:56:41.760
“Is it okay if I hook you up to this heart
monitor?

01:56:41.760 --> 01:56:44.050
We want to gauge your reaction to what you
see.”

01:56:44.050 --> 01:56:47.869
“All I can see,” I told him, “Is an
empty room with a table and what looks like

01:56:47.869 --> 01:56:49.590
a pen on top of some papers.”

01:56:49.590 --> 01:56:55.709
“Correct,” he said, half-smiling as if
I was some kind of idiot, “That’s SCP-067.”

01:56:55.709 --> 01:57:00.260
I thought about telling him that if I needed
years of training before I could see a pen

01:57:00.260 --> 01:57:02.239
then I probably should have taken that fast
food job.

01:57:02.239 --> 01:57:04.489
I could have been shift manager by now.

01:57:04.489 --> 01:57:08.229
They then brought a young chimpanzee into
the room, small enough to be harmless.

01:57:08.229 --> 01:57:12.659
One of the guys forced a pen into the scared
chimp’s hand and something strange happened…

01:57:12.659 --> 01:57:14.820
it started scribbling.

01:57:14.820 --> 01:57:18.989
Nonsense at first, but suddenly it was sketching
and drawing, faster and faster, I could catch

01:57:18.989 --> 01:57:20.760
glimpses of words and images.

01:57:20.760 --> 01:57:24.099
By the time they dragged it out it was flailing
around like it was possessed.

01:57:24.099 --> 01:57:28.249
“That pen has power” said the man in the
lab coat, “a power whose source or origin

01:57:28.249 --> 01:57:29.449
we don’t fully understand.

01:57:29.449 --> 01:57:31.690
That’s why we’re here.

01:57:31.690 --> 01:57:33.670
That’s why you are here.”

01:57:33.670 --> 01:57:37.249
One of the guys in the other room held the
chimp’s drawing up to the window.

01:57:37.249 --> 01:57:41.810
It was a perfect sketch of the Tower of London,
intricate and brilliant.

01:57:41.810 --> 01:57:46.460
Above the sketch was the title, “Tower of
London: Tudor Period, circa 1541, the year

01:57:46.460 --> 01:57:51.060
Margaret Pole, the Countess of Salisbury,
lost her head on the chopping block.”

01:57:51.060 --> 01:57:57.690
Underneath that the chimp had written, “Pity...she
was no traitor, take it from me, I was there.”

01:57:57.690 --> 01:58:02.670
They didn’t need to look at the heart rate
monitor to see that I was shocked.

01:58:02.670 --> 01:58:06.940
That was far from the only anomaly I’d come
into contact with, and I must have been doing

01:58:06.940 --> 01:58:12.560
something right because in time I went from
level 1, to 2, to level 3 security clearance,

01:58:12.560 --> 01:58:14.960
and that’s when they made me a “Containment
Specialist.”

01:58:14.960 --> 01:58:19.530
I won’t bore you with all the details, but
as you can guess, I dealt with the containment

01:58:19.530 --> 01:58:20.639
of anomalies.

01:58:20.639 --> 01:58:25.249
A lot of my time was spent looking through
small windows in cell doors, making sure that

01:58:25.249 --> 01:58:29.219
whatever was inside was still inside and still
in one piece.

01:58:29.219 --> 01:58:33.550
Other times I worked with field agents when
anomalies were brought in, a transition period

01:58:33.550 --> 01:58:36.630
that the arrested freaks didn’t much like.

01:58:36.630 --> 01:58:40.550
There was one certain anomaly though, that
I was tasked to oversee on many occasions.

01:58:40.550 --> 01:58:47.770
I liked to think of it as my pet, but in hindsight,
I was its pet.

01:58:47.770 --> 01:58:54.239
This was SCP-173, something that was in what
we call the Euclid class, a classification

01:58:54.239 --> 01:58:59.409
meaning that we don’t fully understand it,
but know is very dangerous.

01:58:59.409 --> 01:59:05.000
We know it’s intelligent, we know it’s
unpredictable... and we know it will kill.

01:59:05.000 --> 01:59:08.829
And for that reason, there’s people tasked
with containing it and keeping an eye on it

01:59:08.829 --> 01:59:11.239
at all times.

01:59:11.239 --> 01:59:14.699
At first glance, you wouldn’t guess just
how dangerous 173 is.

01:59:14.699 --> 01:59:19.440
You wouldn’t think it’s incredibly intelligent…
in fact you’d probably think the opposite.

01:59:19.440 --> 01:59:24.110
That’s because it’s more or less a walking
slab of concrete and rebar with stunted limbs

01:59:24.110 --> 01:59:27.760
and traces of spray paint that give the impression
of a dopey face.

01:59:27.760 --> 01:59:30.840
We have to enter its cell twice a week for
cleaning duties.

01:59:30.840 --> 01:59:35.639
It leaves a disgusting, foul smelling liquid
on the floor, a reddish brown substance that

01:59:35.639 --> 01:59:38.769
I can only describe as a mix of blood and
waste products.

01:59:38.769 --> 01:59:44.849
Where that stuff comes from has remained a
mystery since we first contained it in 1993.

01:59:44.849 --> 01:59:49.050
Going into the cell was always a three man
job because, and this is maybe the weirdest

01:59:49.050 --> 01:59:53.079
part about 173, it can’t move if human eyes
are watching it.

01:59:53.079 --> 01:59:55.829
That’s why you need at least two people
watching it at all times.

01:59:55.829 --> 02:00:01.170
If you were in the room watching 173 by yourself
and blinked you’d be dead before your eyes

02:00:01.170 --> 02:00:02.170
opened.

02:00:02.170 --> 02:00:05.820
We don’t know how it moves that fast but
in that fraction of a second of a second your

02:00:05.820 --> 02:00:08.699
neck is snapped so hard it’s almost like
being decapitated.

02:00:08.699 --> 02:00:10.780
I’ve seen the videos to prove it.

02:00:10.780 --> 02:00:12.730
All it took was a sneeze.

02:00:12.730 --> 02:00:16.929
He wasn’t even finished getting the rest
of the ACHOO out when there was a flash and

02:00:16.929 --> 02:00:21.959
his partner was left lying on the ground,
his head twisted around the wrong direction.

02:00:21.959 --> 02:00:27.039
So, you can understand why we now require
three men for any time we must enter 173’s

02:00:27.039 --> 02:00:28.079
cell.

02:00:28.079 --> 02:00:33.769
Then a few months ago I was told that a long
process would begin to train and reeducate

02:00:33.769 --> 02:00:36.130
some future Class Ds.

02:00:36.130 --> 02:00:40.010
Class Ds are mostly prisoners with life-long
sentences or those we’ve taken from death

02:00:40.010 --> 02:00:41.820
row and given a new lease on life.

02:00:41.820 --> 02:00:46.449
We were apparently understaffed, so why not
employ men whose lives had pretty much ended

02:00:46.449 --> 02:00:47.449
anyway?

02:00:47.449 --> 02:00:49.949
That was the rationale, or at least that’s
what they told me.

02:00:49.949 --> 02:00:55.349
I was to train them on their new job... mopping
up 173’s mess, so that me and the rest of

02:00:55.349 --> 02:00:58.570
the containment specialists could focus on
more important tasks.

02:00:58.570 --> 02:01:03.599
They hadn’t been through the training I
had, seen what I had seen, but after showing

02:01:03.599 --> 02:01:08.329
them the video of 173 nearly taking off a
man’s head they were more than willing to

02:01:08.329 --> 02:01:09.830
follow the rules.

02:01:09.830 --> 02:01:14.699
They understood not to blink, or turn away,
or sneeze, and that any lapse in focus could

02:01:14.699 --> 02:01:16.579
lead to a violent death.

02:01:16.579 --> 02:01:20.830
So I started to show them the ropes, how we
move as a team into the cell and always keep

02:01:20.830 --> 02:01:23.390
the others informed on what we’re doing.

02:01:23.390 --> 02:01:28.249
173 was always sitting in the corner of the
cell, no expression on that crude face, but

02:01:28.249 --> 02:01:32.630
when we walked in its cell I got the feeling
it knew something had changed.

02:01:32.630 --> 02:01:37.289
I felt almost as if it was communicating with
me, but I couldn’t tell what it was trying

02:01:37.289 --> 02:01:39.190
to say.

02:01:39.190 --> 02:01:41.409
And then it happened.

02:01:41.409 --> 02:01:45.260
It was a Tuesday afternoon, three days from
the last time we’d cleaned.

02:01:45.260 --> 02:01:49.010
As usual, 173 had covered the floor with that
horrible liquid.

02:01:49.010 --> 02:01:53.840
We headed in to clean, my new team alert as
always, and some of them cleaned while others

02:01:53.840 --> 02:01:56.809
kept their eyes focused on the thing in the
corner.

02:01:56.809 --> 02:01:59.479
Things were going smoothly when we heard a
noise I knew very well.

02:01:59.479 --> 02:02:03.880
It was the sound of the cell door locking.

02:02:03.880 --> 02:02:05.050
Someone must have screwed up.

02:02:05.050 --> 02:02:08.670
“Hey guys, we’re locked in here,” I
shouted through the intercom.

02:02:08.670 --> 02:02:09.670
Nothing.

02:02:09.670 --> 02:02:11.519
“Guys, the damn door is locked.”

02:02:11.519 --> 02:02:12.519
Nothing.

02:02:12.519 --> 02:02:15.130
I lost it a bit.

02:02:15.130 --> 02:02:17.389
“Open the door, will you!”

02:02:17.389 --> 02:02:18.559
Nothing.

02:02:18.559 --> 02:02:24.099
My team looked at me, the ones not on eye
contact duty that is, as if I should know

02:02:24.099 --> 02:02:28.099
what to do…hoping that this had happened
before and that there was some kind of standard

02:02:28.099 --> 02:02:29.880
plan to deal with it.

02:02:29.880 --> 02:02:30.880
There wasn’t.

02:02:30.880 --> 02:02:35.159
We were always observed when in the room and
I knew that a technician couldn’t accidentally

02:02:35.159 --> 02:02:36.179
lock the door.

02:02:36.179 --> 02:02:37.709
It was impossible.

02:02:37.709 --> 02:02:39.440
There were protocols.

02:02:39.440 --> 02:02:40.469
Someone had done this on purpose.

02:02:40.469 --> 02:02:46.050
The four of us sat in the corner of the room
as far from 173 as possible, our eyes locked

02:02:46.050 --> 02:02:47.050
on it.

02:02:47.050 --> 02:02:52.750
It didn’t move an inch as usual, just stood,
staring at the wall as it always did.

02:02:52.750 --> 02:02:57.059
We stayed awake through the night, talking
a little, holding on to the slim hope that

02:02:57.059 --> 02:02:59.159
something had gone wrong.

02:02:59.159 --> 02:03:02.510
But as night turned to day again we all began
to lose hope.

02:03:02.510 --> 02:03:04.770
We weren’t sent here to clean.

02:03:04.770 --> 02:03:07.789
We were a test… totally expendable… lab
rats.

02:03:07.789 --> 02:03:10.809
But I wouldn’t go down without a fight.

02:03:10.809 --> 02:03:14.632
We couldn’t just stay up forever, that was
a death sentence.

02:03:14.632 --> 02:03:18.300
I suggested that two of us stand, one sit
and rest, and one get some sleep.

02:03:18.300 --> 02:03:19.810
We’d take shifts.

02:03:19.810 --> 02:03:24.229
A couple hours on, a couple hours off, maybe
if we could show that we wouldn’t give up

02:03:24.229 --> 02:03:28.420
they’d have time to realize what they were
doing was insane, call off the test, and come

02:03:28.420 --> 02:03:29.420
free us.

02:03:29.420 --> 02:03:32.670
We made it through a couple of shifts like
this and it seemed like we’d actually be

02:03:32.670 --> 02:03:36.420
able to make it another day or two when everything
went wrong.

02:03:36.420 --> 02:03:39.670
It was my turn to sit and rest when I heard
the worst possible noise… snoring.

02:03:39.670 --> 02:03:46.300
The con next to me was sleeping quietly so
it must be one of the standers.

02:03:46.300 --> 02:03:50.860
I glanced over for just a split second and
saw both of them, leaning against the cell

02:03:50.860 --> 02:03:51.860
wall, dozing.

02:03:51.860 --> 02:03:54.770
At the same time I saw the flash.

02:03:54.770 --> 02:03:57.329
Crack, snap, pop.

02:03:57.329 --> 02:04:00.070
One after another their necks were snapped.

02:04:00.070 --> 02:04:06.219
I’m not sure how it happened but I was standing
again, staring at 173 who was now in the corner,

02:04:06.219 --> 02:04:09.989
dead bodies with their heads twisted around
piled up in front of it.

02:04:09.989 --> 02:04:14.460
I couldn’t take it anymore, I couldn’t
stare at this thing forever, I felt myself

02:04:14.460 --> 02:04:15.460
giving up.

02:04:15.460 --> 02:04:21.110
I lowered my head to the ground and then finally
broke my gaze, ready to die.

02:04:21.110 --> 02:04:23.929
And then… nothing happened.

02:04:23.929 --> 02:04:29.389
I slowly raised my head back up and -
There it was, it’s hideous face inches away

02:04:29.389 --> 02:04:30.389
from mine.

02:04:30.389 --> 02:04:35.619
It was then that I understood what we’d
been containing, what we’d underestimated.

02:04:35.619 --> 02:04:38.760
I felt again like it was telling me something.

02:04:38.760 --> 02:04:43.559
It was telling me to close my eyes, to sleep.

02:04:43.559 --> 02:04:44.999
So I did.

02:04:44.999 --> 02:04:51.710
But as my eyes closed I didn’t see darkness,
I saw 173, or something like it.

02:04:51.710 --> 02:04:58.340
But not in the cell, I saw it outside, in
the world, standing over children sleeping

02:04:58.340 --> 02:05:00.599
in their beds, watching.

02:05:00.599 --> 02:05:05.309
I saw them hiding in the shadows, staring
out at passers by.

02:05:05.309 --> 02:05:10.599
Then I realized they weren’t watching, waiting
to pounce.

02:05:10.599 --> 02:05:12.860
No, they were hiding.

02:05:12.860 --> 02:05:17.400
My eyes popped open as the door opened and
in rushed six security personnel.

02:05:17.400 --> 02:05:23.199
They took me outside, jabbed my leg with a
syringe injecting me with something as the

02:05:23.199 --> 02:05:27.050
world faded away…

02:05:27.050 --> 02:05:28.050
Incident Report.

02:05:28.050 --> 02:05:29.429
Time and date redacted.

02:05:29.429 --> 02:05:34.739
Following the experimental forced interaction
with Euclid Class anomaly SCP-173, subject

02:05:34.739 --> 02:05:38.420
has ceased responding to external stimuli
and appears to have taken on the traits and

02:05:38.420 --> 02:05:40.219
behaviors of the anomaly.

02:05:40.219 --> 02:05:44.310
Subject now spends entire day sitting in corner
of cell staring at wall.

02:05:44.310 --> 02:05:47.789
Staff are advised to proceed with caution
when dealing with subject as the only behavior

02:05:47.789 --> 02:05:51.469
they engage in is an attempt to strangle anyone
who enters the cell.

02:05:51.469 --> 02:05:56.239
No treatments have shown any effectiveness
and subject will unfortunately require incarceration,

02:05:56.239 --> 02:06:00.900
likely forever.
The SCP Foundation is no stranger to pure

02:06:00.900 --> 02:06:01.900
evil.

02:06:01.900 --> 02:06:07.170
Whether it’s a reptile that wants to end
all life, a sadistic old man with his own

02:06:07.170 --> 02:06:12.719
torture dimension, or the personification
of death itself lurking beyond a limestone

02:06:12.719 --> 02:06:13.719
cavern.

02:06:13.719 --> 02:06:17.020
But what if there was something even worse
out there?

02:06:17.020 --> 02:06:24.550
The embodiment of chaos and cruelty, existing
across multiple realities and dimensions.

02:06:24.550 --> 02:06:28.119
And what if it was coming for us.

02:06:28.119 --> 02:06:33.880
This is The Scarlet King - believed by many
to be the ultimate evil behind much of the

02:06:33.880 --> 02:06:39.459
trouble the Foundation has faced and some
even speculate that fighting him was the reason

02:06:39.459 --> 02:06:43.039
the Foundation was created in the first place.

02:06:43.039 --> 02:06:45.610
But what exactly is the Scarlet King?

02:06:45.610 --> 02:06:51.050
He’s known by many names, almost always
including some allusion to the color “red”,

02:06:51.050 --> 02:06:58.420
and then a reference to royalty or power-
Harak, Khahrahk, the Red Shah, the Crimson

02:06:58.420 --> 02:07:08.189
Khan, PTE-616-Mendes-Ex-Machina, the Lāla
Rājā, and of course SCP - 001 to name a

02:07:08.189 --> 02:07:09.189
few.

02:07:09.189 --> 02:07:14.189
And like many of the Foundation’s mysterious
enemies, stories about his true nature and

02:07:14.189 --> 02:07:18.070
origins abound and are often contradictory.

02:07:18.070 --> 02:07:23.829
According to the official SCP - 001 files
of Tufto’s proposal, symbology of the Scarlet

02:07:23.829 --> 02:07:29.229
King has existed in multiple cultures throughout
history, with the king often depicted the

02:07:29.229 --> 02:07:37.590
same way, as a huge, red demonic figure, often
wearing a gold crown of other headdress indicating

02:07:37.590 --> 02:07:38.590
royalty.

02:07:38.590 --> 02:07:43.440
He shows up looking similarly within different
cultures’ mythologies, despite existing

02:07:43.440 --> 02:07:48.889
at different points in history or them not
having the means to communicate with one another.

02:07:48.889 --> 02:07:53.949
A number of entities that the SCP Foundation
is familiar with are believed to be somehow

02:07:53.949 --> 02:08:01.010
connected to the Scarlet King, including SCP
- 2317 - a wooden door leading to the realm

02:08:01.010 --> 02:08:06.369
of a being known as the Devourer, who’s
expected to escape and cause an apocalyptic

02:08:06.369 --> 02:08:08.550
event in the next thirty years.

02:08:08.550 --> 02:08:14.769
But really, there’s no way of knowing just
how many SCPs are directly connected to the

02:08:14.769 --> 02:08:16.059
Scarlet King.

02:08:16.059 --> 02:08:21.389
Strangely, the Foundation's official file
on the Scarlet King once designated his containment

02:08:21.389 --> 02:08:26.039
class as Keter, but that has since been downgraded
to Safe.

02:08:26.039 --> 02:08:30.969
According to the file, any attempt to change
this designation is likely to lead to horrifying

02:08:30.969 --> 02:08:32.070
results.

02:08:32.070 --> 02:08:36.710
It is widely known that the Scarlet King still
has considerable influence over a number of

02:08:36.710 --> 02:08:43.210
groups, individuals, and anomalies in our
universe, and if ever he made his way into

02:08:43.210 --> 02:08:49.780
our universe, it would likely lead to the
irreversible damage of reality itself, so

02:08:49.780 --> 02:08:51.349
then why safe?

02:08:51.349 --> 02:08:55.719
And why are the O5 Council so adamant that
it remain that way?

02:08:55.719 --> 02:09:00.090
Getting to the bottom of this mystery is exactly
why we’re here today.

02:09:00.090 --> 02:09:05.559
But, to fully grasp the true nature of the
Scarlet King, we must first understand the

02:09:05.559 --> 02:09:11.249
man whose life and fate have always been tied
to it: Dr. Robert Montauk.

02:09:11.249 --> 02:09:16.929
If that name feels oddly familiar to you,
it’s because of its association with one

02:09:16.929 --> 02:09:23.920
of the Scarlet King’s most recent attempts
to enter our reality: SCP - 231.

02:09:23.920 --> 02:09:29.479
This SCP, often referred to as the Brides
of the Scarlet King, was formed of seven women

02:09:29.479 --> 02:09:35.300
- seven, by the way, being an extremely significant
number for the King - all kidnapped by the

02:09:35.300 --> 02:09:40.429
most recent in a long line of the King’s
devoted cults known as The Children of the

02:09:40.429 --> 02:09:41.849
Scarlet King.

02:09:41.849 --> 02:09:46.659
Each of these seven unfortunate women were
impregnated with anomalous horrors, such as

02:09:46.659 --> 02:09:53.000
the infamous SCP-682, and every time one of
these horrors were birthed, a catastrophe

02:09:53.000 --> 02:09:55.400
occurred and the mother died.

02:09:55.400 --> 02:10:01.369
At the time, Dr. Montauk was a prominent researcher
studying this anomaly, and as six catastrophes

02:10:01.369 --> 02:10:06.690
had already occurred, pressure was mounting
to figure out a way to prevent the final birth.

02:10:06.690 --> 02:10:12.579
But as he was working on the issue, Dr. Montauk
was struck with a personal tragedy - The mysterious

02:10:12.579 --> 02:10:15.889
disappearance of his 14 year old brother,
Jacob.

02:10:15.889 --> 02:10:20.679
In his fear and anger, Montauk believed that
this must have had something to do with the

02:10:20.679 --> 02:10:23.179
Scarlet King and his disciples.

02:10:23.179 --> 02:10:28.059
Wanting revenge, Montauk proposed an idea
so horrifying that the details were never

02:10:28.059 --> 02:10:35.110
made public - a procedure known as 110-Montauk
to be performed on the final bride at regular

02:10:35.110 --> 02:10:36.190
intervals.

02:10:36.190 --> 02:10:41.249
However, this wasn’t the end of Dr. Montauk’s
fraught relationship with the Scarlet King

02:10:41.249 --> 02:10:44.389
- it was just the beginning.

02:10:44.389 --> 02:10:50.500
To give you some perspective on just how dangerous
the Scarlet King is, the SCP Foundation and

02:10:50.500 --> 02:10:55.860
the Global Occult Coalition decided to put
aside their differences and form a joint effort

02:10:55.860 --> 02:10:59.040
to stamp out the Children of the Scarlet King.

02:10:59.040 --> 02:11:03.709
They were successful in this mission, and
even managed to capture the Children’s leader

02:11:03.709 --> 02:11:06.479
- a mysterious man named Dipesh Spivak.

02:11:06.479 --> 02:11:13.880
Dr. Montauk, who’d become the lead researcher
on 231 and 2317, was naturally the first choice

02:11:13.880 --> 02:11:19.590
for interviewing Dipesh about the true nature
of The Children and of The Scarlet King.

02:11:19.590 --> 02:11:25.829
Dr. Montauk could never be the impartial interviewer
that the SCP Foundation wanted though, the

02:11:25.829 --> 02:11:30.449
suspicion that the Scarlet King or the Children
had something to do with the loss of his younger

02:11:30.449 --> 02:11:35.170
brother, still lingered just beneath the surface.

02:11:35.170 --> 02:11:40.340
Like a lot of cult leaders, Dipesh was extremely
cryptic in his answers to Dr. Montauk’s

02:11:40.340 --> 02:11:41.340
questioning.

02:11:41.340 --> 02:11:45.889
He’d already heard of the doctor from the
reputation of the horrifying Montauk procedure,

02:11:45.889 --> 02:11:49.550
and was surprised to see him so calm and courteous
in person.

02:11:49.550 --> 02:11:55.179
A few key facts about the King and his cult
were revealed in the first few rounds of questioning:

02:11:55.179 --> 02:11:59.630
The Children had once worked with the Serpent’s
Hand before being excommunicated for their

02:11:59.630 --> 02:12:04.979
allegiance to the King, and they had stolen
sacred texts from the mystical Wanderer’s

02:12:04.979 --> 02:12:07.969
Library to assist in their summoning rituals.

02:12:07.969 --> 02:12:13.489
Dipesh also revealed that the Scarlet King
is bound by three Laws - the Law of Blood,

02:12:13.489 --> 02:12:17.050
the Law of Concrete, and the Law of Howling.

02:12:17.050 --> 02:12:23.050
Dr. Montauk, confused and frustrated by Dipesh’s
secrecy, had to learn more.

02:12:23.050 --> 02:12:27.449
He found an old memoir from a former member
of the Children of the Scarlet King, Jack

02:12:27.449 --> 02:12:32.719
Hearst, who had the ability to invade the
minds of people from the past and experience

02:12:32.719 --> 02:12:34.360
what they experienced.

02:12:34.360 --> 02:12:39.380
He recounted a battle between the Scarlet
King and his followers and a group of time-traveling

02:12:39.380 --> 02:12:43.280
Turkmen warriors from SCP - 3838.

02:12:43.280 --> 02:12:45.980
Hearst saw both sides of the battle.

02:12:45.980 --> 02:12:50.630
From the perspective of the Children of the
Scarlet King, their lord ruled over them from

02:12:50.630 --> 02:12:53.940
an immense fortress embedded in a volcano.

02:12:53.940 --> 02:12:58.959
From the perspective of the Turkmen, the Children
were starved and beaten peasants, commanded

02:12:58.959 --> 02:13:02.929
by the King’s voice in the roaring howl
of the wind.

02:13:02.929 --> 02:13:08.309
Montauk also found extensive records of summoning
rituals performed by various Scarlet King-aligned

02:13:08.309 --> 02:13:09.340
cults.

02:13:09.340 --> 02:13:14.949
Interestingly, some of them incorporated the
use of carved SCP Foundation symbols.

02:13:14.949 --> 02:13:16.599
What could this mean?

02:13:16.599 --> 02:13:21.860
Montauk returned again to Dipesh, who finally
gave him the truth about the Law of Blood.

02:13:21.860 --> 02:13:28.170
This is the Law of the Scarlet King - it’s
defined by poverty, violence, starvation,

02:13:28.170 --> 02:13:30.969
hate, and most of all, fear.

02:13:30.969 --> 02:13:37.249
Like the serfs in the Middle Ages, persecuted
by and subjected to violence from the nobles.

02:13:37.249 --> 02:13:42.479
To the Children of the Scarlet King, this
sense of holy pain and awe is the only way

02:13:42.479 --> 02:13:43.530
to live.

02:13:43.530 --> 02:13:50.110
The alternative is the Law of Concrete - which
means the modern age, defined by empty safety

02:13:50.110 --> 02:13:51.610
and false comfort.

02:13:51.610 --> 02:13:57.499
Buildings, easy to access food, healthcare,
knowledge, technology.

02:13:57.499 --> 02:14:01.250
This is everything that the Scarlet King despises.

02:14:01.250 --> 02:14:06.610
But the mystery only deepened as Montauk found
files from a former Foundation operative by

02:14:06.610 --> 02:14:09.300
the name of Agent de Beauvoir.

02:14:09.300 --> 02:14:14.070
Montauk learned that the Scarlet King didn’t
seem to appear until after the Foundation

02:14:14.070 --> 02:14:19.940
was created, and in fact, it seemed that the
greater interest the Foundation took in the

02:14:19.940 --> 02:14:23.530
Scarlet King, the more powerful he became.

02:14:23.530 --> 02:14:25.000
How could this be?

02:14:25.000 --> 02:14:29.699
Things were also getting stranger on a personal
level for Dr. Montauk - Dipesh repeatedly

02:14:29.699 --> 02:14:34.959
pressed him about his brother’s disappearance,
and the Montauk Procedure, during the interviews.

02:14:34.959 --> 02:14:38.770
Little by little, it was beginning to take
its toll.

02:14:38.770 --> 02:14:42.449
The questions still plagued him: What was
the Law of Howling?

02:14:42.449 --> 02:14:45.209
Who or what really is the Scarlet King?

02:14:45.209 --> 02:14:46.670
How did he come to be?

02:14:46.670 --> 02:14:50.610
Montauk’s search was causing him to act
more like the Children of the Scarlet King

02:14:50.610 --> 02:14:55.650
- ranting about the horrors of the modern
world, how all of us are living a lie.

02:14:55.650 --> 02:15:01.189
how the only “honest” way to live is suffering
under the dominion of the Scarlet King.

02:15:01.189 --> 02:15:06.280
This philosophy is summed up in the words
of one cultist named Ariadne Cartwright who

02:15:06.280 --> 02:15:07.280
said:

02:15:07.280 --> 02:15:09.619
“We must learn what it is to die.

02:15:09.619 --> 02:15:17.429
To be enslaved- truly, brutally enslaved,
with no compassion or compunction from our

02:15:17.429 --> 02:15:18.429
masters.

02:15:18.429 --> 02:15:24.599
We must learn what it is to be taken towards
a single purpose, to know and truly understand

02:15:24.599 --> 02:15:26.699
our lack of agency.

02:15:26.699 --> 02:15:33.030
We must be beholden to a world of gods and
darkness, the tempest-tossed refuse of a race

02:15:33.030 --> 02:15:34.300
of fools.

02:15:34.300 --> 02:15:40.750
We must kill modernity, postmodernity, with
all its analysis and sneering observation.

02:15:40.750 --> 02:15:44.920
There is only one rule; the rule of chaos.

02:15:44.920 --> 02:15:46.199
For humanity!

02:15:46.199 --> 02:15:47.229
For life!

02:15:47.229 --> 02:15:50.050
For the Scarlet King!”

02:15:50.050 --> 02:15:57.039
Basically, any time humanity tries to exert
control over the world, the Scarlet King gets

02:15:57.039 --> 02:15:58.079
stronger.

02:15:58.079 --> 02:16:03.929
Every time they try to understand or organize
or categorize their world, the Scarlet King

02:16:03.929 --> 02:16:04.989
gets stronger.

02:16:04.989 --> 02:16:10.039
As colonial and imperial powers conquered
and invaded lands like India, Africa, and

02:16:10.039 --> 02:16:17.239
South America, and subjugated their beliefs
under western ideas, the Scarlet King got

02:16:17.239 --> 02:16:18.239
stronger.

02:16:18.239 --> 02:16:23.900
Montauk was beginning to truly understand
the power of his enemy here, and even worse,

02:16:23.900 --> 02:16:27.730
he was starting to understand his part in
it.

02:16:27.730 --> 02:16:32.940
Montauk, slowly being driven mad by the knowledge
he was gaining, realized that the Scarlet

02:16:32.940 --> 02:16:39.500
King’s greatest enemy - The SCP Foundation
- was also its greatest asset.

02:16:39.500 --> 02:16:44.990
Every time they tried to understand the monster,
to give him some kind of comprehensible form,

02:16:44.990 --> 02:16:48.010
they only made him more powerful.

02:16:48.010 --> 02:16:53.260
Just in time with Montauk’s new revelation,
a red crack appeared in the wall of Dipesh

02:16:53.260 --> 02:16:59.130
Spivak’s containment cell - a portal to
the realm of the Scarlet King.

02:16:59.130 --> 02:17:03.380
Foundation staff found that they were unable
to enter the cell, and Dipesh demanded a final

02:17:03.380 --> 02:17:04.960
interview with Montauk.

02:17:04.960 --> 02:17:08.150
With no other options, the Foundation relented.

02:17:08.150 --> 02:17:13.860
In their very last conversation, Dipesh congratulated
Montauk for finally understanding what he

02:17:13.860 --> 02:17:14.980
was dealing with.

02:17:14.980 --> 02:17:19.090
The Scarlet King, Dipesh told him, is an idea,
a concept.

02:17:19.090 --> 02:17:24.880
He is a being given power through the conflict
between the old and new.

02:17:24.880 --> 02:17:30.500
This is the Law of the Howling - The Scarlet
King’s endless rage at the direction the

02:17:30.500 --> 02:17:33.670
world and humanity has taken.

02:17:33.670 --> 02:17:39.810
The King, according to Dipesh, hated the Foundation’s
belief that science and rationality was the

02:17:39.810 --> 02:17:41.630
true path to progress.

02:17:41.630 --> 02:17:45.330
The King saw this as little more than petty
arrogance.

02:17:45.330 --> 02:17:50.290
The reason Montauk’s Procedure on the final
Bride of the Scarlet King was so effective

02:17:50.290 --> 02:17:56.150
was because it wasn’t born out of science
- it was born out of hate, pain, the desire

02:17:56.150 --> 02:18:01.679
for revenge, and in the Scarlet King’s realm,
that would be all there is.

02:18:01.679 --> 02:18:08.220
Unless our world, and especially the Foundation
changed course, the Scarlet King’s rise

02:18:08.220 --> 02:18:10.880
to absolute power would be inevitable.

02:18:10.880 --> 02:18:17.880
Montauk, his mind practically gone, asked
one last question: Did the Children or the

02:18:17.880 --> 02:18:20.710
Scarlet King take his brother, Jacob?

02:18:20.710 --> 02:18:23.660
When Dipesh told him the answer… no.

02:18:23.660 --> 02:18:26.880
And in response, Montauk shot him dead.

02:18:26.880 --> 02:18:30.790
Finally bringing an end to the Children of
the Scarlet King.

02:18:30.790 --> 02:18:36.150
In light of his new revelations, Montauk begged
the O5 Council to change their ways in order

02:18:36.150 --> 02:18:39.679
to avoid letting the Scarlet King break into
our reality.

02:18:39.679 --> 02:18:43.780
They refused, saying Montauk’s ideas were
too radical.

02:18:43.780 --> 02:18:48.250
But they knew they couldn’t just ignore
the threat posed by the Scarlet King, they

02:18:48.250 --> 02:18:50.580
would have to take some steps.

02:18:50.580 --> 02:18:56.740
And so, the O5 council of the SCP Foundation,
the most powerful and secretive group in the

02:18:56.740 --> 02:19:01.969
entire world, in order to prevent the most
dangerous threat that humanity has ever known

02:19:01.969 --> 02:19:09.050
from breaking into our reality and enslaving
all the people of the world, finally did something.

02:19:09.050 --> 02:19:15.750
They changed the classification of the Scarlet
King from Keter… to Safe, and made its description

02:19:15.750 --> 02:19:19.610
on the official Foundation files deliberately
vague.

02:19:19.610 --> 02:19:24.370
The O5 council thinks this will be enough
to stop the Scarlet King’s power from continuing

02:19:24.370 --> 02:19:27.320
to grow, but Montauk knew it wasn’t enough.

02:19:27.320 --> 02:19:30.890
He had seen the truth, and he couldn’t unsee
it.

02:19:30.890 --> 02:19:35.540
While the Foundation was going on as normal,
Montauk grew to despise them.

02:19:35.540 --> 02:19:40.610
He knew the Scarlet King was coming, he knew
that he couldn’t be stopped, and that our

02:19:40.610 --> 02:19:44.070
whole reality was little more than sitting
ducks.

02:19:44.070 --> 02:19:51.290
Dr. Robert Montauk is no longer a researcher
for the SCP Foundation, no Dr. Robert Montauk

02:19:51.290 --> 02:19:52.940
chose a different path.

02:19:52.940 --> 02:20:00.410
He’s now a child of the Scarlet King, a
devotee of madness, hate, and chaos.

02:20:00.410 --> 02:20:06.090
You can’t beat the Scarlet King after all,
and as the old adage goes, “If you can’t

02:20:06.090 --> 02:20:11.271
beat ‘em, join ‘em.”
When an anomaly is first detected by an SCP

02:20:11.271 --> 02:20:13.720
Foundation Field Agent, it’s up to the Foundation’s

02:20:13.720 --> 02:20:19.891
Mobile Task Forces to tag and bag the impossible
entities before they can do any more harm.

02:20:19.891 --> 02:20:25.530
Sometimes these retrievals are uneventful,
other times... not so much - especially when

02:20:25.530 --> 02:20:33.040
they’re dealing with brutal forces of nature
like SCP - 096, also known as, The Shy Guy.

02:20:33.040 --> 02:20:38.360
A creature that, from its very first interaction
with the Foundation, had a reputation for

02:20:38.360 --> 02:20:41.561
being dangerous and needed to be feared.

02:20:41.561 --> 02:20:45.860
A series of vague sightings and mysterious
disappearances up in the frosty mountains

02:20:45.860 --> 02:20:49.910
of the Yukon first sparked the Foundation’s
interest. When they were certain that they

02:20:49.910 --> 02:20:56.630
had an anomaly on their hands, two retrieval
teams - Zulu 9-A and Zulu 9-B - were dispatched

02:20:56.630 --> 02:21:01.910
to secure and contain the entity. Zulu 9-A
took the lead in a heavy duty chopper, equipped

02:21:01.910 --> 02:21:08.780
with .50 caliber GAU-19 Heavy Machine-Guns
and carrying an AT-4 Anti-Tank launcher. They

02:21:08.780 --> 02:21:14.370
were prepared for anything - or so they thought
- as they established a visual on SCP - 096

02:21:14.370 --> 02:21:16.870
while two clicks away from the target.

02:21:16.870 --> 02:21:21.490
They couldn’t get a clear line of sight
on the creature, but it appeared to be stationary,

02:21:21.490 --> 02:21:26.921
docile, and was making no attempt to flee.
Piece of cake, right? Little did they know

02:21:26.921 --> 02:21:32.720
that SCP - 096 was just looking away from
them. If it was facing towards them, it’d

02:21:32.720 --> 02:21:37.570
be a whole different horror story, as Zulu
9-A were about to find out.

02:21:37.570 --> 02:21:41.580
The team landed their helicopter next to the
creature and were shocked to see that it was

02:21:41.580 --> 02:21:46.160
completely naked, in spite of the subzero
temperatures all around them. The creature

02:21:46.160 --> 02:21:50.970
was unnaturally thin, as though it’d been
starved for weeks, with bone-white skin and

02:21:50.970 --> 02:21:55.530
unnaturally long limbs. The team guessed that
the creature’s arms must have been at least

02:21:55.530 --> 02:22:00.800
1.5 metres long, but its docile nature and
insubstantial body mass gave the impression

02:22:00.800 --> 02:22:06.200
that it wouldn’t prove too difficult to
contain. That is, until they saw its face.

02:22:06.200 --> 02:22:10.790
Zulu 9-A’s Captain was the lone survivor
of the incident, as he was lucky enough to

02:22:10.790 --> 02:22:15.500
be looking away when the creature turned towards
his team. The rest of the squad ended up staring

02:22:15.500 --> 02:22:22.210
eye to eye with SCP - 096, and from that moment
on it wasn’t docile anymore. The creature

02:22:22.210 --> 02:22:28.860
began to whimper, then cry, then sob uncontrollably
in a way that sounded eerily human. This sudden

02:22:28.860 --> 02:22:33.650
change in temperament startled the rest of
Zulu 9-A and they opened fire on the creature.

02:22:33.650 --> 02:22:39.220
Under the hail of gunfire, SCP - 096 entered
a murderous frenzy and began tearing into

02:22:39.220 --> 02:22:43.950
the hapless squad of soldiers. While its flesh
and organs did seem to take damage as a result

02:22:43.950 --> 02:22:49.160
of the barrage of .50 caliber rounds from
the helicopter mounted machine guns, its skeletal

02:22:49.160 --> 02:22:54.330
structure remained intact and it continued
its onslaught, tearing the team limb from

02:22:54.330 --> 02:22:59.000
limb even after they’d blown practically
all the flesh from the creature.

02:22:59.000 --> 02:23:03.690
The AT-4 Anti-Tank launcher proved equally
ineffective at stopping SCP - 096 while it

02:23:03.690 --> 02:23:08.730
was in attack mode, and it was only after
slaughtering the entire team that it returned

02:23:08.730 --> 02:23:13.420
to its docile state. Nobody knows exactly
what the creature did to Zulu 9-A after the

02:23:13.420 --> 02:23:17.771
gunfire started, but no trace of the team
was left behind.

02:23:17.771 --> 02:23:22.500
Zulu 9-B touched down soon after, and with
a grave warning from the Captain not to look

02:23:22.500 --> 02:23:27.670
at the creature’s face, they were finally
able to subdue it. A bag was placed over SCP

02:23:27.670 --> 02:23:33.150
- 096’s face, which seemed to soothe it
enough to move it to a nearby Foundation facility.

02:23:33.150 --> 02:23:37.601
Little did they know, they’d just obtained
one of the deadliest SCPs of all time, and

02:23:37.601 --> 02:23:41.851
while it may have been under lock and key
for now, it seems inevitable that it would

02:23:41.851 --> 02:23:45.080
get out and cause more violence and chaos.

02:23:45.080 --> 02:23:49.210
Research and containment procedures for the
SCP - 096 were put under the command of Dr.

02:23:49.210 --> 02:23:54.001
Dan, a senior researcher at the site. It was
his job to find out exactly what this being

02:23:54.001 --> 02:23:58.960
was capable of, and the more he tested, the
more he realized that they were dealing with

02:23:58.960 --> 02:24:01.601
something truly terrifying.

02:24:01.601 --> 02:24:05.230
Disposable D-Class personnel were used to
figure out exactly what it was that caused

02:24:05.230 --> 02:24:10.271
the creature to enter its attack mode. Just
as it had during the initial retrieval mission,

02:24:10.271 --> 02:24:16.210
SCP - 096 went berserk when any of the attending
personnel saw its face. In this stage, it

02:24:16.210 --> 02:24:21.540
would enter a period of considerable and unstoppable
distress for one to two minutes - covering

02:24:21.540 --> 02:24:26.500
its face and wailing loudly. When the period
of distress ended, the creature would mercilessly

02:24:26.500 --> 02:24:32.041
slaughter every D-Class that had seen its
face, and just like with Zulu 9-A, no trace

02:24:32.041 --> 02:24:34.580
of their bodies would be left behind.

02:24:34.580 --> 02:24:39.550
Dr. Dan was horrified and intrigued by this
phenomenon. The creature killed anyone that

02:24:39.550 --> 02:24:44.300
saw its face directly, but could the same
be said for indirect depictions of the creature’s

02:24:44.300 --> 02:24:49.420
face - such as images and videos? Dr. Dan
was desperate to find out.

02:24:49.420 --> 02:24:54.580
More D-Class personnel were brought in to
test this, to frightening results. Dr. Dan

02:24:54.580 --> 02:24:58.800
found that the creature did indeed still enter
attack mode when people saw pictures and videos

02:24:58.800 --> 02:25:03.990
of SCP - 096’s face. The creature seemed
to have an innate sense of when people were

02:25:03.990 --> 02:25:08.551
viewing these representations even when it
should have had no conceivable way of knowing.

02:25:08.551 --> 02:25:12.670
It didn’t matter how far away or how many
barriers were in place between the viewer

02:25:12.670 --> 02:25:18.030
and the creature, the attack mode would still
activate. And once it did, it seemed as though

02:25:18.030 --> 02:25:22.040
nothing could stop the creature from hunting
down the one who saw its face.

02:25:22.040 --> 02:25:26.670
With all of this new data, special containment
procedures were devised to keep the creature

02:25:26.670 --> 02:25:33.760
safely under lock and key. Its cell was a
5 m x 5 m x 5 m airtight steel cube, fitted

02:25:33.760 --> 02:25:39.950
with advanced pressure sensors and laser detectors
to ensure that SCP - 096 remained in its cell

02:25:39.950 --> 02:25:44.570
without risking anyone having visual contact
with the creature’s face. All cameras and

02:25:44.570 --> 02:25:48.840
video equipment were strictly forbidden, and
weekly checks for any cracks or holes in the

02:25:48.840 --> 02:25:53.530
containment cell were mandatory. Of course,
none of this would stop the creature if anyone

02:25:53.530 --> 02:25:59.120
somehow saw its face. In order to solve that
little problem, Dr. Dan would need to continue

02:25:59.120 --> 02:26:01.090
his research.

02:26:01.090 --> 02:26:05.420
To find a method of subverting the creature’s
deadly glance, they needed to know exactly

02:26:05.420 --> 02:26:10.540
what they were dealing with - but how could
they, when even a glance at a photo or video

02:26:10.540 --> 02:26:16.040
of the being meant certain death? A potential
solution was proposed - creating an artistic

02:26:16.040 --> 02:26:20.540
representation of the creature’s face, something
that hadn’t yet been attempted. But how

02:26:20.540 --> 02:26:25.540
would they achieve such a feat? Simple - they’d
procure a D-Class prisoner with some artistic

02:26:25.540 --> 02:26:29.710
talent, and they found one who had been a
tattoo artist before becoming a Foundation

02:26:29.710 --> 02:26:30.710
guinea pig.

02:26:30.710 --> 02:26:36.380
Dr. Dan formulated an ingenious plan for keeping
this D-Class alive for long enough to accurately

02:26:36.380 --> 02:26:42.450
draw an image of SCP - 096’s face: He would
be placed in a Bathysphere diving bell several

02:26:42.450 --> 02:26:47.490
kilometers underwater, and tens of kilometers
away from the containment cell where the SCP

02:26:47.490 --> 02:26:52.080
was being held. The D-Class was made to look
at a photograph of the creature’s face,

02:26:52.080 --> 02:26:57.230
and then replicate that image in a pencil
sketch. Dr. Dan first confirmed that the creature’s

02:26:57.230 --> 02:27:01.730
attack mode is only activated by the creature’s
face by having the D-Class look at a series

02:27:01.730 --> 02:27:07.540
of photos of the SCP’s body parts one by
one, finally finishing with its face. The

02:27:07.540 --> 02:27:12.671
D-Class began drawing and even remarked on
how creepy the SCP’s facial features were,

02:27:12.671 --> 02:27:15.120
despite not knowing the deadly context.

02:27:15.120 --> 02:27:21.050
Meanwhile, back in its containment cell SCP
- 096 sensed someone viewing its face, and

02:27:21.050 --> 02:27:25.811
entered its inconsolable crying state followed
by its attack mode. It broke out of containment

02:27:25.811 --> 02:27:30.540
easily, and began making a beeline for the
D-Class, traversing the miles between it and

02:27:30.540 --> 02:27:35.240
its prey. The D-Class didn’t know it as
he locked the finished drawing into a separate,

02:27:35.240 --> 02:27:40.142
autonomous submersible, but he was already
dead. As the drawing made its way up to a

02:27:40.142 --> 02:27:45.250
researcher on the surface, SCP - 096 dived
into the water, and started swimming down

02:27:45.250 --> 02:27:52.940
towards the artist. Minutes later, the bathysphere
was breached, and the D-Class was torn to

02:27:52.940 --> 02:27:53.940
shreds.

02:27:53.940 --> 02:27:59.090
SCP - 096 was recaptured without issue by
surface recovery team Foxtrot-303-A, and further

02:27:59.090 --> 02:28:03.800
testing on the drawing showed that artistic
representations of SCP - 096’s face were

02:28:03.800 --> 02:28:08.690
in fact harmless. From this experience, we
now know that the creature has a gaunt face

02:28:08.690 --> 02:28:14.530
with totally white eyes, possibly indicating
blindness, and a grossly extended jaw. Nevertheless,

02:28:14.530 --> 02:28:20.040
Dr. Dan was adamant that SCP - 096 was too
dangerous to be left alive, and requested

02:28:20.040 --> 02:28:24.030
permission from the upper echelons of the
Foundation to terminate the creature by any

02:28:24.030 --> 02:28:29.790
means necessary. However, the doctor’s request
would fall on deaf ears, until...

02:28:29.790 --> 02:28:33.591
It all started with a seemingly innocent image.
(Use this image: http://scp-wiki.wdfiles.com/local--files/incident-096-1-a/G9zmJ.jpg)

02:28:33.591 --> 02:28:37.820
While it’s now been redacted for your safety,
the black spec inside the yellow circle was

02:28:37.820 --> 02:28:44.990
once a minuscule image of SCP - 096, taken
unknowingly in the 1990s by a semi-professional

02:28:44.990 --> 02:28:48.460
mountaineer. One day, they were looking at
old photographs when his eyes passed over

02:28:48.460 --> 02:28:54.960
the tiny spec without even noticing he had
seen anything. But SCP - 096 noticed, and

02:28:54.960 --> 02:28:57.101
began entering its attack mode.

02:28:57.101 --> 02:29:00.900
It tore through its steel containment unit
like tissue paper, causing the release of

02:29:00.900 --> 02:29:05.210
a nerve agent that killed a number of attending
Foundation staff. The monster then fled the

02:29:05.210 --> 02:29:10.771
base and began pursuing its prey, with Mobile
Task Force Tau-1 in hot pursuit. Dr. Oleksei,

02:29:10.771 --> 02:29:14.950
who was helping to manage the site where the
SCP was contained, was in dismay over the

02:29:14.950 --> 02:29:19.160
situation. Dr. Dan was out of the country
at the time, trying to discover more about

02:29:19.160 --> 02:29:23.690
the creature’s origins. However, he did
leave the Mobile Task Force with a new secret

02:29:23.690 --> 02:29:27.900
weapon against the rampaging Shy Guy… Project
SCRAMBLE.

02:29:27.900 --> 02:29:32.131
SCRAMBLE were state of the art goggles featuring
a new technology created by Dr. Dan, which

02:29:32.131 --> 02:29:37.250
- using artistic renditions of 096’s facial
features - could detect and scramble the features

02:29:37.250 --> 02:29:43.210
of SCP - 096 into an unrecognizable form,
preventing the normally deadly effect of gazing

02:29:43.210 --> 02:29:49.750
upon on its face. In theory, this would allow
MTF Tau-1 to engage safely with 096 once its

02:29:49.750 --> 02:29:54.870
prey had been eliminated and bring it back
into containment. But disaster struck on two

02:29:54.870 --> 02:29:59.920
fronts. First, the prey in question was located
in a population center, creating the potential

02:29:59.920 --> 02:30:01.431
for a huge loss of life.

02:30:01.431 --> 02:30:06.070
And the second bigger problem was that the
SCRAMBLE technology didn’t work, as stray

02:30:06.070 --> 02:30:09.860
pixels of the creature’s face would reach
the eyes of the task force before the internal

02:30:09.860 --> 02:30:14.690
microprocessor had time to scramble them.
The mission turned into a death sentence,

02:30:14.690 --> 02:30:20.080
as SCP - 096 slaughtered almost the entire
task force, as well as a number of civilians

02:30:20.080 --> 02:30:26.110
in town - including an infant and its entire
family. It was a monumental disaster, made

02:30:26.110 --> 02:30:31.290
even worse by a final revelation: Dr. Dan
and Dr. Oleksei had themselves facilitated

02:30:31.290 --> 02:30:36.190
the entire containment breach and allowed
the resulting massacre to happen, with Dr.

02:30:36.190 --> 02:30:40.630
Dan hoping it would be enough motivation for
Foundation Command to green-light his research

02:30:40.630 --> 02:30:43.011
into destroying the creature.

02:30:43.011 --> 02:30:47.290
Anything that would give him the opportunity
to kill this thing would be worth the bloodshed.

02:30:47.290 --> 02:30:54.410
His plan worked and the SCP Foundation saw
it his way, approving his request to neutralize

02:30:54.410 --> 02:30:59.610
SCP - 096. However, success comes at a cost
for Dr. Dan. Once he figures out a way to

02:30:59.610 --> 02:31:04.891
finally kill the creature, though done in
the line of duty, he himself will be terminated

02:31:04.891 --> 02:31:08.101
by the Foundation for his crimes against humanity.

02:31:08.101 --> 02:31:12.891
But considering how much damage SCP - 096
is capable of causing if it ever got to a

02:31:12.891 --> 02:31:18.101
major population center, or - even worse - was
ever caught on camera and broadcast to a worldwide

02:31:18.101 --> 02:31:23.780
audience, the doctor himself would likely
deem his own death a justifiable cost. To

02:31:23.780 --> 02:31:27.811
this day, the Foundation is researching ways
to kill the creature, and they’re still

02:31:27.811 --> 02:31:32.830
looking for their silver bullet. And the pressure
is on. They hadn’t known about the seemingly

02:31:32.830 --> 02:31:38.010
innocent picture that sparked the last containment
breach. The one taken decades ago, in which

02:31:38.010 --> 02:31:44.040
the Shy Guy had only occupied four tiny pixels.
Four tiny pixels that resulted in multiple

02:31:44.040 --> 02:31:46.720
innocent lives lost.

02:31:46.720 --> 02:31:51.351
So be careful where you look because who knows
how many other photos of the creature are

02:31:51.351 --> 02:31:55.960
lurking out there, photos with an innocent
dot in the background. Your eyes glance over

02:31:55.960 --> 02:32:01.540
it, not even noticing the little blip, until
you hear a distant wailing that seems to be

02:32:01.540 --> 02:32:11.110
getting closer, and closer, and closer. And
then... it’s already too late.

02:32:11.110 --> 02:32:15.630
The SCP Foundation does their best to live
up to their famous namesake: They secure and

02:32:15.630 --> 02:32:21.050
contain anomalies and monsters from all around
the world - or sometimes even off-world - and

02:32:21.050 --> 02:32:25.561
protect the public from the dangers that these
strange entities might pose.

02:32:25.561 --> 02:32:29.960
However, despite their efforts to maintain
security and keep their subjects under lock

02:32:29.960 --> 02:32:35.950
and key, there are sometimes creatures so
clever, so devious, and so determined to escape

02:32:35.950 --> 02:32:40.820
their captivity and wreak havoc on the world,
that even the SCP foundation struggles to

02:32:40.820 --> 02:32:43.030
keep them from getting free.

02:32:43.030 --> 02:32:48.580
One example is SCP-035, or the Possessive
Mask.

02:32:48.580 --> 02:32:54.260
SCP-035 is one of the most dangerous test
subjects in SCP Foundation custody, and its

02:32:54.260 --> 02:33:00.380
mere presence at the Foundation has resulted
in untold damage, death, and destruction.

02:33:00.380 --> 02:33:03.040
It seems innocent enough, to the untrained
eye.

02:33:03.040 --> 02:33:07.561
The mask, which resembles a classic white
porcelain “comedy” mask - though it occasionally

02:33:07.561 --> 02:33:12.811
changes its expression to “tragedy” - has
been in existence since at least the 1800s.

02:33:12.811 --> 02:33:18.251
In the late 19th century the Foundation discovered
the mask in a sealed crypt beneath an abandoned

02:33:18.251 --> 02:33:19.580
home in Venice.

02:33:19.580 --> 02:33:23.160
It is unknown how it got there, or how the
Foundation knew to look for it.

02:33:23.160 --> 02:33:28.170
If there ever was an explanation for its discovery,
it has long since been removed or redacted

02:33:28.170 --> 02:33:30.010
from the Foundation’s archives.

02:33:30.010 --> 02:33:34.800
You’re probably wondering: How can a simple
mask leave multiple seasoned Foundation employees

02:33:34.800 --> 02:33:35.800
dead?

02:33:35.800 --> 02:33:39.931
Well, like everything at the SCP foundation,
this mask is not what it seems.

02:33:39.931 --> 02:33:45.271
There is a reason its classification is “keter”,
a designation that refers to an entity that’s

02:33:45.271 --> 02:33:49.290
excessively difficult to contain - and it
couples this difficulty with a pronounced

02:33:49.290 --> 02:33:53.941
hostility toward human life, and the ability
to cause widespread destruction in the event

02:33:53.941 --> 02:33:55.610
of a containment breach.

02:33:55.610 --> 02:34:01.501
These are qualities that the poor unfortunate
souls assigned to guard SCP-035 would come

02:34:01.501 --> 02:34:03.771
to understand all too well.

02:34:03.771 --> 02:34:08.650
The Possessive Mask is a parasitic entity,
constantly seeking out a host willing to put

02:34:08.650 --> 02:34:09.650
it on.

02:34:09.650 --> 02:34:14.351
Any human being in the mask’s proximity
experiences a sudden, unexplainable urge to

02:34:14.351 --> 02:34:16.971
put it on and once they do, there’s no going
back.

02:34:16.971 --> 02:34:23.030
SCP Foundation research has determined that
once a host has put on the mask, their brain

02:34:23.030 --> 02:34:27.960
waves are replaced with an alternative pattern,
this one coming from the mask, rendering the

02:34:27.960 --> 02:34:30.180
host effectively brain dead.

02:34:30.180 --> 02:34:34.480
Once the host’s brain function has been
eliminated, the mask takes over, piloting

02:34:34.480 --> 02:34:36.540
their body and even speaking through them.

02:34:36.540 --> 02:34:40.910
However, the mask can only occupy a host for
a small amount of time before the body begins

02:34:40.910 --> 02:34:46.380
to decay and decompose, eventually rotting
away completely, leaving nothing but desiccated

02:34:46.380 --> 02:34:50.521
flesh and bones where there once was a person.

02:34:50.521 --> 02:34:55.500
SCP-035 is capable of possessing any humanoid
being, whether that’s an actual human being

02:34:55.500 --> 02:34:58.190
or a lifeless humanoid shape.

02:34:58.190 --> 02:35:03.360
Despite all their research, the SCP Foundation
unknowingly gave the Mask all the tools and

02:35:03.360 --> 02:35:09.460
resources it needed to break containment...
and leave a trail of bodies in its wake.

02:35:09.460 --> 02:35:14.561
For a time, the mask was given “host privileges,”
meaning that it was purposely allowed to occupy

02:35:14.561 --> 02:35:17.840
a host in order to speak with the scientists
studying it.

02:35:17.840 --> 02:35:21.760
In order to avoid murky ethical issues, the
host was usually something inanimate like

02:35:21.760 --> 02:35:23.730
a mannequin or a statue.

02:35:23.730 --> 02:35:27.800
These conditions, however unsettling, allowed
the researchers to carry out interviews with

02:35:27.800 --> 02:35:32.021
the consciousness housed inside the mask,
in the hope of beginning to understand it

02:35:32.021 --> 02:35:33.950
and its motivations.

02:35:33.950 --> 02:35:40.501
However, SCP-035 lost all access to its host
privileges after it almost pulled off an unprecedented,

02:35:40.501 --> 02:35:44.530
shocking, and nearly catastrophic escape attempt.

02:35:44.530 --> 02:35:48.540
In its early days at the facility, when it
was still allowed host privileges, it was

02:35:48.540 --> 02:35:53.030
contained in a triple locked room and monitored
by several research personnel.

02:35:53.030 --> 02:35:56.521
These were experienced researchers who had
been with the Foundation for a minimum of

02:35:56.521 --> 02:36:01.430
five years each, an unusually long tenure
in such a dangerous and mentally corrosive

02:36:01.430 --> 02:36:02.690
line of work.

02:36:02.690 --> 02:36:06.550
These research staff members were thought
to be the most capable of handling interactions

02:36:06.550 --> 02:36:10.561
with the mask, and be able to resist its attempts
at manipulation.

02:36:10.561 --> 02:36:16.400
Unfortunately, these assumptions were naive,
and seriously underestimated the mask’s

02:36:16.400 --> 02:36:17.400
power.

02:36:17.400 --> 02:36:21.851
Research on the mask indicates that the mask
is incredibly intelligent and a skilled manipulator.

02:36:21.851 --> 02:36:26.551
It has a photographic memory, intelligence
that would rank in the 99th percentile of

02:36:26.551 --> 02:36:31.460
humans, and the ability to incite dramatic
changes in the behavior in people that it

02:36:31.460 --> 02:36:32.460
talks to.

02:36:32.460 --> 02:36:38.160
One particularly infamous interview, between
the entity and an unnamed Doctor at the Foundation,

02:36:38.160 --> 02:36:41.690
suggested that the mask may even possess telepathic
abilities.

02:36:41.690 --> 02:36:45.570
The mask was able to give details about the
Doctor’s life that no one else was privy

02:36:45.570 --> 02:36:49.580
to, including knowledge of an affair that
his wife was having.

02:36:49.580 --> 02:36:53.721
Following the interview, the Doctor suffered
a psychotic break and committed suicide just

02:36:53.721 --> 02:36:55.200
24 hours later.

02:36:55.200 --> 02:37:00.420
The mask is able to use its superior intelligence,
charismatic personality, and mind reading

02:37:00.420 --> 02:37:03.740
abilities to get inside the heads of those
it speaks with.

02:37:03.740 --> 02:37:09.090
It will pull out any and all psychological
stops to get what it wants, leaving broken

02:37:09.090 --> 02:37:11.771
minds and spirits in its wake.

02:37:11.771 --> 02:37:16.660
It was really only a matter of time before
it used this skill set to its advantage and

02:37:16.660 --> 02:37:18.700
attempted to escape its confinement.

02:37:18.700 --> 02:37:21.750
The day of the escape attempt was like any
other.

02:37:21.750 --> 02:37:26.771
The research staff, a team of three intelligent,
experienced men, checked into the facility,

02:37:26.771 --> 02:37:30.690
measured the conditions of the mask’s containment
unit, and began the process of interviewing

02:37:30.690 --> 02:37:32.521
the mask like normal.

02:37:32.521 --> 02:37:36.960
Its motions were slow and looked to require
great effort, as its current host was beginning

02:37:36.960 --> 02:37:39.170
to degrade beyond use.

02:37:39.170 --> 02:37:43.380
The mask was attached to the blank face of
a mannequin, and corrosive black liquid could

02:37:43.380 --> 02:37:46.230
be seen oozing from its eye and mouth holes.

02:37:46.230 --> 02:37:51.420
This liquid is excreted by the mask at a near-constant
rate, and is thought to be at least partially

02:37:51.420 --> 02:37:54.851
responsible for the accelerated decay of the
host bodies.

02:37:54.851 --> 02:37:59.611
In spite of the entity’s unsettling, nightmarish
appearance, it was just another day’s work

02:37:59.611 --> 02:38:06.790
for the men assigned to monitor SCP-035, and
so they carried on with their daily routine.

02:38:06.790 --> 02:38:11.021
Everything was going according to plan until
one of the men, Dr. Jones, began to behave

02:38:11.021 --> 02:38:12.021
erratically.

02:38:12.021 --> 02:38:15.501
He demanded that his fellow scientists leave
him alone with the mask for a while, and allow

02:38:15.501 --> 02:38:18.590
him to engage in a private conversation with
it.

02:38:18.590 --> 02:38:23.080
It is unknown what exactly the two spoke about
while the other two scientists were absent,

02:38:23.080 --> 02:38:25.820
as the security footage captured has no sound.

02:38:25.820 --> 02:38:30.391
However, several minutes into the conversation
in the footage, Dr. Jones can be seen dissolving

02:38:30.391 --> 02:38:36.000
into a fit of tears, laying on the ground
and shaking with sobs as the mask dispassionately

02:38:36.000 --> 02:38:37.000
watches.

02:38:37.000 --> 02:38:42.331
He then climbs onto his knees, begging the
mask for something, before he embraces it.

02:38:42.331 --> 02:38:48.050
He holds the mannequin in his arms for five
straight minutes, weeping again, before they

02:38:48.050 --> 02:38:49.050
separate.

02:38:49.050 --> 02:38:53.210
After this disturbing emotional display, Dr.
Jones brought the other scientists back into

02:38:53.210 --> 02:38:55.170
the room with him.

02:38:55.170 --> 02:38:59.490
What happened next is still uncertain, but
there are a few things that we know for sure.

02:38:59.490 --> 02:39:01.540
The other scientists began to speak with the
mask.

02:39:01.540 --> 02:39:06.010
In later interviews, the other scientists
were bordering on incoherent, babbling about

02:39:06.010 --> 02:39:08.090
various traumas from their lives.

02:39:08.090 --> 02:39:12.110
One repeatedly referred to a drunk driving
accident where a dear friend was killed, and

02:39:12.110 --> 02:39:13.730
he was at fault.

02:39:13.730 --> 02:39:16.620
Another simply cried out for his mother again
and again.

02:39:16.620 --> 02:39:21.800
Whatever the mask said to them, it was enough
to completely destroy their mental health.

02:39:21.800 --> 02:39:26.420
After the other two scientists had been emotionally
devastated by the mask, Dr. Jones escalated

02:39:26.420 --> 02:39:28.040
the situation further.

02:39:28.040 --> 02:39:33.340
Dr. Jones removed the mask from the decaying
mannequin body, and, shocking everyone who

02:39:33.340 --> 02:39:38.500
would later review the security footage, placed
it onto his own face.

02:39:38.500 --> 02:39:39.760
Once the mask was in place, Dr. Jones went
unnaturally still for several moments, as

02:39:39.760 --> 02:39:40.760
his colleagues looked on.

02:39:40.760 --> 02:39:41.760
This is where the security footage ends.

02:39:41.760 --> 02:39:46.170
At the command of the mask which was now speaking
through Dr. Jones, the other two men switched

02:39:46.170 --> 02:39:50.230
off all security cameras monitoring SCP-035’s
containment facility.

02:39:50.230 --> 02:39:56.430
The mask, piloting the body of Dr. Jones like
a horrible fleshy puppet, made its way through

02:39:56.430 --> 02:40:01.170
the facility, avoiding detection until it
reached the exit doors, where it was finally

02:40:01.170 --> 02:40:04.620
stopped by a team of over a dozen security
guards.

02:40:04.620 --> 02:40:08.710
Knowing the dangers of touching the mask,
all Foundation employees involved in the re-containment

02:40:08.710 --> 02:40:12.831
of SCP-035 refused to remove it from Dr. Jones’
face.

02:40:12.831 --> 02:40:17.610
Instead, he was placed in the locked room
with the mask still on, left alone to be observed

02:40:17.610 --> 02:40:21.830
over the security cameras until his body had
decomposed beyond use.

02:40:21.830 --> 02:40:26.860
His body paced back and forth in its cell
for days, flesh rotting and dropping away

02:40:26.860 --> 02:40:29.500
until only sinew and bone remained.

02:40:29.500 --> 02:40:34.080
Only when the bones began to turn black and
brittle, crumbling apart into dust, did the

02:40:34.080 --> 02:40:36.140
body finally stop moving.

02:40:36.140 --> 02:40:40.870
His family was notified, the mask was carefully
removed from what was left of his body, and

02:40:40.870 --> 02:40:42.820
his remains were destroyed.

02:40:42.820 --> 02:40:47.921
The other two scientists involved in the SCP-035
escape attempt were terminated, and their

02:40:47.921 --> 02:40:49.420
files destroyed.

02:40:49.420 --> 02:40:53.900
After this incident, a few more failed escape
attempts, and the acknowledgement of the devastation

02:40:53.900 --> 02:40:58.650
that could have been caused if the mask had
made its way out into the general population,

02:40:58.650 --> 02:41:02.590
SCP-035 lost its host privileges altogether.

02:41:02.590 --> 02:41:06.500
Several research staff protested this decision,
insisting that there was more to be learned

02:41:06.500 --> 02:41:10.920
from speaking with the entity, and citing
valuable information that it had given about

02:41:10.920 --> 02:41:11.960
other SCP’s.

02:41:11.960 --> 02:41:16.911
However, the risk was determined to considerably
outweigh the potential reward, and the request

02:41:16.911 --> 02:41:20.980
to reinstate 035’s host privileges was denied.

02:41:20.980 --> 02:41:26.500
Several staff members went so far as to erupt
into violent outbursts on 035’s behalf,

02:41:26.500 --> 02:41:31.021
attacking their superiors who refused to provide
the mask with a new host, clawing at them

02:41:31.021 --> 02:41:33.090
with animalistic rage.

02:41:33.090 --> 02:41:37.160
Any staff members that submitted a request
to reinstate said privileges were considered

02:41:37.160 --> 02:41:43.130
a security threat, and reassigned to a different
SCP or in some cases terminated.

02:41:43.130 --> 02:41:48.660
Any staff member who had direct contact with
SCP-035 was also terminated, in order to avoid

02:41:48.660 --> 02:41:52.051
the risk of any more staff-aided escape attempts.

02:41:52.051 --> 02:41:56.431
The mask is now kept in a hermetically-sealed
glass case, and there is a psychologist on

02:41:56.431 --> 02:42:01.001
call to provide assistance to anyone guarding
it, in case of adverse effects on their mental

02:42:01.001 --> 02:42:03.570
health from the mask’s presence.

02:42:03.570 --> 02:42:07.780
Personnel that work around the mask, even
in its current dormant state, experience frequent

02:42:07.780 --> 02:42:11.120
violent outbursts and a higher rate of suicide.

02:42:11.120 --> 02:42:15.221
Even without a host, the mask’s corrosive
effects have spread across its containment

02:42:15.221 --> 02:42:16.240
facility.

02:42:16.240 --> 02:42:20.561
The walls of the room have begun to secrete
the same black liquid that emanates from the

02:42:20.561 --> 02:42:25.090
mask, which tests have revealed to be highly
contaminated human blood, that damages the

02:42:25.090 --> 02:42:29.000
structural integrity of the walls following
prolonged contact.

02:42:29.000 --> 02:42:34.220
This blood has begun to form patterns on the
walls, spelling out words and phrases in Italian,

02:42:34.220 --> 02:42:40.820
Latin, Greek, and Sanskrit, as well as depicting
drawings of ritual sacrifice and mutilation.

02:42:40.820 --> 02:42:45.200
Staff members also report hearing unintelligible
whispering and horrifying, high-pitched laughter

02:42:45.200 --> 02:42:47.590
when in proximity to the mask.

02:42:47.590 --> 02:42:52.791
Further exposure to the mask results in migraines,
hemorrhaging around the eyes, mouth, and nose,

02:42:52.791 --> 02:42:55.380
and an eventual psychotic break.

02:42:55.380 --> 02:42:59.051
Between the corrosive substance appearing
on the walls, and the physical and psychological

02:42:59.051 --> 02:43:05.900
damage to employees, SCP-035 is becoming increasingly
difficult to contain and there are debates

02:43:05.900 --> 02:43:11.090
among staff as to whether the entity can,
in fact, be contained at all.

02:43:11.090 --> 02:43:16.660
As soon as possible, SCP-035 will be moved
into a new containment facility, and its previous

02:43:16.660 --> 02:43:20.390
cell will be isolated from the rest of the
foundation’s property and destroyed for

02:43:20.390 --> 02:43:21.601
the safety of all involved.

02:43:21.601 --> 02:43:25.681
We can only hope that the new containment
procedures are more effective than the last

02:43:25.681 --> 02:43:29.851
ones, and that this mask never makes its way
into the world again.

02:43:29.851 --> 02:43:33.940
If it does, who knows how many lives it will
claim?

02:43:33.940 --> 02:43:38.570
In the meantime, if you ever come across a
strange mask and feel a nearly uncontrollable

02:43:38.570 --> 02:43:43.870
urge to put it on…ignore the whispered pleas
to just try it, ignore the echoing laugher

02:43:43.870 --> 02:43:48.780
and the sensation of something older and more
powerful than you can imagine rummaging through

02:43:48.780 --> 02:43:51.840
your deepest, darkest secret thoughts.

02:43:51.840 --> 02:43:57.240
Turn around, and run as fast as you can in
the other direction.

02:43:57.240 --> 02:43:58.760
You’ll be glad that you did.

02:43:58.760 --> 02:44:01.891
It’s 3:00 AM, and the facility is quiet.

02:44:01.891 --> 02:44:04.420
Office workers and administrators roam the
halls.

02:44:04.420 --> 02:44:09.240
Security Officers stand at their posts, clad
in advanced tactical armour and carrying standard-issue

02:44:09.240 --> 02:44:10.391
M4 Carbines.

02:44:10.391 --> 02:44:14.210
Three Foundation employees sit at flickering
monitors, watching a live feed of footage

02:44:14.210 --> 02:44:19.790
from the containment cell of the infamous
SCP-106, or as it’s referred to by staff,

02:44:19.790 --> 02:44:20.820
The Old Man.

02:44:20.820 --> 02:44:25.271
No Foundation personnel are permitted to travel
within sixty feet of the cell for security

02:44:25.271 --> 02:44:29.320
reasons, and nobody is permitted to physically
interact with the anomaly without the approval

02:44:29.320 --> 02:44:31.660
of two-thirds of O5-Command.

02:44:31.660 --> 02:44:36.110
The observer’s eyes itch and sting from
the hours of unending blue-light exposure,

02:44:36.110 --> 02:44:37.620
but they can’t look away.

02:44:37.620 --> 02:44:41.960
The Old Man is crafty – he may have the
insatiable bloodlust of a hungry great white

02:44:41.960 --> 02:44:43.190
shark, but he’s not mindless.

02:44:43.190 --> 02:44:48.011
He’s a calculating predator, more sadistic
than the worst human serial killer, and he’s

02:44:48.011 --> 02:44:50.120
always searching for the next opportunity.

02:44:50.120 --> 02:44:53.931
According to Foundation records, he’s been
active since at least World War II, and it

02:44:53.931 --> 02:44:57.590
is estimated that he has hundreds if not thousands
of victims to his name.

02:44:57.590 --> 02:45:02.440
And many of those made the simple, but extremely
foolish mistake of underestimating him.

02:45:02.440 --> 02:45:07.171
After all, it only takes a few seconds of
inattentiveness, the briefest moment of distraction,

02:45:07.171 --> 02:45:08.780
to give him the window he needs.

02:45:08.780 --> 02:45:10.290
To do what, you ask?

02:45:10.290 --> 02:45:13.430
Oh, don’t worry, you’ll find out – just
like they did.

02:45:13.430 --> 02:45:18.521
The Old Man has his nickname for a reason
– most of the time, he really does look

02:45:18.521 --> 02:45:20.101
like exactly that - an old man.

02:45:20.101 --> 02:45:25.280
Or more specifically, an Old Man’s decaying
corpse, his body covered in rotten, dark greyish-black

02:45:25.280 --> 02:45:27.630
flesh that looks like putrid meat.

02:45:27.630 --> 02:45:31.630
Though the creature has been observed being
able to change shape, the rot seems to run

02:45:31.630 --> 02:45:34.311
too deep for the Old Man to ever hide it.

02:45:34.311 --> 02:45:38.860
Foundation employees that have observed SCP-106
for extended periods of time have reported

02:45:38.860 --> 02:45:43.710
seeing it assume the form of grinning, decayed
children, and women whose rotted flesh barely

02:45:43.710 --> 02:45:45.690
hangs on to their creaking bones.

02:45:45.690 --> 02:45:49.980
Just seeing the images through a video feed
is enough to cause a lifetime of insomnia

02:45:49.980 --> 02:45:51.490
and other sleeping issues.

02:45:51.490 --> 02:45:55.010
Still, they have a job to do, and the cameras
remain fixed on the Old Man.

02:45:55.010 --> 02:45:59.131
He’s been completely motionless for three
months, just sitting there, like a Buddhist

02:45:59.131 --> 02:46:00.550
monk in deep meditation.

02:46:00.550 --> 02:46:04.591
A novice might see this period of inactivity
as a cause for celebration, but those with

02:46:04.591 --> 02:46:08.420
experience know that this is merely the calm
before the storm.

02:46:08.420 --> 02:46:12.261
SCP–106 can remain in a dormant state for
months at a time.

02:46:12.261 --> 02:46:16.150
Described by Foundation scientists as a “lulling
state,” it is believed that The Old Man

02:46:16.150 --> 02:46:20.630
is simply waiting for its captors to get soft,
make a mistake, or simply have a momentary

02:46:20.630 --> 02:46:24.050
lapse in concentration, which is all it needs
to make its move.

02:46:24.050 --> 02:46:27.930
It had happened so many times before, and
it was about to happen again.

02:46:27.930 --> 02:46:32.530
One of the observers must have felt an overwhelming
wave of anxiety when he saw the creature ever

02:46:32.530 --> 02:46:34.710
so slightly twitch.

02:46:34.710 --> 02:46:36.771
Just a tiny quiver in the shoulder muscles.

02:46:36.771 --> 02:46:40.960
But that was enough to tell the observer that
their day had just taken a terrifying turn.

02:46:40.960 --> 02:46:45.210
He grabbed the emergency phone fixed to his
desk and practically screamed into the receiver

02:46:45.210 --> 02:46:48.880
that 106 is moving, that they needed a tactical
team stat.

02:46:48.880 --> 02:46:49.880
But it was already too late.

02:46:49.880 --> 02:46:53.280
He and the two other observers stared into
the monitors with their mouths agape, as a

02:46:53.280 --> 02:46:58.330
gooey, rust-like substance began to pool around
the creature on the floor of its cell.

02:46:58.330 --> 02:47:00.930
Slowly, the creature craned its withered neck
around.

02:47:00.930 --> 02:47:04.641
Its face was fixed into a broad, yellow-toothed,
lipless grin.

02:47:04.641 --> 02:47:08.240
Its eyes had the kind of dull, flat malice
of an underwater predator.

02:47:08.240 --> 02:47:10.601
It looked directly into the camera.

02:47:10.601 --> 02:47:11.601
Directly at them.

02:47:11.601 --> 02:47:12.601
And smiled.

02:47:12.601 --> 02:47:14.420
The observers know this was bad.

02:47:14.420 --> 02:47:16.090
Really, really bad.

02:47:16.090 --> 02:47:20.910
With what they could have sworn was a little
nod, the Old Man began sinking into the rusty

02:47:20.910 --> 02:47:25.260
puddle it’d made on the ground beneath it,
until it had disappeared entirely.

02:47:25.260 --> 02:47:29.590
SCP–106 is capable of phasing through any
solid surface with ease, making it one of

02:47:29.590 --> 02:47:34.250
the hardest entities to reliably contain,
and earning it a spot on the dreaded “Keter”

02:47:34.250 --> 02:47:38.561
class – reserved for the anomalies that
are a complete nightmare to keep locked up.

02:47:38.561 --> 02:47:42.040
Through years of costly research and deadly
trial and error, the Foundation would later

02:47:42.040 --> 02:47:44.620
devise ways of at least slowing the creature
down.

02:47:44.620 --> 02:47:49.130
It’s shown to have an aversion to lead,
highly complex or random physical structures,

02:47:49.130 --> 02:47:50.890
and intense bright light.

02:47:50.890 --> 02:47:55.061
None of these cause harm to the creature – as
far as we know, literally nothing can – but

02:47:55.061 --> 02:48:00.591
they’ll at least buy you some precious extra
seconds with which to at least try and escape,

02:48:00.591 --> 02:48:02.860
seconds the three observers didn’t have.

02:48:02.860 --> 02:48:06.590
One of them grabbed the emergency line again
and barked into it that they had lost visual

02:48:06.590 --> 02:48:07.771
on the anomaly.

02:48:07.771 --> 02:48:12.601
Just then the observers heard a faint crackling
sound behind them, and the hissing of a chemical

02:48:12.601 --> 02:48:13.601
burn.

02:48:13.601 --> 02:48:17.432
They turned in horror to see a huge, rusty
burnmark expanding across the wall, right

02:48:17.432 --> 02:48:20.250
next to the door – which was their only
escape route.

02:48:20.250 --> 02:48:24.910
They backed as far away from the door as they
could as a rotten hand began reaching out

02:48:24.910 --> 02:48:30.780
of the mass of corrosive, black sludge, followed
by the grinning face of SCP–106, ready to

02:48:30.780 --> 02:48:31.780
have some fun.

02:48:31.780 --> 02:48:36.130
Meanwhile, two heavily-armed Security Officers
– Agents Goodwin and Resnick – came charging

02:48:36.130 --> 02:48:38.200
down the corridor towards the observation
rooms.

02:48:38.200 --> 02:48:42.950
It’d become a bleak slogan during SCP–106
escape attempts that all you need to do is

02:48:42.950 --> 02:48:43.950
“follow the screams.”

02:48:43.950 --> 02:48:47.591
And that motto was proven true that night,
because awful things were happening to the

02:48:47.591 --> 02:48:50.840
observation personnel, they were certainly
screaming about it.

02:48:50.840 --> 02:48:54.771
Of course, even with top-of-the-line firearms,
there was little they could do to harm the

02:48:54.771 --> 02:48:56.280
rampaging Old Man.

02:48:56.280 --> 02:48:58.820
He seemed immune to all forms of physical
damage.

02:48:58.820 --> 02:49:02.710
All they could hope to do was keep the thing
distracted until the scientists and containment

02:49:02.710 --> 02:49:07.210
specialists finished the preparations to lure
him back into his containment cell.

02:49:07.210 --> 02:49:10.040
Goodwin surged forward while Resnick covered
his six.

02:49:10.040 --> 02:49:14.940
Vigilance was key, as – unlike a standard
human combatant – SCP–106 could attack

02:49:14.940 --> 02:49:18.271
from literally any angle including above or
below.

02:49:18.271 --> 02:49:21.890
Physical obstacles were irrelevant to him
and no cover was safe.

02:49:21.890 --> 02:49:25.680
The hardened security officers could see the
burnmark on the wall of the observation room

02:49:25.680 --> 02:49:27.120
as they approached.

02:49:27.120 --> 02:49:32.190
SCP–106 was perpetually coated in a thick,
black mucus with powerful corrosive properties

02:49:32.190 --> 02:49:35.450
that left any surfaces it touched permanently
marred.

02:49:35.450 --> 02:49:39.530
Foundation Scientists speculated that this
mucus served as a kind of pre-digestive substance

02:49:39.530 --> 02:49:44.620
that tenderizes meat and bone alike, but to
what purpose this serves is a mystery as the

02:49:44.620 --> 02:49:46.410
Old Man has never been observed eating.

02:49:46.410 --> 02:49:50.210
It’s postulated that the only purpose is
causing additional pain.

02:49:50.210 --> 02:49:54.471
Goodwin and Resnick knew to treat this hissing
sludge as a potential threat, as the corrosive

02:49:54.471 --> 02:49:58.690
properties would remain active for as much
as six hours before finally fizzling out.

02:49:58.690 --> 02:50:03.330
The two officers shared a quiet nod, before
Goodwin breached the observation room door

02:50:03.330 --> 02:50:04.510
with a hard kick.

02:50:04.510 --> 02:50:07.181
The two of them surged inside, guns at the
ready.

02:50:07.181 --> 02:50:11.370
In their time working at the Foundation, they’d
seen some truly horrific sights.

02:50:11.370 --> 02:50:16.490
From the mutilation of D-Class Personnel – typically
death row prison inmates brought in for use

02:50:16.490 --> 02:50:20.500
as SCP guinea pigs – to the violence and
mayhem of a containment breach.

02:50:20.500 --> 02:50:24.061
But there was nothing in their past that would
ever make the horrifying sight they saw in

02:50:24.061 --> 02:50:26.980
the observation room that night feel “normal.”

02:50:26.980 --> 02:50:28.870
All three observers were dead.

02:50:28.870 --> 02:50:33.370
Almost nothing remained of two of them, and
the third, while still intact, no longer looked

02:50:33.370 --> 02:50:34.370
human.

02:50:34.370 --> 02:50:37.590
He looked like he’d somehow been dead a
hundred years in the brief period that the

02:50:37.590 --> 02:50:38.590
Old Man had been free.

02:50:38.590 --> 02:50:43.780
His skin was grey and completely dried out,
and his mouth was locked into a perpetual

02:50:43.780 --> 02:50:44.780
scream.

02:50:44.780 --> 02:50:47.090
It was a massacre, but there was no sign of
the Old Man.

02:50:47.090 --> 02:50:51.090
Goodwin grabbed his radio, and whispered “This
is Goodwin in observation room six.

02:50:51.090 --> 02:50:52.090
Requesting immediate back up.

02:50:52.090 --> 02:50:56.021
We have no idea where this thing—”
But his sentence was cut off by a sudden scream

02:50:56.021 --> 02:50:57.320
from Agent Resnick.

02:50:57.320 --> 02:51:01.670
SCP Foundation security officers are as tough
as nails – the best of the best, you might

02:51:01.670 --> 02:51:06.280
say, recruited from the top military organizations
in the world – so hearing one of them scream

02:51:06.280 --> 02:51:09.590
in fright is a rare if not impossible occurrence.

02:51:09.590 --> 02:51:13.720
But even they were forced to yell out in fear
when they looked up to see the Old Man standing

02:51:13.720 --> 02:51:15.830
on the ceiling, grinning down at them.

02:51:15.830 --> 02:51:20.040
Resnick raised his M4 and shot a three-round
burst at center mass.

02:51:20.040 --> 02:51:21.790
SCP–106 didn’t care.

02:51:21.790 --> 02:51:25.641
Even under sustained gunfire from the two
security officers, it didn’t even flinch.

02:51:25.641 --> 02:51:29.720
The Old Man simply reached down and snatched
Agent Resnick from the ground, like it was

02:51:29.720 --> 02:51:31.480
picking an apple from a tree.

02:51:31.480 --> 02:51:36.271
The Old Man held Resnick in one hand and pounded
its other rotten fist into the Agent’s body,

02:51:36.271 --> 02:51:37.771
breaking all of his bones.

02:51:37.771 --> 02:51:40.750
Resnick screamed for his partner to help him
but there was no time.

02:51:40.750 --> 02:51:46.040
Before Goodwin could do anything, SCP–106
began receding back into another slimy burnmark

02:51:46.040 --> 02:51:47.101
on the wall.

02:51:47.101 --> 02:51:50.230
Only this time, he was taking his screaming
victim with him.

02:51:50.230 --> 02:51:54.720
Agent Resnick gave one more horrified scream
before he was pulled backwards into the inky

02:51:54.720 --> 02:51:59.130
darkness leaving the room silent except for
the burning hiss of the corrosive goo left

02:51:59.130 --> 02:52:00.130
behind.

02:52:00.130 --> 02:52:02.540
You might think this would be the end of it,
but no.

02:52:02.540 --> 02:52:05.700
For poor Agent Resnick, the worst was yet
to come.

02:52:05.700 --> 02:52:10.670
He was being dragged into what SCP Foundation
scientists refer to as the Old Man’s “Pocket

02:52:10.670 --> 02:52:15.380
Dimension”, a miniature layer of reality
within our own where the malicious SCP is

02:52:15.380 --> 02:52:18.590
essentially a cruel, all-powerful God.

02:52:18.590 --> 02:52:22.910
According to witness reports extracted from
victims who were taken to this little nightmare

02:52:22.910 --> 02:52:27.250
realm, the dimension resembles a series of
twisting, endless corridors where the Old

02:52:27.250 --> 02:52:31.701
Man stalks and tortures his captured victims
to the breaking point, manipulating space

02:52:31.701 --> 02:52:34.140
and time to its own sadistic ends.

02:52:34.140 --> 02:52:38.870
On rare occasions, the SCP will even release
its victims, just for the joy of hunting,

02:52:38.870 --> 02:52:41.780
capturing, and torturing them all over again.

02:52:41.780 --> 02:52:45.890
While Agent Resnick was learning the true
meaning of terror, containment specialists

02:52:45.890 --> 02:52:50.690
were mobilizing in its cell, preparing the
one known tried-and-true method of luring

02:52:50.690 --> 02:52:55.150
the Old Man back: Tempting it with the prospect
of causing even more suffering.

02:52:55.150 --> 02:52:59.620
In order to do this, Foundation personnel
take one of the aforementioned Class D personnel

02:52:59.620 --> 02:53:05.470
and begin inducing extreme pain by breaking
a major bone or slicing a tendon every twenty

02:53:05.470 --> 02:53:06.470
minutes.

02:53:06.470 --> 02:53:10.470
The victim’s agonized screams are then played
over the facility’s intercom, acting as

02:53:10.470 --> 02:53:12.690
bait for the pain-loving Old Man.

02:53:12.690 --> 02:53:17.140
The screams echo through the facility’s
otherwise silent halls, as the mutilated corpse

02:53:17.140 --> 02:53:20.271
of Agent Resnick falls from a new scorch mark
on the ceiling.

02:53:20.271 --> 02:53:24.092
The Old Man can hear the sounds of suffering
ringing out through the air around him, and

02:53:24.092 --> 02:53:28.840
he can barely contain his excitement over
the prospect of a new plaything.

02:53:28.840 --> 02:53:32.700
The snapped femurs, the torn Achilles tendons,
it was all too good to miss.

02:53:32.700 --> 02:53:37.410
Having had its twisted fun with the security
officers and observers, SCP-106 wandered back

02:53:37.410 --> 02:53:40.740
to its containment cell, where a new screaming
victim awaited.

02:53:40.740 --> 02:53:45.700
The other security officers, containment specialists,
and scientists evacuated the area, leaving

02:53:45.700 --> 02:53:47.690
the Old Man alone with his prey.

02:53:47.690 --> 02:53:51.370
While the unfortunate Class D was left to
his fate, the rest of the staff commenced

02:53:51.370 --> 02:53:55.880
clean up procedures, which mainly involved
wiping the brown and black mucus from the

02:53:55.880 --> 02:53:56.880
walls.

02:53:56.880 --> 02:54:00.250
It would probably be at least another month
before anything like this happened again,

02:54:00.250 --> 02:54:04.181
and new personnel would be transferred over
to the facility to replace the fallen.

02:54:04.181 --> 02:54:08.960
All in all, just another night at The SCP
Foundation.

02:54:08.960 --> 02:54:12.670
“SCP-682 must be destroyed as soon as possible.”

02:54:12.670 --> 02:54:19.460
So begins the SCP Foundation file on the dreaded
SCP - 682, a highly-intelligent reptilian

02:54:19.460 --> 02:54:24.970
monster that has - despite the Foundation’s
best efforts - proved impossible to kill.

02:54:24.970 --> 02:54:29.711
It may not be the most dangerous SCP out there,
considering that some are capable of eliminating

02:54:29.711 --> 02:54:34.180
entire realities, but it’s one of the most
iconic, and you’ve probably heard tales

02:54:34.180 --> 02:54:39.080
of the monster that death forgot, and you
know exactly why everyone is so afraid of

02:54:39.080 --> 02:54:41.340
the so-called “Hard to Kill Reptile”.

02:54:41.340 --> 02:54:45.670
It’s been subjected to some of the most
deadly weapons and traps the Foundation could

02:54:45.670 --> 02:54:49.870
devise, and survived attacks from some of
its deadliest fellow SCPs.

02:54:49.870 --> 02:54:53.910
But before we tell you about the Foundation’s
many failed assassination attempts against

02:54:53.910 --> 02:54:58.720
the so-called “Hard to Kill Reptile”,
we need a little more groundwork on what this

02:54:58.720 --> 02:55:00.220
creature even is.

02:55:00.220 --> 02:55:05.130
The first thing to know about SCP - 682, is
that this thing wants you and everyone you

02:55:05.130 --> 02:55:06.421
know dead.

02:55:06.421 --> 02:55:13.030
Unlike some other creatures like SCP - 096
and SCP - 173, which are murderous but exhibit

02:55:13.030 --> 02:55:19.580
no real higher processing skills, SCP - 682
possesses cunning, advanced reasoning, and

02:55:19.580 --> 02:55:21.910
even human-level logical intelligence.

02:55:21.910 --> 02:55:27.930
SCP - 682 can engage you in conversation,
but just talking to the creature calmly and

02:55:27.930 --> 02:55:31.550
cordially will sometimes cause it to enter
its “rage state” where it becomes even

02:55:31.550 --> 02:55:33.400
more dangerous and volatile.

02:55:33.400 --> 02:55:37.891
The beast is perpetually kept in a huge tank
of powerful hydrochloric acid, melting its

02:55:37.891 --> 02:55:42.261
tissue to prevent it from reaching its full
potential and going on a rampage.

02:55:42.261 --> 02:55:46.960
The creature’s most terrifying asset, and
the reason it’s proven impossible to terminate

02:55:46.960 --> 02:55:52.330
thus far, is its incredible adaptability to
any and all external stimuli.

02:55:52.330 --> 02:55:58.851
682 is a reactive being, capable of not only
surviving and regenerating from all attacks,

02:55:58.851 --> 02:56:02.410
but often incorporating those attacks into
its own wide arsenal.

02:56:02.410 --> 02:56:06.851
In other words, if you’re hoping to kill
this thing, you better kill it on the first

02:56:06.851 --> 02:56:12.300
hit - cause if you don’t, you better believe
it’s gonna hit you back a hundred times

02:56:12.300 --> 02:56:13.940
harder.

02:56:13.940 --> 02:56:18.430
This brings us to the main event: Some of
the SCP Foundation’s most ambitious and

02:56:18.430 --> 02:56:24.190
frightening attempts to terminate SCP - 682,
or even understand how it could theoretically

02:56:24.190 --> 02:56:25.190
be terminated.

02:56:25.190 --> 02:56:29.772
There are quite literally too many unsuccessful
attempts for us to list them all here, so

02:56:29.772 --> 02:56:33.771
think of this as a highlight reel of the Foundation’s
most prominent failures.

02:56:33.771 --> 02:56:39.601
682 was first cross-tested with SCP - 017,
a humanoid shadow-entity shown to be able

02:56:39.601 --> 02:56:44.021
to consume matter with its shadows and leave
no traces behind.

02:56:44.021 --> 02:56:49.660
Tests on tissue samples from 682 showed that
SCP - 017 was able to consume said tissues

02:56:49.660 --> 02:56:51.430
with no adverse effects.

02:56:51.430 --> 02:56:57.510
However, when SCP - 017 was placed into the
containment chamber with the actual creature,

02:56:57.510 --> 02:57:02.530
682 let out a horrific roar that was so loud
it damaged nearby audio equipment.

02:57:02.530 --> 02:57:08.601
SCP - 017 fled to the corner of the room,
and 682, in its rage state, attempted to breach

02:57:08.601 --> 02:57:10.351
containment.

02:57:10.351 --> 02:57:15.101
Agents managed to suppress and remove the
creature, but no meaningful damage was logged.

02:57:15.101 --> 02:57:16.101
Attempt failed.

02:57:16.101 --> 02:57:21.680
SCP - 173 - the Killer statue - was later
brought in, hoping that its thus-far impeccable

02:57:21.680 --> 02:57:24.271
track recording for killing would hold strong.

02:57:24.271 --> 02:57:29.410
The second that 173 was introduced into the
testing area, 682 retreated to the far wall

02:57:29.410 --> 02:57:31.171
and began screeching intensely.

02:57:31.171 --> 02:57:33.890
It was intelligent enough to know what it
was dealing with here.

02:57:33.890 --> 02:57:38.351
While the researchers and guards expected
an instantaneous reaction, there was actually

02:57:38.351 --> 02:57:44.160
a stalemate for over six hours as 682 stared
at 173 continuously.

02:57:44.160 --> 02:57:49.070
Eventually, the tie was broken when Agents
shot out 682’s eyes with high-caliber sniper

02:57:49.070 --> 02:57:53.021
rifles, breaking the line of sight and causing
173 to attack.

02:57:53.021 --> 02:57:57.890
Though 682 sustained damage to several parts
of its body while its eyes regenerated, the

02:57:57.890 --> 02:57:59.101
creature was not killed.

02:57:59.101 --> 02:58:04.390
It then regenerated a number of eyes all over
its body, covered in a clear, armored carapace

02:58:04.390 --> 02:58:06.690
that made them resistant to bullets.

02:58:06.690 --> 02:58:11.480
The stalemate continued for an additional
twelve hours, as 682 maintained perpetual

02:58:11.480 --> 02:58:12.480
eye contact.

02:58:12.480 --> 02:58:17.230
173 was eventually removed from the containment
unit, and the mission was aborted.

02:58:17.230 --> 02:58:18.351
Attempt failed.

02:58:18.351 --> 02:58:23.800
In their desperation, the SCP Foundation resorted
to bringing in another dangerous and seemingly

02:58:23.800 --> 02:58:31.351
unkillable monster to take on 682: SCP - 096,
also known as The Shy Guy.

02:58:31.351 --> 02:58:36.940
As astute SCP fans will already know, this
being kills anything that sees its face, with

02:58:36.940 --> 02:58:42.091
no known exceptions - and when it enters its
attack mode, it’s thought to be quite literally

02:58:42.091 --> 02:58:43.400
unstoppable.

02:58:43.400 --> 02:58:46.620
Or, at least, it was.

02:58:46.620 --> 02:58:53.190
While SCP - 096 was able to destroy 85% of
682’s original body mass during their 27

02:58:53.190 --> 02:58:59.160
hour battle, it was left mentally broken - wounded,
and huddled in the corner.

02:58:59.160 --> 02:59:04.760
To this day, if ever confronted with SCP 682,
the Shy Guy reacts in pure terror, turning

02:59:04.760 --> 02:59:07.610
away and clawing at his own face.

02:59:07.610 --> 02:59:09.771
Attempt failed.

02:59:09.771 --> 02:59:14.950
During a deadly containment breach, SCP - 682
also went head to head organically with another

02:59:14.950 --> 02:59:21.351
iconic SCP hall-of-famer: SCP - 106, also
known as The Old Man.

02:59:21.351 --> 02:59:27.890
The Old Man and a shapeshifting, psionic anomaly
known as SCP - 953 broke into 682’s containment

02:59:27.890 --> 02:59:28.890
cell.

02:59:28.890 --> 02:59:32.791
The Old Man pulled both of his fellow anomalous
combatants into his pocket dimension to continue

02:59:32.791 --> 02:59:34.420
the battle on his terms.

02:59:34.420 --> 02:59:40.061
However, despite losing 67% of his body mass
during the ensuing pocket dimension showdown,

02:59:40.061 --> 02:59:46.120
682 still prevailed - with the Old Man eventually
fleeing back to his cell, and 953 being collected

02:59:46.120 --> 02:59:48.010
and taken away by agents.

02:59:48.010 --> 02:59:52.131
Once again, SCP - 682 continued to hold the
title.

02:59:52.131 --> 02:59:56.620
But it wasn’t just cross-testing experiments,
intentional or otherwise.

02:59:56.620 --> 03:00:01.450
The SCP Foundation’s quest to kill 682 lead
them to a number of more conventional murder

03:00:01.450 --> 03:00:03.920
methods, all with varying degrees of success.

03:00:03.920 --> 03:00:10.170
Due to SCP - 682’s highly adaptive abilities,
some methods were discounted from the outset.

03:00:10.170 --> 03:00:14.480
For example, launching a powerful thermonuclear
missile at the creature was soundly rejected

03:00:14.480 --> 03:00:18.811
by O5 Command - on the premise that, if the
creature wasn’t destroyed and evolved to

03:00:18.811 --> 03:00:23.700
the point where it could shrug off nukes,
humanity would be pretty much done for.

03:00:23.700 --> 03:00:27.811
Other ideas were abandoned just for being
too ridiculous - such as one researcher’s

03:00:27.811 --> 03:00:31.180
suggestion to fly the creature through the
air and drop it from a considerable height,

03:00:31.180 --> 03:00:32.990
hoping to kill it with the high-altitude impact.

03:00:32.990 --> 03:00:36.601
I’m not sure we even need to tell you why
that’s a terrible idea.

03:00:36.601 --> 03:00:42.230
But, during the experiments on SCP - 682,
the studies ranged from honest to incompetent

03:00:42.230 --> 03:00:45.030
to straight-up evil.

03:00:45.030 --> 03:00:49.160
One guest researcher fed two small, innocent
children to the creature, just to see what

03:00:49.160 --> 03:00:50.160
would happen.

03:00:50.160 --> 03:00:53.811
He was then himself fed to the creature for
his sadistic behavior, which was viewed as

03:00:53.811 --> 03:00:56.820
getting in the way of his professional conduct.

03:00:56.820 --> 03:01:00.030
After all, the Foundation is meant to be cold,
not cruel.

03:01:00.030 --> 03:01:03.670
It was SCP - 682 that had the monopoly on
cruelty.

03:01:03.670 --> 03:01:06.320
Memetic Kill agents were a resounding failure.

03:01:06.320 --> 03:01:11.030
They attempted to dismember 682 with a powerful
laser, only to have the creature develop reflective

03:01:11.030 --> 03:01:15.761
surfaces that displaced the beam and caused
catastrophic damage to the area around it.

03:01:15.761 --> 03:01:19.790
They attempted to kill the creature by sucking
all the air out of its containment facility

03:01:19.790 --> 03:01:25.040
and creating a vacuum, but it expelled a dangerous
gaseous compound that reacted violently and

03:01:25.040 --> 03:01:28.320
exploded when air was once again introduced
into the room.

03:01:28.320 --> 03:01:34.530
The Foundation used high-precision blades
to slice SCP - 682 into approximately 12,000

03:01:34.530 --> 03:01:37.000
pieces then separated these pieces.

03:01:37.000 --> 03:01:40.320
Unsurprisingly by this point, this attempt
also failed.

03:01:40.320 --> 03:01:44.820
The 12,000 pieces reformed a short while later
into the fully operational killing machine

03:01:44.820 --> 03:01:46.290
we all know and fear.

03:01:46.290 --> 03:01:50.771
In one particularly frightening display of
intelligence and adaptability, the Foundation

03:01:50.771 --> 03:01:55.960
attempted to kill 682 with extreme heat, but
it shielded itself by developing a secondary

03:01:55.960 --> 03:01:58.150
carapace composed of solid helium.

03:01:58.150 --> 03:02:01.811
When personnel entered the room following
the failed attempt on the creature’s life,

03:02:01.811 --> 03:02:06.720
it shattered its helium carapace into deadly
shards that fired around the room and shredded

03:02:06.720 --> 03:02:09.000
all Foundation personnel in attendance.

03:02:09.000 --> 03:02:13.690
It’d set a trap, and that trap had been
wildly successful.

03:02:13.690 --> 03:02:18.040
The creature’s ability to adapt to seemingly
any offensive is unparalleled, to the point

03:02:18.040 --> 03:02:23.090
where Foundation staff have no idea how to
classify this creature - whether it’s organic,

03:02:23.090 --> 03:02:27.910
inorganic, or even alive at all based on any
definitions we could understand.

03:02:27.910 --> 03:02:31.410
At every turn, the creature just raised more
questions.

03:02:31.410 --> 03:02:32.410
What is it?

03:02:32.410 --> 03:02:35.120
Is it possible to destroy it at all by any
means?

03:02:35.120 --> 03:02:37.581
Who was even trying to kill who here?

03:02:37.581 --> 03:02:42.851
Because it certainly seemed like SCP - 682
had a masterful K/D ratio by now.

03:02:42.851 --> 03:02:46.910
More extreme feats of cross-testing continued
in the Foundation’s growing desperation

03:02:46.910 --> 03:02:48.920
to eliminate this monster.

03:02:48.920 --> 03:02:54.480
SCP - 162, which is a hypnotic ball of sharp
objects, hooks, and high-tension fishing line,

03:02:54.480 --> 03:02:57.030
was introduced to 682’s containment cell.

03:02:57.030 --> 03:03:01.521
The hooks latched onto the creature and tore
huge portions off, including its entire lower

03:03:01.521 --> 03:03:03.561
jaw and one of its limbs.

03:03:03.561 --> 03:03:10.480
However, 682 was still able to breach containment,
kill eleven people, and badly wound 86 others.

03:03:10.480 --> 03:03:13.681
It regenerated its severe injuries in no time.

03:03:13.681 --> 03:03:17.680
The beast was even taken to the domain of
The Gate Guardian, one of the proposals for

03:03:17.680 --> 03:03:19.470
SCP - 001.

03:03:19.470 --> 03:03:24.050
The Guardian has a flaming sword hotter than
the sun, capable of destroying its targets

03:03:24.050 --> 03:03:25.811
on an atomic level.

03:03:25.811 --> 03:03:30.521
Naturally, SCP - 682 survived and regenerated.

03:03:30.521 --> 03:03:37.271
Perhaps the most fascinating cross-test of
all was between 682 and SCP - 053, who manifests

03:03:37.271 --> 03:03:42.190
as a kind, innocent little girl with the unfortunate
condition of causing homicidal tendencies

03:03:42.190 --> 03:03:46.470
in all who come into contact with her for
more than ten minutes.

03:03:46.470 --> 03:03:49.950
The people with these tendencies would then
attempt to harm the girl, but would immediately

03:03:49.950 --> 03:03:53.851
drop dead shortly after, leaving the girl
intact.

03:03:53.851 --> 03:03:58.351
The researchers present anticipated two possible
outcomes here: The optimistic outcome, in

03:03:58.351 --> 03:04:02.230
which 682 entered a rage state, attacked 053,
and died for good.

03:04:02.230 --> 03:04:07.811
And the realistic outcome, in which 682 attacked
053, possibly experienced some minor injury

03:04:07.811 --> 03:04:12.190
or nothing at all, and 053 had to be removed
from the containment cell.

03:04:12.190 --> 03:04:13.640
But that didn’t happen.

03:04:13.640 --> 03:04:18.101
What did occur was considerably more shocking
than any kind of violence.

03:04:18.101 --> 03:04:24.490
When 053 entered 682’s containment chamber,
the monster became uncharacteristically docile.

03:04:24.490 --> 03:04:29.351
Researchers and staff were baffled, and watched
with amazement as 053 approached the terrifying,

03:04:29.351 --> 03:04:34.021
immortal, mass-murdering monster...and began
to play with it.

03:04:34.021 --> 03:04:38.521
682 even allowed 053 to draw on its face with
crayons.

03:04:38.521 --> 03:04:42.420
Researchers thought they must’ve been dreaming,
seeing this surreal display play out.

03:04:42.420 --> 03:04:45.750
053 even appeared to have affection for this
unkillable misanthrope.

03:04:45.750 --> 03:04:50.300
It was a single act in defiance of everything
they thought they knew.

03:04:50.300 --> 03:04:55.470
When Foundation personnel entered the containment
cell to separate the two, 682 went ballistic

03:04:55.470 --> 03:04:57.271
and killed multiple guards.

03:04:57.271 --> 03:05:01.890
053 also wept, sad at being separated from
her new friend.

03:05:01.890 --> 03:05:07.671
To this day, despite further testing, the
Foundation has no idea how or why this happened.

03:05:07.671 --> 03:05:14.530
Like many details surrounding SCP - 682, it’s
shrouded in deeply frustrating mystery.

03:05:14.530 --> 03:05:20.840
And so the tale of SCP - 682 continues, in
spite of the Foundation’s best efforts.

03:05:20.840 --> 03:05:25.421
The monster continues to breach containment
and slaughter with some regularity, taking

03:05:25.421 --> 03:05:31.320
out its seemingly limitless hatred for not
only human beings, but anything that dares

03:05:31.320 --> 03:05:33.070
draw breath.

03:05:33.070 --> 03:05:37.660
Nobody knows where exactly the creature is
from, what its true nature is, or why its

03:05:37.660 --> 03:05:43.050
ability to adapt and regenerate far exceeds
any known organism on this planet.

03:05:43.050 --> 03:05:47.530
Perhaps one day, through enough research and
cross testing, we can someday answer these

03:05:47.530 --> 03:05:55.140
questions with scientific precision, but until
then, we only have one answer: Hatred never

03:05:55.140 --> 03:05:57.380
dies.

03:05:57.380 --> 03:06:02.550
Almost all cross-testing to kill or pacify
SCP – 682 had failed miserably.

03:06:02.550 --> 03:06:07.830
It faced the Gate Guardian, an SCP with a
flaming sword hotter than the sun – capable

03:06:07.830 --> 03:06:11.630
of tearing your atoms to shreds – and came
out fine.

03:06:11.630 --> 03:06:17.590
In its face-off with the horrifying SCP – 096,
also known as the Shy Guy, it broke the Shy

03:06:17.590 --> 03:06:21.300
Guy’s mind and reduced it to gibbering despair.

03:06:21.300 --> 03:06:27.660
Even SCPs with supposedly unlimited powers
simply refused to engage the beast in combat.

03:06:27.660 --> 03:06:34.290
So, when it was proposed that they test 682
with SCP – 999, a creature known among Foundation

03:06:34.290 --> 03:06:38.240
staff as “The Tickle Monster,” the idea
was considered laughable.

03:06:38.240 --> 03:06:44.720
682 had been burned, suffocated, cut up, incinerated,
and growled in the faces of Gods.

03:06:44.720 --> 03:06:48.820
How could this so-called Tickle Monster ever
hope to survive an encounter, let alone win

03:06:48.820 --> 03:06:50.101
a fight?

03:06:50.101 --> 03:06:53.700
Some even believed that this was the last
we’d see of SCP – 999.

03:06:53.700 --> 03:06:58.800
But what makes this story truly remarkable
is that that isn’t how this played out.

03:06:58.800 --> 03:07:05.351
As you’ll soon discover, 0SCP – 999 is
an amazing and unique SCP in and of itself,

03:07:05.351 --> 03:07:10.230
but its secret origins and its interactions
with some other prominent figures in the SCP

03:07:10.230 --> 03:07:15.180
universe are what make this humble, slimy
creature beyond extraordinary.

03:07:15.180 --> 03:07:19.860
Prepare yourself for the heartwarming – yes,
you heard that right - the heartwarming story

03:07:19.860 --> 03:07:23.230
of SCP – 999.

03:07:23.230 --> 03:07:28.900
Several highly-trained agents on 682 detail
placed 999 into the immortal lizard’s cell.

03:07:28.900 --> 03:07:33.521
Compared to the giant, reptilian sitting across
from it, 999 wasn’t much to look at – it’s

03:07:33.521 --> 03:07:37.030
a large, orange, amorphous blob of anomalous
slime.

03:07:37.030 --> 03:07:42.530
Weighing in at around 120 pounds, SCP - 999
was nothing compared to the monstrosity it

03:07:42.530 --> 03:07:43.771
was supposed to face.

03:07:43.771 --> 03:07:48.771
While its weight has, in the past, caused
minor injuries to some of its human handlers,

03:07:48.771 --> 03:07:53.711
it has never caused serious or long-lasting
damage of any kind to a living thing.

03:07:53.711 --> 03:07:58.521
Even its diet consists only of candy and sweets,
with a particular preference for M&amp;Ms and

03:07:58.521 --> 03:08:00.101
Necco wafers.

03:08:00.101 --> 03:08:04.680
It consumes these treats through the cell
membrane of its slimy body, much like an amoeba.

03:08:04.680 --> 03:08:08.670
This extremely stretchy membrane means the
creature is highly malleable, including the

03:08:08.670 --> 03:08:12.910
ability to stretch and flatten itself out
to a mere two centimeters thick.

03:08:12.910 --> 03:08:18.601
At rest, the creature takes a dome-like shape
around two meters wide and one meter in height.

03:08:18.601 --> 03:08:23.570
The closest things the creature has to limbs
are prehensile pseudopods, those are the arm-like

03:08:23.570 --> 03:08:28.710
projections normally seen on single celled
organisms, of which it has at least three.

03:08:28.710 --> 03:08:32.330
The more you hear about this utterly harmless
creature, the more that matching it up with

03:08:32.330 --> 03:08:37.961
the pure embodiment of absolute hatred known
as SCP – 682 feels downright cruel.

03:08:37.961 --> 03:08:43.570
In absolute contrast to the misanthropic attitudes
of the reptile, 999 loves humans.

03:08:43.570 --> 03:08:45.660
It has a playful, dog-like attitude.

03:08:45.660 --> 03:08:50.690
Much like an over-excited puppy, when approached,
999 will react with extreme joy and slither

03:08:50.690 --> 03:08:53.851
towards the nearest person in order to interact.

03:08:53.851 --> 03:08:58.601
It will leap onto them, using two of its three
prehensile pseudopods to hug the person, while

03:08:58.601 --> 03:09:03.900
the third nuzzles the person’s face – emitting
high-pitched cooing and gurgling noises throughout.

03:09:03.900 --> 03:09:08.210
The creature is apparently pleasant in every
conceivable fashion, as even its odor has

03:09:08.210 --> 03:09:12.420
been reported to smell just like the favorite
scent of whoever is smelling it.

03:09:12.420 --> 03:09:16.851
Examples have included chocolate, fresh laundry,
bacon, roses, and Play-Doh.

03:09:16.851 --> 03:09:21.391
It's almost impossible to oversell just how
beloved and benevolent this strange creature

03:09:21.391 --> 03:09:22.391
is.

03:09:22.391 --> 03:09:26.170
It’s one of the rare sapient SCPs to earn
the “Safe” class, and it’s allowed to

03:09:26.170 --> 03:09:30.950
roam freely around its facility at all times,
apart from a one hour bedtime period between

03:09:30.950 --> 03:09:32.450
8 and 9 PM.

03:09:32.450 --> 03:09:37.350
In the rare instances that 999 has caused
harm to a worker at the facility, it immediately

03:09:37.350 --> 03:09:42.620
began to back away and contract its body while
whimpering in a kind of dog-like apology.

03:09:42.620 --> 03:09:46.420
The closest the Foundation had ever come to
having a real incident with the creature was

03:09:46.420 --> 03:09:50.510
the time someone accidentally fed it a can
of caffeinated cola, causing it to become

03:09:50.510 --> 03:09:53.610
hyper for an hour before becoming visibly
queasy.

03:09:53.610 --> 03:09:57.320
You’ll be relieved to know that it’s since
made a full recovery.

03:09:57.320 --> 03:10:02.021
But what would happen when this whimsical
creature is forced to go toe-to-toe with the

03:10:02.021 --> 03:10:04.210
Foundation’s most ill-tempered monster?

03:10:04.210 --> 03:10:08.641
The employees observing the test watched in
suspense as 999 began to enthusiastically

03:10:08.641 --> 03:10:10.390
slither towards 682.

03:10:10.390 --> 03:10:14.601
It’s no surprise that after being tortured
and almost killed hundreds of times during

03:10:14.601 --> 03:10:19.110
testing, 682 had grown jaded to the cross-tests
it was regularly subjected to.

03:10:19.110 --> 03:10:24.221
When it saw this strange, orange blob squelching
across the ground towards it, it sighed and

03:10:24.221 --> 03:10:25.450
groaned, expecting the worst.

03:10:25.450 --> 03:10:26.980
“What is that?”

03:10:26.980 --> 03:10:29.880
the creature asked of its gelatinous guest.

03:10:29.880 --> 03:10:36.180
SCP – 999 began jumping up and down in front
of 682 like an excited puppy, creating a high-pitched

03:10:36.180 --> 03:10:37.920
squealing noise.

03:10:37.920 --> 03:10:42.100
Just as it regarded all living things, 682
thought the creature bouncing around before

03:10:42.100 --> 03:10:45.541
it was disgusting and hardly worth the effort
to destroy.

03:10:45.541 --> 03:10:47.561
Was the Foundation even trying anymore?

03:10:47.561 --> 03:10:52.771
With a single vicious stomp, 682 flattened
the friendly creature beneath one of its feet.

03:10:52.771 --> 03:10:57.890
Observers were prepared to charge in and liberate
999 from under 682’s claws, but then something

03:10:57.890 --> 03:10:59.920
truly unexpected happened.

03:10:59.920 --> 03:11:04.760
The expression on 682’s acid-eaten face
began to slowly change.

03:11:04.760 --> 03:11:07.431
It was beginning... to smile.

03:11:07.431 --> 03:11:10.371
Observers recorded a noise that they thought
could have been a chuckle, as the creature

03:11:10.371 --> 03:11:13.170
growled and said, “Hmmm?

03:11:13.170 --> 03:11:18.230
What is this…I feel… good…”

03:11:18.230 --> 03:11:23.620
While the observers looked on, stunned at
what was happening, 999 began to slither and

03:11:23.620 --> 03:11:25.140
crawl up from between 682’s toes.

03:11:25.140 --> 03:11:31.110
It reformed on its scaly leg and slithered
up along its side until it reached the neck.

03:11:31.110 --> 03:11:34.790
There, it began to nuzzle like it had never
nuzzled before.

03:11:34.790 --> 03:11:37.070
The results spoke for themselves.

03:11:37.070 --> 03:11:41.890
682 was grinning and chuckling, repeating
a phrase that the Foundation never would have

03:11:41.890 --> 03:11:49.430
even imagined coming from 682: “Feel…
so… happy.

03:11:49.430 --> 03:11:52.801
Happy…happy… happy…”

03:11:52.801 --> 03:11:57.370
Just when you thought SCP – 999 couldn’t
possibly be more adorable, you learn about

03:11:57.370 --> 03:12:00.341
its greatest power: Bringing joy.

03:12:00.341 --> 03:12:04.820
Anyone and anything that comes into contact
with the creature, even in passing, will experience

03:12:04.820 --> 03:12:06.641
a kind of mild euphoria.

03:12:06.641 --> 03:12:11.120
As one’s contact with the creature is prolonged,
this overwhelming sense of joy increases,

03:12:11.120 --> 03:12:14.080
and continues long after you’re separated
from it.

03:12:14.080 --> 03:12:19.040
Prolonged contact has completely cured depression,
anxiety, and PTSD, along with a number of

03:12:19.040 --> 03:12:23.561
other conditions, including rage and antisocial
personality disorders.

03:12:23.561 --> 03:12:28.230
Serial killers practically become saints after
coming into prolonged contact with 999, and

03:12:28.230 --> 03:12:31.930
in that moment, 682 was no exception.

03:12:31.930 --> 03:12:34.440
And there truly does appear to be no exceptions.

03:12:34.440 --> 03:12:39.730
While “causing happiness and joy” isn’t
a dangerous weapon, when it comes to SCP – 999,

03:12:39.730 --> 03:12:41.860
it is an extremely powerful one.

03:12:41.860 --> 03:12:46.750
And what’s more, SCP – 999 also appears
to have an innate sense for those who need

03:12:46.750 --> 03:12:51.480
its help most – with a particular affection
for the hurt and the unhappy.

03:12:51.480 --> 03:12:56.051
The creature appears to be a true altruist
on a fundamental level, even risking its own

03:12:56.051 --> 03:12:59.620
safety to help humans during dangerous containment
breaches.

03:12:59.620 --> 03:13:04.290
In one dramatic instance, 999 leaped into
the air to block a bullet from making contact

03:13:04.290 --> 03:13:06.230
with a member of staff.

03:13:06.230 --> 03:13:11.400
As a result, the creature is pretty much universally
loved by all members of Foundation staff.

03:13:11.400 --> 03:13:15.650
It’s the one SCP who never made trouble
for anyone.

03:13:15.650 --> 03:13:20.440
Back in SCP – 682’s containment cell,
the beast was still smiling and laughing as

03:13:20.440 --> 03:13:22.410
999 rubbed against its neck.

03:13:22.410 --> 03:13:27.280
It was an event so strange, so unprecedented
that the observers in attendance felt like

03:13:27.280 --> 03:13:28.690
they were hallucinating.

03:13:28.690 --> 03:13:33.891
For a few minutes, the monster kept dreamily
repeating the word “happy” but then, suddenly,

03:13:33.891 --> 03:13:37.460
the creature began to enter a fit of uncontrollable,
booming laughter.

03:13:37.460 --> 03:13:41.950
It rolled onto its back, slamming its huge
tail against the door.

03:13:41.950 --> 03:13:47.760
It’d just fallen victim to one of 999’s
favorite pastimes: Tickle Fights, hence how

03:13:47.760 --> 03:13:51.180
it earned its Tickle Monster nickname among
staff.

03:13:51.180 --> 03:13:56.120
The tickle fight continued until 682 appeared
to tire and fall asleep, with a smile still

03:13:56.120 --> 03:13:57.851
on its face.

03:13:57.851 --> 03:14:02.550
After fifteen minutes of inactivity, two D-Class
personnel were commanded to enter and retrieve

03:14:02.550 --> 03:14:05.021
SCP – 999 from the containment cell.

03:14:05.021 --> 03:14:10.840
They did so successfully, but as soon as 999
was removed, 682 roused from its slumber and

03:14:10.840 --> 03:14:15.181
released a powerful psychic attack from its
entire body while laughing maniacally.

03:14:15.181 --> 03:14:20.030
It rendered all personnel within a certain
distance incapacitated as they collapsed in

03:14:20.030 --> 03:14:24.820
fits of laughter, allowing 682 to escape and
go on a violent rampage.

03:14:24.820 --> 03:14:30.010
However, in spite of this, 999 showed no fear,
and helped save some of the bystanders as

03:14:30.010 --> 03:14:33.790
security officers subdued and recaptured 682.

03:14:33.790 --> 03:14:40.170
And even after all this, 999 showed no hard
feelings towards 682, and indicated a desire

03:14:40.170 --> 03:14:41.250
to play again.

03:14:41.250 --> 03:14:45.380
It’s a creature whose capacity for love
is so limitless that it’s practically immune

03:14:45.380 --> 03:14:46.680
to fear.

03:14:46.680 --> 03:14:52.110
Which is all well and good, because the true
enemy that 999 is destined to face is infinitely

03:14:52.110 --> 03:14:56.990
more powerful and terrifying than 682 could
ever hope to be.

03:14:56.990 --> 03:15:00.971
What is this monster, and why should 999 have
to face it someday?

03:15:00.971 --> 03:15:06.590
The answers to these questions all lie in
the true origins of SCP – 999, available

03:15:06.590 --> 03:15:09.030
only to those with level 5 clearance and beyond.

03:15:09.030 --> 03:15:13.830
It’s a perfect example of how something
good can come from the darkest places…

03:15:13.830 --> 03:15:18.681
There would be no SCP – 999 without SCP
– 231 – 7.

03:15:18.681 --> 03:15:24.340
SCP – 231 was a collection of seven girls,
all impregnated by horrific nightmares in

03:15:24.340 --> 03:15:29.210
a ritual performed by a cult known as the
Children of the Scarlet King.

03:15:29.210 --> 03:15:33.870
Each of these girls, over the years that followed,
gave birth to some of the most horrific monsters

03:15:33.870 --> 03:15:40.010
imaginable – one of which, according to
some, was SCP – 682.

03:15:40.010 --> 03:15:44.910
These beings were manifested by the Scarlet
King, a powerful interdimensional nightmare

03:15:44.910 --> 03:15:49.010
God, believed to be behind a great deal of
the darkness and horror present within our

03:15:49.010 --> 03:15:51.320
and many other dimensions.

03:15:51.320 --> 03:15:55.030
Foundation higher-ups have declared the Scarlet
King to be the greatest existing threat to

03:15:55.030 --> 03:16:02.771
the Multiverse at large, and SCP – 231 was
his latest direct interaction with our universe.

03:16:02.771 --> 03:16:09.090
The only surviving member of SCP – 231,
SCP – 231 – 7, gave birth in secret.

03:16:09.090 --> 03:16:15.351
But she didn’t give birth to a monster – she
gave birth to SCP – 999, a being of pure

03:16:15.351 --> 03:16:16.351
goodness.

03:16:16.351 --> 03:16:22.960
That’s right: The nicest, kindest, cuddliest
SCP of all is the direct descendent of a being

03:16:22.960 --> 03:16:26.190
that’s essentially the Dark God of all evil.

03:16:26.190 --> 03:16:29.120
Feel free to take a moment to absorb that.

03:16:29.120 --> 03:16:33.480
The creature even healed the girl who birthed
it, and allowed her to return to normal life

03:16:33.480 --> 03:16:35.390
with her family once more.

03:16:35.390 --> 03:16:41.021
From its first moments, SCP - 999 was making
positive changes to the world around it.

03:16:41.021 --> 03:16:45.130
And according to ancient texts from a Scarlet
King-aligned culture known as the Daevas,

03:16:45.130 --> 03:16:51.200
SCP – 999 is still very much in its infancy,
yet it already has the power to pacify its

03:16:51.200 --> 03:16:54.400
monstrous siblings like the aforementioned
682.

03:16:54.400 --> 03:16:59.130
It’s believed, according to some prophecies
and Foundation theories, that the power of

03:16:59.130 --> 03:17:03.260
SCP – 999 will grow exponentially as it
matures.

03:17:03.260 --> 03:17:05.040
Why does this matter?

03:17:05.040 --> 03:17:10.051
Well, it’s believed by some that one day
999 will grow powerful enough to overthrow

03:17:10.051 --> 03:17:16.510
not only its own monstrous siblings, but the
thought-to-be-unstoppable Scarlet King himself.

03:17:16.510 --> 03:17:20.940
Not through violence or hate, but through
the pure force of happiness and love burning

03:17:20.940 --> 03:17:23.751
out the darkness and purifying the corrupted.

03:17:23.751 --> 03:17:29.940
While the humble SCP – 999 rarely outshines
its frightening competitors, to those truly

03:17:29.940 --> 03:17:36.622
in the know, 999 is one of the most powerful
and valuable SCPs in existence, and may be

03:17:36.622 --> 03:17:42.391
the greatest asset in the Foundation’s arsenal
for the war against dangerous anomalous activity.

03:17:42.391 --> 03:17:46.550
After all, what could strike more fear into
their hearts than the knowledge that it might

03:17:46.550 --> 03:17:52.000
be love rather than firepower that finally
dethrones the Scarlet King?

03:17:52.000 --> 03:17:56.431
And for the knowledge that it may one day
save everything we know from a fate so much

03:17:56.431 --> 03:18:01.000
worse than death with nothing but affection
for everyone and everything, it’s worth

03:18:01.000 --> 03:18:06.431
offering thanks to the little orange blob,
or at least an extra pack of M&amp;Ms before bedtime.

